{
  "version": 1,
  "guides": {
    "ffguide": [
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "To read this codex, use your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset; and click the Book icon.",
        "normalizedSource": "To read this codex, use your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset; and click the Book icon.",
        "translation": "このコーデックスを読むには、^orange;個人用トライコーダー^reset;を使って、本のアイコンをクリックしてください。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "description",
        "source": "How to Play",
        "normalizedSource": "How to Play",
        "translation": "遊び方"
      },
      {
        "field": "longContentPages",
        "source": "This guide will brief you on what you need to know to play with Frackin' Universe effectively. You need to keep in mind that a lot of the default play of Starbound has been altered by many aspects of the mod. \n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;The Tricorder - Your Best Friend:\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nThis device is the ^cyan;singlemost useful item in your inventory^reset; at any time. It provides access to the ^orange;Research System^reset;, along with numerous other functions accessed via the icons on its screen. It also has the following additional functions:\n\n^green;Right Mouse Button^reset; - Accesses the Quest tracker. This will provide you access to the FU tutorials and a wealth of useful rewards. It's well worth your time.\n\n^green;Shift + Click^reset; - Accesses the Configuration menu. Through this you can customize your Matter Manipulator output, and can even swap your own chosen tools into slots normally occupied by the paintbrush, wire tool, etc. Very handy. Using this, you can make the Tricorder a permanent hotkey item!\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Research? What do you mean, Research?^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nFrackinUniverse now introduces a progression overhaul we've called the ^orange;Research System^reset;. Accessed through your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset;, ^orange;SAIL Computer^reset; or ^orange;Quickbar^reset; , it is the sole means by which you learn new blueprints for crafting. To unlock new blueprints you'll need resources as well as the important currency known as ^green;Research^reset;.\n\nThrough this system, you'll be able to custom-tailor the new unlocks you want and in the order you choose to pursue them.\n\n\nYou gain ^green;Research^reset; at a rate of 1 every second, passively, as long as you are playing. This rate increases by +1 per planet tier. Thus, a Threat 6 planet will provide 7 total passive gain.\n\nYou can also gain ^green;Research^reset; through other means, including:\n^cyan;Laptops and Data Centers^reset;\n^cyan;Fossil Collection^reset;\n^cyan;Microscopes^reset;\n^cyan;Having high Madness^reset;\n^cyan;Certain armor and gear^reset;\n^green;Protheon / 10^reset; (to a maximum of +10)\n\nIn short, play and experiment and you'll get all the research you need. ^red;NOTE: Research gain slows down while you are not exploring. AFK collection to easy-mode progression will not work.^reset;.\n\nIf you have unlocked things that ^red;should^reset; appear at a station but do not seem to: Be sure you have ^orange;upgraded^reset; the station. That still needs to be done to create higher-tier items.\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;What the heck is Protheon^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nA rare currency resource, it will allow you to procure tons of Research by converting it at certain shops or processes. It can affect you in other ways when amassed, however, allowing you to work Madness off at a much faster rate (especially in an Insta-Freud) as well as increase your Research gain rates.\n\nObtaining this Protheon resource will require artifacts and luck.\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Racial Abilities^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nEach of the various species in the FU universe has different gameplay mechanics. Some are more resistant to fire, while others might have special powers or are really good with swords. This provides players with many new gameplay options.\n\n^yellow;I don't want to play with racial abilities^reset;!\n\nYou can enable and disable racial abilities from within your ^orange;ship SAIL computer^reset;. Simply access it, press the ^green;[ MISC ] ^reset;button and choose to disable the option.\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Special Techs^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\n^orange;Tech Usage Costs^reset;\nCertain techs in FU consume Food instead of Energy, if applicable, to a certain threshold. Past that threshold, they will drain Energy, and in some cases health!\n\n^orange;Directional/Cursor Aim Techs^reset;:\nThese techs are used with ^green;Head Tech Key^reset;, either tapped or held.\n^orange;Directional Aim Techs^reset; are aimed by holding ^green;movement keys^reset; and can fire in 8 different directions! To aim straight up or down hold the ^green;Walk^reset; key.\nIn FU, these techs use Directional Aim: Hunter/Razor/Miner Claw.\n^orange;Cursor Aim Techs^reset; need no fancy keys, and simply fire toward your cursor!\nIn FU, these techs use Cursor Aim: Psychic/Shard Blast, Acid Spit. Additionally, Shard Blast allows a fully randomized spread by holding ^green;Walk^reset;, while Acid Spit will fire a tile destroying glob instead of a caustic missile.\n\n^orange;Tech Scaling^reset;:\nCertain techs scale with your stats! Some are listed here for convenience.\n^orange;Shadowborne^reset;: Scales with Max Energy.\n^orange;Acid Spit^reset;: Scale with Bonus Health. Caustic missile deals DoT damage, tile destroyer deals damage and lasts longer.\n^orange;Miner Claws^reset;: Scales with current Food level.\n^orange;Psychic Blast^reset;: Scales with Max Energy and Defense.\n^orange;Razor^reset;/^orange;Hunter Claws^reset;: Hunting damage that scales with Max Health, Power and current Food level.\n^orange;Elduu'khar Burst^reset;, ^orange;Shard Blast^reset;, ^orange;Dragonfire^reset;: Scale with Max Energy, Defense and current Food level.\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Combat^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nSee FU Guide: Battle\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Mechs^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nMechs are not the same as you're used to in Starbound. They now ^red;require fuel^reset;, and can be refueled with many types. In addition, they have separate Health from their Fuel/Energy bar. The end result is a much more useful vehicle that can extend mining trips and greatly improve survivability in harsh environments.\n\nMechs now ^green;calculate their Mass^reset;. ^cyan;Heavier^reset; mechs are able to ^green;stomp and do massive damage^reset; to the ground as well as having better armor. ^cyan;Light^reset; mechs are ^green;much faster^reset; and have vastly ^green;improved fuel efficiency^reset;.\n\nYour mech can ^green;Sprint^reset; by double-tapping ^cyan;A^reset; or ^cyan;D^reset;.\n\nYour mech can switch to ^green;Flight Mode^reset; by double-tapping ^cyan;W^reset;.\n\nThere are dozens of new types of mech part, including Mech Modules. These act like Augments for your Mech and can allow a great amount of customization. There's a mech part for your playstyle.\n\nRefuel or Re-equip your mech through your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset;.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Status Effects^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nFrackinUniverse adds a ^green;great number^reset; of new Status Effects, beneficial and harmful, that can affect characters and monsters alike. Most can be resisted or ignored with the proper equipment.\n\nPart of the experience is learning how to survive in new environments through experimentation and ingenuity, and strategizing your ^orange;Research^reset; around it.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Madness^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nAnother form of currency in FrackinUniverse. It can be gained from many actions (most commonly the bizarre or terrifying) but will also fade away with time. The more ^#e43774;Madness^reset; you possess, the greater the negative effects you experience.\n\nCarrying around terrifying things in your bag can also result in gaining ^#e43774;Madness^reset; over time. Pay attention if SAIL warns you of this.\n\nThere are more than 50 possible effects of ^#e43774;Madness^reset;.\n\n^yellow;How do I lose madness?^reset;\n\nSpending your ^#e43774;Madness^reset; on ^green;Research^reset; in ^orange;Metaphysics^reset;\nShip Counsellor Crewmates\n^orange;Instafreud^reset; machines, when sat in, will rapidly consume madness.\n^green;Protheon / 10^reset; (to a maximum of -10)\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Genes^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nThis currency replaced the ^red;33 separate Gene items^reset; used from 2014-2020. Now, a singular form of ^green;Gene^reset; is used, making tracking your totals much easier and giving you more than 30 less resources to store.\n\n^green;Genes^reset; are used for ^orange;Agriculture^reset; and ^orange;Genetics^reset;.\n\nYou can trade in your current genes for the new currency by simply placing them into a Xeno Lab or Sprouting Table.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;BYOS (Build your own Ship)^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nIn FrackinUniverse, you can create your own ship from the ground up. This system means you no longer need to purchase Ship Upgrades, as any expansion is done by yourself. You'll also need to craft your own engines and will be able to craft special equipment to benefit your ship.\nNote that if you select BYOS mode at character creation, this choice is permanent.\n\nAt Character Creation, you can select ^cyan;Frackin Ship^reset; or ^cyan;Vanilla Ship^reset;. The Frackin Ship is the BYOS option. Once you make this choice, you're given options for starting ship configurations. Once they make this choice, they begin play like usual.\n\nCrew use special rules on these ships:\n\nYou can use ^orange;Crew Deeds^reset;, which follow the same rules as ^orange;Colony Deeds^reset; (Walls, Door, Lights, Bed) ^red;\n\n-or-\n\n^reset; you can opt to use ^orange;Crew Beds^reset; if quick-and-dirty with little planning is more your style.\n\nYou can ^red;not^reset; use both a ^orange;Crew Deed^reset; and ^orange;Crew Bed^reset; together in the same room.\n\nThere is a hard-cap of 12 crew. Mods that increase crew limits likely will not operate properly with BYOS.\n\nBYOS ships have additional options in construction, namely better engines and thrusters that can prove useful in exploration.\n\n\n\n^red;'Help, I have BYOS lag!' ^reset; or  ^yellow;I don't want atmosphere effects on my ship^reset;!\n\nBYOS has an atmosphere mode you can enable and disable from within your ^orange;ship SAIL computer^reset;. Simply access it, press the ^green;[ MISC ] ^reset;button and choose to disable the option.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Swimming^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nSwimming operates differently than you're used to:\n\nSwim : ^yellow;W A S D^reset;\n\nJump Out : ^green;hold ^yellow;W^green; , press ^yellow;Spacebar^reset;.\n\nIt will take you a bit to get used to it, but the end result is a much easier control experience.\n\nNote that not all liquids provide buoyancy like water or other similar fluids. In these liquids, or within gases, physics can behave quite different than expected.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;The Frackin Wiki\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nIf you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here:\n^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset;\n\n^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.",
        "normalizedSource": "This guide will brief you on what you need to know to play with Frackin' Universe effectively. You need to keep in mind that a lot of the default play of Starbound has been altered by many aspects of the mod. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;The Tricorder - Your Best Friend: ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; This device is the ^cyan;singlemost useful item in your inventory^reset; at any time. It provides access to the ^orange;Research System^reset;, along with numerous other functions accessed via the icons on its screen. It also has the following additional functions: ^green;Right Mouse Button^reset; - Accesses the Quest tracker. This will provide you access to the FU tutorials and a wealth of useful rewards. It's well worth your time. ^green;Shift + Click^reset; - Accesses the Configuration menu. Through this you can customize your Matter Manipulator output, and can even swap your own chosen tools into slots normally occupied by the paintbrush, wire tool, etc. Very handy. Using this, you can make the Tricorder a permanent hotkey item! ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^cyan;Research? What do you mean, Research?^reset; ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; FrackinUniverse now introduces a progression overhaul we've called the ^orange;Research System^reset;. Accessed through your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset;, ^orange;SAIL Computer^reset; or ^orange;Quickbar^reset; , it is the sole means by which you learn new blueprints for crafting. To unlock new blueprints you'll need resources as well as the important currency known as ^green;Research^reset;. Through this system, you'll be able to custom-tailor the new unlocks you want and in the order you choose to pursue them. You gain ^green;Research^reset; at a rate of 1 every second, passively, as long as you are playing. This rate increases by +1 per planet tier. Thus, a Threat 6 planet will provide 7 total passive gain. You can also gain ^green;Research^reset; through other means, including: ^cyan;Laptops and Data Centers^reset; ^cyan;Fossil Collection^reset; ^cyan;Microscopes^reset; ^cyan;Having high Madness^reset; ^cyan;Certain armor and gear^reset; ^green;Protheon / 10^reset; (to a maximum of +10) In short, play and experiment and you'll get all the research you need. ^red;NOTE: Research gain slows down while you are not exploring. AFK collection to easy-mode progression will not work.^reset;. If you have unlocked things that ^red;should^reset; appear at a station but do not seem to: Be sure you have ^orange;upgraded^reset; the station. That still needs to be done to create higher-tier items. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^cyan;What the heck is Protheon^reset; ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; A rare currency resource, it will allow you to procure tons of Research by converting it at certain shops or processes. It can affect you in other ways when amassed, however, allowing you to work Madness off at a much faster rate (especially in an Insta-Freud) as well as increase your Research gain rates. Obtaining this Protheon resource will require artifacts and luck. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^cyan;Racial Abilities^reset; ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; Each of the various species in the FU universe has different gameplay mechanics. Some are more resistant to fire, while others might have special powers or are really good with swords. This provides players with many new gameplay options. ^yellow;I don't want to play with racial abilities^reset;! You can enable and disable racial abilities from within your ^orange;ship SAIL computer^reset;. Simply access it, press the ^green;[ MISC ] ^reset;button and choose to disable the option. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^cyan;Special Techs^reset; ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Tech Usage Costs^reset; Certain techs in FU consume Food instead of Energy, if applicable, to a certain threshold. Past that threshold, they will drain Energy, and in some cases health! ^orange;Directional/Cursor Aim Techs^reset;: These techs are used with ^green;Head Tech Key^reset;, either tapped or held. ^orange;Directional Aim Techs^reset; are aimed by holding ^green;movement keys^reset; and can fire in 8 different directions! To aim straight up or down hold the ^green;Walk^reset; key. In FU, these techs use Directional Aim: Hunter/Razor/Miner Claw. ^orange;Cursor Aim Techs^reset; need no fancy keys, and simply fire toward your cursor! In FU, these techs use Cursor Aim: Psychic/Shard Blast, Acid Spit. Additionally, Shard Blast allows a fully randomized spread by holding ^green;Walk^reset;, while Acid Spit will fire a tile destroying glob instead of a caustic missile. ^orange;Tech Scaling^reset;: Certain techs scale with your stats! Some are listed here for convenience. ^orange;Shadowborne^reset;: Scales with Max Energy. ^orange;Acid Spit^reset;: Scale with Bonus Health. Caustic missile deals DoT damage, tile destroyer deals damage and lasts longer. ^orange;Miner Claws^reset;: Scales with current Food level. ^orange;Psychic Blast^reset;: Scales with Max Energy and Defense. ^orange;Razor^reset;/^orange;Hunter Claws^reset;: Hunting damage that scales with Max Health, Power and current Food level. ^orange;Elduu'khar Burst^reset;, ^orange;Shard Blast^reset;, ^orange;Dragonfire^reset;: Scale with Max Energy, Defense and current Food level. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^cyan;Combat^reset; ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; See FU Guide: Battle ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^cyan;Mechs^reset; ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; Mechs are not the same as you're used to in Starbound. They now ^red;require fuel^reset;, and can be refueled with many types. In addition, they have separate Health from their Fuel/Energy bar. The end result is a much more useful vehicle that can extend mining trips and greatly improve survivability in harsh environments. Mechs now ^green;calculate their Mass^reset;. ^cyan;Heavier^reset; mechs are able to ^green;stomp and do massive damage^reset; to the ground as well as having better armor. ^cyan;Light^reset; mechs are ^green;much faster^reset; and have vastly ^green;improved fuel efficiency^reset;. Your mech can ^green;Sprint^reset; by double-tapping ^cyan;A^reset; or ^cyan;D^reset;. Your mech can switch to ^green;Flight Mode^reset; by double-tapping ^cyan;W^reset;. There are dozens of new types of mech part, including Mech Modules. These act like Augments for your Mech and can allow a great amount of customization. There's a mech part for your playstyle. Refuel or Re-equip your mech through your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset;. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^cyan;Status Effects^reset; ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; FrackinUniverse adds a ^green;great number^reset; of new Status Effects, beneficial and harmful, that can affect characters and monsters alike. Most can be resisted or ignored with the proper equipment. Part of the experience is learning how to survive in new environments through experimentation and ingenuity, and strategizing your ^orange;Research^reset; around it. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^cyan;Madness^reset; ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; Another form of currency in FrackinUniverse. It can be gained from many actions (most commonly the bizarre or terrifying) but will also fade away with time. The more ^#e43774;Madness^reset; you possess, the greater the negative effects you experience. Carrying around terrifying things in your bag can also result in gaining ^#e43774;Madness^reset; over time. Pay attention if SAIL warns you of this. There are more than 50 possible effects of ^#e43774;Madness^reset;. ^yellow;How do I lose madness?^reset; Spending your ^#e43774;Madness^reset; on ^green;Research^reset; in ^orange;Metaphysics^reset; Ship Counsellor Crewmates ^orange;Instafreud^reset; machines, when sat in, will rapidly consume madness. ^green;Protheon / 10^reset; (to a maximum of -10) ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^cyan;Genes^reset; ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; This currency replaced the ^red;33 separate Gene items^reset; used from 2014-2020. Now, a singular form of ^green;Gene^reset; is used, making tracking your totals much easier and giving you more than 30 less resources to store. ^green;Genes^reset; are used for ^orange;Agriculture^reset; and ^orange;Genetics^reset;. You can trade in your current genes for the new currency by simply placing them into a Xeno Lab or Sprouting Table. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^cyan;BYOS (Build your own Ship)^reset; ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; In FrackinUniverse, you can create your own ship from the ground up. This system means you no longer need to purchase Ship Upgrades, as any expansion is done by yourself. You'll also need to craft your own engines and will be able to craft special equipment to benefit your ship. Note that if you select BYOS mode at character creation, this choice is permanent. At Character Creation, you can select ^cyan;Frackin Ship^reset; or ^cyan;Vanilla Ship^reset;. The Frackin Ship is the BYOS option. Once you make this choice, you're given options for starting ship configurations. Once they make this choice, they begin play like usual. Crew use special rules on these ships: You can use ^orange;Crew Deeds^reset;, which follow the same rules as ^orange;Colony Deeds^reset; (Walls, Door, Lights, Bed) ^red; -or- ^reset; you can opt to use ^orange;Crew Beds^reset; if quick-and-dirty with little planning is more your style. You can ^red;not^reset; use both a ^orange;Crew Deed^reset; and ^orange;Crew Bed^reset; together in the same room. There is a hard-cap of 12 crew. Mods that increase crew limits likely will not operate properly with BYOS. BYOS ships have additional options in construction, namely better engines and thrusters that can prove useful in exploration. ^red;'Help, I have BYOS lag!' ^reset; or ^yellow;I don't want atmosphere effects on my ship^reset;! BYOS has an atmosphere mode you can enable and disable from within your ^orange;ship SAIL computer^reset;. Simply access it, press the ^green;[ MISC ] ^reset;button and choose to disable the option. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^cyan;Swimming^reset; ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; Swimming operates differently than you're used to: Swim : ^yellow;W A S D^reset; Jump Out : ^green;hold ^yellow;W^green; , press ^yellow;Spacebar^reset;. It will take you a bit to get used to it, but the end result is a much easier control experience. Note that not all liquids provide buoyancy like water or other similar fluids. In these liquids, or within gases, physics can behave quite different than expected. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;The Frackin Wiki ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; If you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here: ^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset; ^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.",
        "translation": "このガイドでは、Frackin' Universeを遊ぶうえで知っておきたい基本事項を説明します。このMODは、Starbound本来の遊び方をさまざまな面で変更しています。 \n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;トライコーダー ― 冒険の心強い相棒：\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nトライコーダーは、いつでも^cyan;持ち物の中で最も役立つ道具^reset;です。^orange;研究システム^reset;を開けるほか、画面のアイコンからさまざまな機能を利用できます。さらに、次の操作にも対応しています。\n\n^green;マウスの右ボタン^reset; ― クエスト一覧を開きます。FUのチュートリアルを進めたり、役立つ報酬を手に入れたりできます。ぜひ活用してください。\n\n^green;Shift＋クリック^reset; ― 設定メニューを開きます。マターマニピュレーターの動作を調整したり、ペイントツールやワイヤーツールなどのスロットに、好きな道具を割り当てたりできます。トライコーダーを常設のショートカットにすることもできます。\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;研究って何をするの？^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nFrackinUniverseでは、ゲームの進行を支える^orange;研究システム^reset;が導入されています。^orange;個人用トライコーダー^reset;、^orange;SAILコンピューター^reset;、または^orange;クイックバー^reset;から開くことができ、新しい製作レシピを習得するために使います。レシピの解放には資源に加え、^green;研究ポイント^reset;という重要な通貨が必要です。\n\n研究システムでは、解放したいものを選び、自分の好きな順序で進められます。\n\n\nプレイ中は、何もしなくても毎秒1の^green;研究ポイント^reset;を獲得します。この獲得量は、惑星のティアが1上がるごとに+1増加します。たとえば危険度6の惑星では、基礎分と合わせて7を獲得します。\n\n^green;研究ポイント^reset;は、次のような方法でも獲得できます。\n^cyan;ノートパソコンとデータセンター^reset;\n^cyan;化石の収集^reset;\n^cyan;顕微鏡^reset;\n^cyan;高い狂気値^reset;\n^cyan;特定の防具や装備^reset;\n^green;プロテオン / 10^reset;（最大+10）\n\n探索や実験を続ければ、必要な研究ポイントは集まっていきます。^red;注意：探索していない間は研究ポイントの獲得速度が低下します。放置するだけで簡単に進めることはできません。^reset;\n\n解放したのに製作設備の一覧へ^red;表示されるはずのものが出てこない^reset;場合は、その設備を^orange;アップグレード^reset;したか確認してください。上位ティアのアイテムを作るには、設備のアップグレードも必要です。\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;プロテオンとは？^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nプロテオンは希少な通貨資源です。特定の店や加工方法で変換すると、大量の研究ポイントを得られます。多く集めることで、狂気値が下がる速度や研究ポイントの獲得速度にも影響します。特にインスタ・フロイトでは、狂気値をより速く減らせます。\n\nプロテオンを手に入れるには、アーティファクトと運が必要です。\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;種族固有の能力^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nFUのさまざまな種族には、それぞれ異なる特徴があります。火に強い種族、特別な能力を持つ種族、剣の扱いが得意な種族などがあり、遊び方の選択肢が広がります。\n\n^yellow;種族固有の能力を使いたくない場合^reset;\n\n種族固有の能力は、^orange;船のSAILコンピューター^reset;で有効・無効を切り替えられます。SAILを開いて^green;［その他］^reset;ボタンを押し、該当する設定を無効にしてください。\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;特殊なテック^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\n^orange;テックの使用コスト^reset;\nFUの一部のテックは、食料ゲージが利用できる場合、一定量まではエネルギーの代わりに食料を消費します。それを下回るとエネルギーを消費し、場合によっては体力も消費します。\n\n^orange;方向指定・カーソル照準のテック^reset;：\nこれらのテックは、^green;ヘッドテックのキー^reset;を押す、または押し続けることで使います。\n^orange;方向指定のテック^reset;は、^green;移動キー^reset;で向きを指定し、8方向に発動できます。真上や真下を狙うときは、^green;歩行キー^reset;を押し続けてください。\nFUでは、ハンタークロウ、レイザークロウ、マイナークロウが方向指定に対応しています。\n^orange;カーソル照準のテック^reset;には特別な方向入力は必要なく、カーソルの位置へ向けて発動します。\nFUでは、サイキックブラスト、シャードブラスト、アシッドスピットがカーソル照準に対応しています。さらに、^green;歩行キー^reset;を押し続けると、シャードブラストはランダムな方向へ拡散し、アシッドスピットは腐食弾の代わりにブロックを破壊する塊を発射します。\n\n^orange;能力値に応じたテックの強化^reset;：\n一部のテックは能力値に応じて強化されます。代表的なものを以下に示します。\n^orange;シャドウボーン^reset;：最大エネルギーに応じて強化されます。\n^orange;アシッドスピット^reset;：体力の増加量に応じて強化されます。腐食弾は継続ダメージを与え、ブロック破壊用の塊はダメージと持続時間が増えます。\n^orange;マイナークロウ^reset;：現在の食料ゲージに応じて強化されます。\n^orange;サイキックブラスト^reset;：最大エネルギーと防御力に応じて強化されます。\n^orange;レイザークロウ^reset;／^orange;ハンタークロウ^reset;：最大体力、攻撃力、現在の食料ゲージに応じて強化される狩猟ダメージを与えます。\n^orange;エルドゥウハルバースト^reset;、^orange;シャードブラスト^reset;、^orange;ドラゴンファイア^reset;：最大エネルギー、防御力、現在の食料ゲージに応じて強化されます。\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;戦闘^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n「FUガイド：戦闘」を参照してください。\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;メック^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nFUのメックは、Starbound本来のメックとは異なります。^red;燃料が必要^reset;になり、さまざまな種類の燃料を補給できます。また、体力と燃料・エネルギーのゲージが分かれています。長時間の採掘を支え、厳しい環境で生き延びやすくなる、より便利な乗り物です。\n\nメックには^green;質量^reset;が設定されます。^cyan;重い^reset;メックは^green;踏みつけで地面に大きなダメージ^reset;を与えられ、装甲も優れています。^cyan;軽い^reset;メックは^green;移動が速く^reset;、^green;燃費も大幅に向上^reset;します。\n\nメックの^green;ダッシュ^reset;は、^cyan;A^reset;または^cyan;D^reset;を素早く2回押すと使えます。\n\nメックの^green;飛行モード^reset;へ切り替えるには、^cyan;W^reset;を素早く2回押します。\n\nメックモジュールをはじめ、数十種類の新しいメック部品が追加されています。モジュールはメック用の拡張パーツとして働き、幅広いカスタマイズを可能にします。自分の遊び方に合う部品を探してみてください。\n\nメックの燃料補給や装備変更は、^orange;個人用トライコーダー^reset;から行えます。\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;状態効果^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nFrackinUniverseは、キャラクターにもモンスターにも作用する、^green;数多く^reset;の状態効果を追加します。有利なものも不利なものもあり、適切な装備を使えば、多くの効果を軽減したり無効化したりできます。\n\n実験や工夫で新しい環境を生き抜く方法を見つけ、そのための^orange;研究^reset;を計画することも、FUの楽しみのひとつです。\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;狂気^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n狂気は、FrackinUniverseに登場するもうひとつの通貨です。さまざまな行動、特に奇妙なことや恐ろしいことによって増えますが、時間とともに減少します。^#e43774;狂気値^reset;が高いほど、受ける悪影響も大きくなります。\n\n恐ろしいものを持ち歩いていると、時間とともに^#e43774;狂気値^reset;が増えることもあります。SAILが警告したときは、持ち物を確認してください。\n\n^#e43774;狂気^reset;によって起こりうる効果は、50種類以上あります。\n\n^yellow;狂気値を減らすには？^reset;\n\n^#e43774;狂気^reset;は、^green;研究^reset;の^orange;形而上学^reset;で消費できます。\n船のカウンセラーをクルーにする。\n^orange;インスタ・フロイト^reset;に座る：狂気値を急速に減らせます。\n^green;プロテオン / 10^reset;（最大-10）\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;遺伝子^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n遺伝子通貨は、2014～2020年に使われていた^red;33種類の遺伝子アイテム^reset;を置き換えたものです。現在は^green;遺伝子^reset;という1種類の通貨に統合され、総量を把握しやすくなりました。保管する資源の種類も30種類以上減っています。\n\n^green;遺伝子^reset;は、^orange;農業^reset;と^orange;遺伝学^reset;で使用します。\n\n以前の遺伝子アイテムは、ゼノラボまたは発芽台に入れるだけで、新しい遺伝子通貨へ変換できます。\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;BYOS（自分だけの船を作る）^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nFrackinUniverseでは、自分の船を一から建造できます。船の拡張はすべて自分で行うため、船のアップグレードを購入する必要はありません。エンジンも自作し、船を便利にする専用設備を製作できます。\nキャラクター作成時にBYOSを選ぶと、後から変更できない点に注意してください。\n\nキャラクター作成時には、^cyan;FUの船（Frackin Ship）^reset;または^cyan;標準の船（Vanilla Ship）^reset;を選べます。FUの船がBYOSに相当します。選択すると船の初期構成を決められ、その後は通常どおりプレイを始めます。\n\nBYOSの船では、クルーの受け入れに専用のルールを使います。\n\n^orange;クルー用権利証^reset;を使う場合は、^orange;コロニー用権利証^reset;と同じ条件を満たす必要があります（壁、ドア、照明、ベッド）。^red;\n\nまたは、\n\n^reset;手軽に受け入れたい場合は、^orange;クルー用ベッド^reset;を使えます。\n\n同じ部屋で^red;併用はできません^reset;。^orange;クルー用権利証^reset;か^orange;クルー用ベッド^reset;のどちらかを選んでください。\n\nクルーの上限は12人です。クルーの上限を増やすMODは、BYOSでは正常に動作しない可能性があります。\n\nBYOSの船には、高性能なエンジンやスラスターなど、探索に役立つ追加の建造オプションがあります。\n\n\n\n^red;「BYOSの船が重くて動作が遅い！」^reset;、または^yellow;「船内の大気の影響を無効にしたい！」^reset;場合\n\nBYOSの大気シミュレーションは、^orange;船のSAILコンピューター^reset;で有効・無効を切り替えられます。SAILを開いて^green;［その他］^reset;ボタンを押し、該当する設定を無効にしてください。\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;泳ぎ方^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n泳ぎの操作は、Starbound本来の操作と異なります。\n\n泳ぐ：^yellow;W A S D^reset;\n\n水面から飛び出す：^green;まず^yellow;W^green;を押し続け、^yellow;スペースキー^reset;を押します。\n\n慣れるまで少し時間がかかりますが、慣れれば泳ぎやすくなります。\n\n水と同じように浮力が働く液体ばかりではありません。そうした液体や気体の中では、動き方が予想と大きく異なることがあります。\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;Frackin' Universe Wiki\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nWikiで調べる場合は、次の^cyan;公式Wiki^reset;を利用してください。\n^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset;\n\nFandom版のWikiは情報が大幅に古くなっているため、^red;使用しないでください^reset;。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "title",
        "source": "001 ^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : ^yellow;^reset;Core Guide^yellow;^reset;",
        "normalizedSource": "001 ^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : ^yellow;^reset;Core Guide^yellow;^reset;",
        "translation": "001 ^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : ^yellow;^reset;基本ガイド^yellow;^reset;"
      }
    ],
    "ffguide2": [
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "To read this codex, use your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset; and click the Book icon.",
        "normalizedSource": "To read this codex, use your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset; and click the Book icon.",
        "translation": "このコーデックスを読むには、^orange;個人用トライコーダー^reset;を使って、本のアイコンをクリックしてください。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "description",
        "source": "How to Play",
        "normalizedSource": "How to Play",
        "translation": "遊び方"
      },
      {
        "field": "longContentPages",
        "source": "There are new worlds across the cosmos awaiting exploration. The next few pages will detail some of them. Note that there are many more than listed.\n\nBiomes can appear around different types of stars, and some appear only in specific stars. For example: You will never find an ^orange;Infernus^reset; around a ^white;Gentle Star^reset;.\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Star Types^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nGentle Star\nTemperate\nRadioactive\nFrozen\nFiery\nBinary\nRed\nBlue\nBlack\nDying\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Bog^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nRich in algae, muck, and plant life. They are ripe with rainy weather, and thick swamps. Travel can be difficult, but the surplus algae will be useful.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Rainforest^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nTeeming with plantlife, Rainforests have rich soil, far exceeding the capacity of ordinary dirt. They host a wide array of wildlife, including plenty of bees.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Crystalline^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nA rich source of silicon (thanks to the extraction of Purple Crystal) and ^yellow;Lunari^reset; crystals. Watch out for the crystal rain, though.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Gelatinous^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nGreat for genetic material. Definitely don't try the lettuce, unless you really like flavorless gelatin soup squishing in your mouth. If you need goopy stuff, this is your first stop.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Proto World^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese bizarre planets are not inhospitable, but the natural biological slime there can melt your flesh. Plus the slime storms, ew. And really, really weird plant life. But they are the only place to get the extremely valuable protocite. You'll need it. Also be advised that the atmosphere contains bizarre bacteria that affect unconditioned lifeforms negatively. Use caution when exploring.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Ice Waste^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nIce wastes are absolutely terrifyingly cold. Don't swim in the water or you'll freeze even faster. They do have some unique sorts of ice there, which provide something extra when extracting. Furthermore, valuable Isogen ore is plentiful on them.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Sulphuric^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese are among the harshest environments you'll encounter. Every moment on a sulphur world is lethal. Deadly winds, blowing debris, no oxygen. Lovely. But, they are extremely rich in Sulphur. Not the place for a summer house, though. Yet people keep trying...\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Penumbra^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nPitch black for most of their existence, these rare worlds have some sort of environmental barrier to the sun. A natural sunglasses-effect in the ozone, or something. Whatever the case...dark and spooky.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Wasteland^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nOnce bustling populations lived on these desolate rocks. Now, their ruins stud the surface like discarded refuse. Technology may remain that can be scavenged, and there is no shortage of Spare Parts if you are looking for some.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Irradiated^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese radioactive rocks are curiously abundant in native life. Granted, it's not edible and you still don't want to hang out there too much. You'll find heaps of radioactive resources here, obviously.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Infernus^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nI'd not suggest going here without a lot of protection. Their surfaces are far from hospitable. They are teeming with danger of every sort, but the allure of Pyreite ore is hard to resist.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Frozen Moon^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese frigid moons are quaint, and not altogether threatening. No life walks on their surfaces. On account of the whole no-air thing.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Nitrogen Sea^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nDoesn't this sound like a fun place to swim? Yea, it really isn't. Some handy liquid there, though.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Cybersphere^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nSomeone, at some point, built these impossibly huge constructs in space. How these were ever engineered remains a hotly contested debate among the scientific community.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Primeval Forest^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nHuge trees, lots of wildlife and abundant natural resources make these a wonderful place to visit. Typically not too dangerous, but watch your back anyhow...you never know what lurks in these huge forests. I've heard rumors of titanic reptiles standing 10 or more metres in the air!\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Atropus^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nA violation of all things decent, Atropus planets are both living and dead. They are quite literally composed of flesh, and some even believe them to be sentient. How they are even possible remains unknown but there is no doubt it is unnatural in every sense of tthe word.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Mountainous^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nWhile it is probably fairly obvious by the name, I have been instructed to inform you that these worlds are rather bumpy and mountainy. They are rich in resources, possessing more metal than most biomes (other than Sulphuric) including rare Zerchesium ore.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Tidewater^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nThese oceans are vastly more rocky and unstable than typical water planets. They generally lack tropical islands, but if you love rocky terrain and coral reefs they might be right up your alley. Through Tidewater, explorers have found unusual nodules capable of scientific miracles.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Lightless^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese unusual worlds are ancient and something prevents any sun from reaching their surfaces. There may be some useful things there, however. Bring lots of lights!\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;The Frackin Wiki\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nIf you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here:\n^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset;\n\n^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.",
        "normalizedSource": "There are new worlds across the cosmos awaiting exploration. The next few pages will detail some of them. Note that there are many more than listed. Biomes can appear around different types of stars, and some appear only in specific stars. For example: You will never find an ^orange;Infernus^reset; around a ^white;Gentle Star^reset;. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Star Types^reset; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Gentle Star Temperate Radioactive Frozen Fiery Binary Red Blue Black Dying ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Bog^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Rich in algae, muck, and plant life. They are ripe with rainy weather, and thick swamps. Travel can be difficult, but the surplus algae will be useful. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Rainforest^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Teeming with plantlife, Rainforests have rich soil, far exceeding the capacity of ordinary dirt. They host a wide array of wildlife, including plenty of bees. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Crystalline^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; A rich source of silicon (thanks to the extraction of Purple Crystal) and ^yellow;Lunari^reset; crystals. Watch out for the crystal rain, though. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Gelatinous^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Great for genetic material. Definitely don't try the lettuce, unless you really like flavorless gelatin soup squishing in your mouth. If you need goopy stuff, this is your first stop. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Proto World^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; These bizarre planets are not inhospitable, but the natural biological slime there can melt your flesh. Plus the slime storms, ew. And really, really weird plant life. But they are the only place to get the extremely valuable protocite. You'll need it. Also be advised that the atmosphere contains bizarre bacteria that affect unconditioned lifeforms negatively. Use caution when exploring. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Ice Waste^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Ice wastes are absolutely terrifyingly cold. Don't swim in the water or you'll freeze even faster. They do have some unique sorts of ice there, which provide something extra when extracting. Furthermore, valuable Isogen ore is plentiful on them. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Sulphuric^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; These are among the harshest environments you'll encounter. Every moment on a sulphur world is lethal. Deadly winds, blowing debris, no oxygen. Lovely. But, they are extremely rich in Sulphur. Not the place for a summer house, though. Yet people keep trying... ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Penumbra^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Pitch black for most of their existence, these rare worlds have some sort of environmental barrier to the sun. A natural sunglasses-effect in the ozone, or something. Whatever the case...dark and spooky. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Wasteland^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Once bustling populations lived on these desolate rocks. Now, their ruins stud the surface like discarded refuse. Technology may remain that can be scavenged, and there is no shortage of Spare Parts if you are looking for some. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Irradiated^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; These radioactive rocks are curiously abundant in native life. Granted, it's not edible and you still don't want to hang out there too much. You'll find heaps of radioactive resources here, obviously. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Infernus^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; I'd not suggest going here without a lot of protection. Their surfaces are far from hospitable. They are teeming with danger of every sort, but the allure of Pyreite ore is hard to resist. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Frozen Moon^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; These frigid moons are quaint, and not altogether threatening. No life walks on their surfaces. On account of the whole no-air thing. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Nitrogen Sea^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Doesn't this sound like a fun place to swim? Yea, it really isn't. Some handy liquid there, though. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Cybersphere^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Someone, at some point, built these impossibly huge constructs in space. How these were ever engineered remains a hotly contested debate among the scientific community. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Primeval Forest^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Huge trees, lots of wildlife and abundant natural resources make these a wonderful place to visit. Typically not too dangerous, but watch your back anyhow...you never know what lurks in these huge forests. I've heard rumors of titanic reptiles standing 10 or more metres in the air! ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Atropus^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; A violation of all things decent, Atropus planets are both living and dead. They are quite literally composed of flesh, and some even believe them to be sentient. How they are even possible remains unknown but there is no doubt it is unnatural in every sense of tthe word. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Mountainous^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; While it is probably fairly obvious by the name, I have been instructed to inform you that these worlds are rather bumpy and mountainy. They are rich in resources, possessing more metal than most biomes (other than Sulphuric) including rare Zerchesium ore. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Tidewater^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; These oceans are vastly more rocky and unstable than typical water planets. They generally lack tropical islands, but if you love rocky terrain and coral reefs they might be right up your alley. Through Tidewater, explorers have found unusual nodules capable of scientific miracles. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Lightless^white; ^blue;------------------------^reset; These unusual worlds are ancient and something prevents any sun from reaching their surfaces. There may be some useful things there, however. Bring lots of lights! ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;The Frackin Wiki ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; If you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here: ^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset; ^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.",
        "translation": "宇宙には新しい世界があり、探究を待っています。 次のいくつかのページでは、それらのいくつかを詳述します。 リストされている以上のものがあることに注意してください。\n\n生物体は様々な種類の星の周りに現れ、特定の星にのみ現れるものもある。 例えば、^orange;灼熱地獄 ^reset; は ^white; ジェントルスター ^reset; の周りには決して見つかりません。\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;StarTypes^reset;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\nジェントルスター\n温度\n放射性物質\n凍結\n火\nバイナリ\n赤\n青\n黒\n死因\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;沼地^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n藻類、マック、植物が豊富。 雨天と厚い沼地で熟しています。 旅行は難しいかもしれませんが、余剰藻類が役立ちます。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;熱帯雨林^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n熱帯雨林は、植物を育て、豊かな土壌を持ち、通常の土の容量をはるかに超えています。 たくさんのミツバチを含む幅広い野生生物を飼育しています。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;クリスタルライン^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\nシリコン(パープル結晶の抽出のおかげで)と^yellow;ルナリ^reset;結晶の豊富なソース。 ただし、結晶雨には注意してください。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;Gelatinous^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n遺伝材料に最適です。 レタスを口の中で口の中で口にくっつくような無味ゼラチンスープが本当に気に入らないなら、絶対に試してみないでください。 グーピーなものが必要なら、これはあなたの最初の停留所です。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;ProtoWorld^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\nこの奇妙な惑星は、決して不快なものではありませんが、自然の生物学的な粘液はあなたの肉を溶かすことができます。 あと、悪天候も。 本当に奇妙な植物です しかし、彼らは非常に貴重なプロトサイトを取得する唯一の場所です。 必要なんだ。 また、大気には、無条件の生活に悪影響を及ぼす奇妙な細菌が含まれていることも注意してください。 探索するときは注意してください。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;氷廃棄物^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n氷の廃棄物は絶対に恐ろしく寒い。 水中を泳いではいけない。さもないともっと早く凍るよ。 それらは、抽出時に余分な何かを提供する氷のいくつかのユニークな種類を持っています。 また、貴重ないそげん鉱石も豊富です。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green; 硫黄 ^white; 。\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\nこれらはあなたが遭遇する最も厳しい環境です。 硫黄の世界のすべての瞬間は致命的です。 風が強く、破片を吹き、酸素がない。 素敵。 しかし、彼らは硫黄が非常に豊富です。 でも、夏の家のための場所ではありません。 でも、みんな試しに...\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;半影^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n黒く光るこの珍しい世界は、太陽に何らかの環境的な障壁を与えています。 オゾン、または何かに自然なサングラス効果。 どんな場合も...暗くて不気味です。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;荒廃地^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\nかつては荒廃した岩石の上に、賑やかな人々が住んでいた。 遺骸は捨てられたゴミのように表面を覆う。 スキャベンジされる技術のままで、探しているのなら予備部品が不足することはありません。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;照射^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\nこれらの放射性岩は、ネイティブの生活に好奇心をそそるほど豊富です。 確かに、それは食べられないし、あなたはまだあまりにもそこにたむろしたくない。 放射性資源の山はここにあります\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;灼熱地獄^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n保護があまり無いでここには行きたくない。 彼らの表面は決して親切ではない。 彼らはあらゆる種類の危険を冒していますが、パイライト鉱石の魅力には抵抗できません。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;凍った月^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\nこれらの冷たい月は古風で、脅威ではありません。 命は表面を歩かない。 空気を使わないことのすべてを考慮に入れます。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;窒素海^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\nここは泳ぐのが楽しい場所のように聞こえませんか? そうだな、そうじゃない。 でも、便利な液体がある。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;Cybersphere^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\nある時点で、誰かが宇宙で信じられないほど巨大な構造物を組み立てました。 こういった研究がどのように行われたかは、科学界の間では議論の的になっている。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;原生林 森林 ^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n巨大な木々、たくさんの野生動物、豊富な天然資源がこれらを訪問する素晴らしい場所です。 普通は危険すぎないけど、背中を見張って...この巨大な森に潜むものなんて、全然分からない。 タイタニック・レチルが立っているという噂を聞きました 10 空中でそれ以上!\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;アトロポス^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\nアトロプス惑星は、生きたものと死んだものの両方です。 文字通り肉体でできていて、感覚的だと考える人もいる。 それらがどのように可能かは不明だが、言葉のあらゆる意味で不自然であることは間違いない。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;山岳^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n名前からはかなり明らかですが、私はこれらの世界はややふさふさで山っぽいことをあなたに知らせるよう指示されています。 資源が豊富で、希少なゼルケシウム鉱石を含むほとんどの生物群(硫黄を除く)よりも多くの金属を保有する。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;潮水^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n\nこれらの海は、典型的な水惑星よりもはるかに岩石が多く不安定です。 一般的に熱帯の島はなく、岩の多い地形やサンゴ礁が好きな人は、あなたの路地を直ぐ上るかもしれません。 潮流水を通して、探検家たちは科学的な奇跡を起こせる異常な結節を発見した。\n\n\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n^green;光のない^white;\n^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\nこれらの珍しい世界は古代であり、何かが太陽が表面に達するのを防ぎます。 でも、便利なことがあるかもしれない。 ライトをたくさん持ってきてください!\n\n^blue; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^yellow; ウィキの亀裂\n^blue; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\nWikiのヘルプが必要な場合は、 ^cyan; 公式wiki ^reset; _ をここで使用します。\n^green;frackinUniverse.miraheze.org ^reset;\n\n^red; ^reset; は Fandom wiki を使用しないでください。 恐ろしく時代遅れです。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "title",
        "source": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Biomes",
        "normalizedSource": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Biomes",
        "translation": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : バイオーム"
      }
    ],
    "ffguide3": [
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "To read this codex, use your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset; and click the Book icon.",
        "normalizedSource": "To read this codex, use your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset; and click the Book icon.",
        "translation": "このコーデックスを読むには、^orange;個人用トライコーダー^reset;を使って、本のアイコンをクリックしてください。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "description",
        "source": "FU Stats",
        "normalizedSource": "FU Stats",
        "translation": "FUの能力値"
      },
      {
        "field": "longContentPages",
        "source": "In addition to stats normally present in Starbound, FU adds a host of its own as well. Some may be character stats, some may be weapon stats. Some may be both! They are detailed within this guide for easy access later.\n\n^green;Charisma^white; - When shopping on FU space stations, Charisma helps you to make a profit by influencing ^cyan;Selling and Buying^reset; values. A high charisma means a high income ratio! Note that this only applies on Space Station trades and their related Kiosks for the time being. As a special note, every 33% charisma will allow you to bring an additional crewmember with you in the field. Be warned, penalties to charisma can have the opposite effect!\n\n^green;Stun Chance^white; - With blunt weapons, each hit has a chance to stun enemies. Likewise with successful shieldbashes. This stat influences the chance that this stun will occur. This also can occur with daggers, rapiers, and a few other weapons.\n\n^green;Shieldbash Chance^white; - When blocking with your shield, you have a chance to shieldbash. This stat influences the chances that the bash succeeds.\n\n^green;Shieldbash Push^white; - How far a shieldbash will push an enemy, and how much damage it will inflict when successful.\n\n^green;Projectile Count^white; - Typically only seen as a stat on weapons, it is indicated in most gun tooltips by 3 diagonally aligned bullets. This indicates how many projectiles are fired at once.\n\n^green;Burst Count^white; - Exclusively on weapons. Indicated in the tooltip by a spread of 4 small bullets. These weapons fire a burst of projectiles in sequence.\n\n^green;Tech Bonus^white; - There are various types of Tech Bonus. These will be listed when relevant. Any such bonus will influence techs. For example 'Jump Tech +25%' increase the efficiency of any Jump related techs by that amount.\n\n^green;Weapon Mastery^white; - Occasionally you'll find gear that can grant 'Weapon Mastery' at different levels. Weapon Mastery provides additional benefits to particular weapons.\n\n^green;Crit Chance^white; - The likelihood that you will score a successful critical attack with your weapon. Note that this can be a stat on both you -and- on a weapon. They will combine.\n\n^green;Crit Damage Bonus^white; - The total bonus applied, in percentage, to critical damage strikes.\n\n^green;Leech^white; - A form of healing that is unaffected by normal healing modifiers. This healing is divided over a duration (10 seconds at base); +10% leech means you will heal up to 1% of your health per second for 10 seconds per instance.\n\n^green;Maximum Leech^white; - The maximum amount of healing you can have at a time, from leech. The default is 10%; from all leech instances you will not be able to heal more than 10% of your health per second.\n\n^#e43774;Madness^white; - A measurement of your current sanity. The higher the value, the crazier you are. More than 50 effects can occur from madness, and not all are bad. You can spend Madness in the ^#e43774;Metaphysics Research Tree^reset;.\n\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;The Frackin Wiki\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nIf you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here:\n^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset;\n\n^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.",
        "normalizedSource": "In addition to stats normally present in Starbound, FU adds a host of its own as well. Some may be character stats, some may be weapon stats. Some may be both! They are detailed within this guide for easy access later. ^green;Charisma^white; - When shopping on FU space stations, Charisma helps you to make a profit by influencing ^cyan;Selling and Buying^reset; values. A high charisma means a high income ratio! Note that this only applies on Space Station trades and their related Kiosks for the time being. As a special note, every 33% charisma will allow you to bring an additional crewmember with you in the field. Be warned, penalties to charisma can have the opposite effect! ^green;Stun Chance^white; - With blunt weapons, each hit has a chance to stun enemies. Likewise with successful shieldbashes. This stat influences the chance that this stun will occur. This also can occur with daggers, rapiers, and a few other weapons. ^green;Shieldbash Chance^white; - When blocking with your shield, you have a chance to shieldbash. This stat influences the chances that the bash succeeds. ^green;Shieldbash Push^white; - How far a shieldbash will push an enemy, and how much damage it will inflict when successful. ^green;Projectile Count^white; - Typically only seen as a stat on weapons, it is indicated in most gun tooltips by 3 diagonally aligned bullets. This indicates how many projectiles are fired at once. ^green;Burst Count^white; - Exclusively on weapons. Indicated in the tooltip by a spread of 4 small bullets. These weapons fire a burst of projectiles in sequence. ^green;Tech Bonus^white; - There are various types of Tech Bonus. These will be listed when relevant. Any such bonus will influence techs. For example 'Jump Tech +25%' increase the efficiency of any Jump related techs by that amount. ^green;Weapon Mastery^white; - Occasionally you'll find gear that can grant 'Weapon Mastery' at different levels. Weapon Mastery provides additional benefits to particular weapons. ^green;Crit Chance^white; - The likelihood that you will score a successful critical attack with your weapon. Note that this can be a stat on both you -and- on a weapon. They will combine. ^green;Crit Damage Bonus^white; - The total bonus applied, in percentage, to critical damage strikes. ^green;Leech^white; - A form of healing that is unaffected by normal healing modifiers. This healing is divided over a duration (10 seconds at base); +10% leech means you will heal up to 1% of your health per second for 10 seconds per instance. ^green;Maximum Leech^white; - The maximum amount of healing you can have at a time, from leech. The default is 10%; from all leech instances you will not be able to heal more than 10% of your health per second. ^#e43774;Madness^white; - A measurement of your current sanity. The higher the value, the crazier you are. More than 50 effects can occur from madness, and not all are bad. You can spend Madness in the ^#e43774;Metaphysics Research Tree^reset;. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;The Frackin Wiki ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; If you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here: ^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset; ^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.",
        "translation": "Starboundに通常存在する統計に加えて、FUは自身のホストも追加する。 文字統計値、武器統計値など。 両方かもしれない。 後日簡単にアクセスできるように、このガイドで詳しく説明されています。\n\n^green; カリスマ ^white; - FU宇宙ステーションで買い物をするとき、カリスマは ^cyan; 販売と購入 ^reset; 値に影響を与えて利益を上げるのに役立ちます。 高カリスマ性は高所得率を意味します! なお、これは当面は宇宙ステーションの取引とその関連キオスクにのみ適用される。 特別な注意として、すべての 33% カリスマでは、フィールドに追加のクルーメンバーを連れて行くことができます。 注意してください、カリスマへの罰則は反対の効果を持つことができます!\n\n^green;気絶 確率 ^white; - 鈍い武器で、各ヒットは敵を刺すチャンスがあります。 同様に、シールドバッシュも成功した。 この統計は、このスタンが発生する可能性に影響を与えます。 これは短剣、レイピア、およびその他のいくつかの武器でも起こり得ます。\n\n^green; Shieldbash 確率 ^white; - シールドでブロックすると、シールドバッシュを選択できます。 この統計は、bashが成功する可能性に影響を与えます。\n\n^green; Shieldbash 押し出し ^white; - シールドバッシュが敵をどのくらい押し出すか、そしてそれが成功したときにどれだけの損害を与えるか。\n\n^green;Projectile Count ^white; - 典型的には武器のステータスと見なされるだけであり、ほとんどの銃器の先端には3斜めに並んだ弾丸で示されています。 これは一度に発射される発射物の数を示しています。\n\n^green;バーストカウント^white; - 武器に排他的。 4 小さな弾丸の広がりによってツールチップに表示します。 これらの武器は一連の発射物を発射する。\n\n^green;Tech ボーナス ^white; - さまざまな種類のTech ボーナスがあります。 これらは関連する場合にリストされます。 そのようなボーナスは技術に影響を与えます。 例えば、'JumpTech+25%' は、ジャンプ関連の技術の効率をその量で向上させます。\n\n^green;武器 習熟度 ^white; - 時には、異なるレベルで「武器 習熟度」を付与できるギアを見つけることがあります。 武器 習熟度は、特定の武器に追加のメリットを提供します。\n\n^green;クリティカル率 ^white; - 武器でクリティカルアタックを成功させる可能性。 これは、武器のオンとオンの両方のステータスである可能性があることに注意してください。 組み合わせる。\n\n^green;クリティカル ダメージボーナス ^white; - 重大なダメージストライクに対して適用される合計ボーナス。\n\n^green;吸収^white; - 通常の治癒修飾剤の影響を受けない癒しの形態。 この癒しは、期間(期間)で分割されます。10 ベースで秒。 +10% リーチとは 癒しを 1% 毎秒の健康状態を 10 インスタンスあたり秒数\n\n^green;最大リーチ^white; - リーチから一度に受けられる最大の癒し。 デフォルトは 10% です。すべてのリーチインスタンスから、毎秒のヘルスの 10% 以上のヒーリングを行うことはできません。\n\n^#e43774;狂気^white; - あなたの現在の正気の測定。 値が高いほど、クレイジーです。 50 以上の効果は狂気から発生する可能性があり、すべてが悪いわけではありません。 狂気は^#e43774; 形而上学 研究 Tree ^reset; で過ごすことができます。\n\n\n\n^blue; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^yellow; ウィキの亀裂\n^blue; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\nWikiのヘルプが必要な場合は、 ^cyan; 公式wiki ^reset; _ をここで使用します。\n^green;frackinUniverse.miraheze.org ^reset;\n\n^red; ^reset; は Fandom wiki を使用しないでください。 恐ろしく時代遅れです。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "title",
        "source": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Stats",
        "normalizedSource": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Stats",
        "translation": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : 能力値"
      }
    ],
    "ffguide4": [
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "To read this codex, use your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset; and click the Book icon.",
        "normalizedSource": "To read this codex, use your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset; and click the Book icon.",
        "translation": "このコーデックスを読むには、^orange;個人用トライコーダー^reset;を使って、本のアイコンをクリックしてください。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "description",
        "source": "A comprehensive list of medical station buffs.",
        "normalizedSource": "A comprehensive list of medical station buffs.",
        "translation": "医療ステーションで受けられる強化効果の一覧。"
      },
      {
        "field": "longContentPages",
        "source": "Welcome customer to the 3rd edition brochure of [REDACTED]'s medical station technologies, detailing all the possible ^orange;Enhancements^reset; that our medical personnel can bestow upon you.\nAs our staff will confirm, all procedures and fees are final, refunds are not available. For your safety, these modifications will not persist through a respawn chamber. Our available benefits are as follows:\n\n^red;Berserker Rage^reset;: ^green;25% More^reset; Power, Increased Movement Speed. -^red;50^reset;% Knockback Resistance, -^red;35^reset; Protection.\n\n^gray;Glass Cannon^reset;: ^green;100% More^reset; Damage at the cost of ^red;90% Less^reset; Protection\n\n^green;Immunization^reset;: Provides ^cyan;immunity^reset; to most negative status effects. ^red;10% Less^reset; Power and Protection.\n\n^white;Juggernaut^reset;: You become ^cyan;immune^reset; to knockback and gain ^green;50^reset; protection, but your movement speed is reduced by ^red;33%^reset;.\n\n^green;Toxic Cloud^reset;: Every 3 seconds a ^green;toxic cloud^reset; that lasts 5 seconds and deals 30 piercing damage is released at your location. Every time this happens, you take ^red;5^reset; piercing damage. ^red;20^reset;% Increased Hunger Drain.\n\n^#B200FF;Experiment #322^reset;: Applies random ^green;positive^reset; and/or ^red;negative^reset; statuses every 10 seconds which last 15-25 seconds.\n\n^red;Trollblood^reset;: Regenerate ^green;40^reset;% of damage taken over 5 seconds, at the cost of ^red;20% Less^reset; HP and ^red;50^reset;% increased Energy Block Time.\n\n^green;Renergizer^reset;: ^green;50% More^reset; Energy, ^green;33% More^reset; Energy Regeneration. Hunger Drain increased by ^red;25^reset;%. ^red;100^reset;% Increased Energy Block Time.\n\n^yellow;Hypopanic^reset;: ^green;33% More^reset; Energy Regen, -^red;50^reset; Energy. In addition, Increased movement speed the less energy you have (up to +^green;67^reset;% speed at 35% energy remaining). Taking damage briefly ^red;stops^reset; energy regen, and ^red;consumes energy^reset; for 150% of damage.\n\n^green;Hivemind^reset;: While over 10% health, drains ^red;1.25^reset;% of your Maximum Health to ^green;shoot a projectile^reset; at the closest enemy, prioritizing targets not hit recently, in a medium radius with a clear line of fire every 0.5 seconds, dealing ^green;2.5^reset;% of your Max HP as base damage (^orange;affected by power multiplier^reset;) on impact and causing ^red;Beestings^reset;.\n\n^cyan;Mitochondria^reset;: Consumes ^red;2^reset; energy to regenerate ^green;1^reset; health every 0.15 seconds. Energy will regenerate only at full health.\n\n^#7A7D81;Shadow Repel^reset;: Increases shadow resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to shadow status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%.\n\n^#C5B00A;Radiation Repel^reset;: Increases radiation resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to radiation status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%.\n\n^#69B115;Poison Repel^reset;: Increases poison resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to poison status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%.\n\n^#A1F1FE;Ice Repel^reset;: Increases ice resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to ice status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%.\n\n^#E99400;Fire Repel^reset;: Increases fire resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to fire status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%.\n\n^#9711E4;Electrical Repel^reset;: Increases electric resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to electric status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%.\n\n^#6062EB;Cosmic Repel^reset;: Increases cosmic resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to cosmic status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%.",
        "normalizedSource": "Welcome customer to the 3rd edition brochure of [REDACTED]'s medical station technologies, detailing all the possible ^orange;Enhancements^reset; that our medical personnel can bestow upon you. As our staff will confirm, all procedures and fees are final, refunds are not available. For your safety, these modifications will not persist through a respawn chamber. Our available benefits are as follows: ^red;Berserker Rage^reset;: ^green;25% More^reset; Power, Increased Movement Speed. -^red;50^reset;% Knockback Resistance, -^red;35^reset; Protection. ^gray;Glass Cannon^reset;: ^green;100% More^reset; Damage at the cost of ^red;90% Less^reset; Protection ^green;Immunization^reset;: Provides ^cyan;immunity^reset; to most negative status effects. ^red;10% Less^reset; Power and Protection. ^white;Juggernaut^reset;: You become ^cyan;immune^reset; to knockback and gain ^green;50^reset; protection, but your movement speed is reduced by ^red;33%^reset;. ^green;Toxic Cloud^reset;: Every 3 seconds a ^green;toxic cloud^reset; that lasts 5 seconds and deals 30 piercing damage is released at your location. Every time this happens, you take ^red;5^reset; piercing damage. ^red;20^reset;% Increased Hunger Drain. ^#B200FF;Experiment #322^reset;: Applies random ^green;positive^reset; and/or ^red;negative^reset; statuses every 10 seconds which last 15-25 seconds. ^red;Trollblood^reset;: Regenerate ^green;40^reset;% of damage taken over 5 seconds, at the cost of ^red;20% Less^reset; HP and ^red;50^reset;% increased Energy Block Time. ^green;Renergizer^reset;: ^green;50% More^reset; Energy, ^green;33% More^reset; Energy Regeneration. Hunger Drain increased by ^red;25^reset;%. ^red;100^reset;% Increased Energy Block Time. ^yellow;Hypopanic^reset;: ^green;33% More^reset; Energy Regen, -^red;50^reset; Energy. In addition, Increased movement speed the less energy you have (up to +^green;67^reset;% speed at 35% energy remaining). Taking damage briefly ^red;stops^reset; energy regen, and ^red;consumes energy^reset; for 150% of damage. ^green;Hivemind^reset;: While over 10% health, drains ^red;1.25^reset;% of your Maximum Health to ^green;shoot a projectile^reset; at the closest enemy, prioritizing targets not hit recently, in a medium radius with a clear line of fire every 0.5 seconds, dealing ^green;2.5^reset;% of your Max HP as base damage (^orange;affected by power multiplier^reset;) on impact and causing ^red;Beestings^reset;. ^cyan;Mitochondria^reset;: Consumes ^red;2^reset; energy to regenerate ^green;1^reset; health every 0.15 seconds. Energy will regenerate only at full health. ^#7A7D81;Shadow Repel^reset;: Increases shadow resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to shadow status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%. ^#C5B00A;Radiation Repel^reset;: Increases radiation resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to radiation status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%. ^#69B115;Poison Repel^reset;: Increases poison resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to poison status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%. ^#A1F1FE;Ice Repel^reset;: Increases ice resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to ice status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%. ^#E99400;Fire Repel^reset;: Increases fire resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to fire status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%. ^#9711E4;Electrical Repel^reset;: Increases electric resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to electric status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%. ^#6062EB;Cosmic Repel^reset;: Increases cosmic resistance by ^green;50^reset;% and grants ^cyan;immunity^reset; to cosmic status effects, but reduces the overall effectiveness of other resistances (except physical) by ^red;33^reset;%.",
        "translation": "リダクト)の医療ステーション技術の3rdエディションのパンフレットにお客様を歓迎します。可能なすべての^orange;Enhancements ^reset;を詳述します。\nスタッフが確認しますので、すべての手順と料金は最終であり、払い戻しはできません。 あなたの安全のために、これらの変更は再生室を通して持続しません。 利用可能な利点は次のとおりです。\n\n^red;Berserker 激怒 ^reset;:^green;25%More ^reset;Power、移動速度を増加。 -^red;50^reset;% ノックバック抵抗、-^red;35^reset; 保護。\n\n^gray;ガラス砲 ^reset;:^green;100% 以上 ^reset; ^red;90% より少ない ^reset; 保護の費用で損傷します。\n\n^green;免疫^reset;:ほとんどの負の状態効果に^cyan;免疫^reset;を提供します。 ^red;10%Less ^reset;電源と保護。\n\n^white;ジャガーノート^reset;:^cyan;免疫^reset;は、ノックバックして獲得します^green;50^reset;保護が、あなたの移動速度は^red;33%^reset;によって減少します。\n\n^green;有毒 Cloud^reset;全て 3 秒A ^green;毒雲^reset; それは続く 5 秒と取引 30 ピアス損傷は あなたの場所で解除されます。 このたびに ^red;5^reset; ピアス損傷を受ける。 ^red;20^reset;%飢餓ドレインを増やしました。\n\n^#B200FF;実験#322^reset;: ランダムに適用します。 ^green;ポジティブ^reset; そして/または ^red;ネガティブ^reset; 全てのステータス 10 最後の秒 15-25 秒ね\n\n^red;血を回す^reset;:再生 ^green;40^reset;% 被害を受けたこと 5 数秒で ^red;20% 少ない^reset; HPと ^red;50^reset;% エネルギーブロック時間の増加。\n\n^green;リナジャイザー ^reset;:^green;50%More ^reset;エネルギー, ^green;33%More ^reset;エネルギー再生。 飢餓ドレインは ^red;25^reset;% で増加しました。 ^red;100^reset;% エネルギーブロック時間の増加。\n\n^yellow; ヒポパニック ^reset;: ^green;33% より ^reset; エネルギーレーゲン、-^red;50^reset; エネルギー。 さらに、移動速度が増加すると、エネルギーが減少します(+^green;67^reset;% は 35% のエネルギーが残ります)。 手短に損害賠償します。 ^red;止まれ^reset; エネルギーを再生し ^red;エネルギーを消費し^reset; です 150% 被害を\n\n^green;心がけなさい^reset;: 終りまで 10% 健康 排水 ^red;1.25^reset;% 最大健康状態の ^green;発射物を発射する.^reset; 近距離の敵では 最近 撃たれていない目標を 0.5 秒数 取引 ^green;2.5^reset;% 最大 HP のベースとなる損傷。^orange;パワー・マルチプライヤーによって^reset;影響と原因について ^red;蜂^reset;.\n\n^cyan;Mitochondria ^reset; : ^red;2^reset; エネルギーを消費し、 ^green;1^reset; 健康を毎 0.15 秒再生します。 エネルギーは健康でのみ再生します。\n\n^#7A7D81;シャドウリペル^reset;:シャドウ抵抗を^green;50^reset;%で増加させ、シャドウステータス効果に^cyan;免疫^reset;を付与しますが、他の抵抗(物理を除く)の全体的な効果は^red;33^reset;%によって減少します。\n\n^#C5B00A; 放射線抵抗 ^reset; : 放射線抵抗を ^green;50^reset;% で増加させ、放射線状態効果に ^cyan; 免疫 ^reset; を与えるが、他の抵抗(物理を除く)の全体的な効果は ^red;33^reset;% によって減少する。\n\n^#69B115;毒 Repel ^reset; : 毒抵抗力を^green;50^reset;% で増加させ、毒ステータス効果に^cyan;免疫^reset; を付与しますが、他の抵抗の全体的な効果を^red;33^reset;% によって(物理的を除く)低下させます。\n\n^#A1F1FE;氷 Repel ^reset; : 氷の状態効果に対して^green;50^reset;% による耐氷性の向上と ^cyan; 免疫性 ^reset; を付与するが、他の抵抗(物理を除く)の全体的な有効性は ^red;33^reset;% によって低下する。\n\n^#E99400;ファイアリペル^reset; : ファイアステータス効果に対しては、^green;50^reset;% で耐火性を高め、^cyan; 免疫 ^reset; を付与しますが、他の抵抗(物理を除く)の全体的な効果は ^red;33^reset;% で減少します。\n\n^#9711E4;電気抵抗^reset;:電気抵抗を^green;50^reset;%で増加させ、電気状態効果に^cyan;免疫^reset;を付与しますが、^red;33^reset;%によって(物理的を除く)他の抵抗の全体的な有効性を減少させます。\n\n^#6062EB;宇宙属性 Repel ^reset; : 宇宙抵抗を^green;50^reset;% で増加させ、宇宙状態効果に ^cyan; 免疫 ^reset; を与えるが、他の抵抗(物理を除く)の全体的な有効性は ^red;33^reset;% によって減少する。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "title",
        "source": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset;: Medical Station Buffs",
        "normalizedSource": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset;: Medical Station Buffs",
        "translation": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset;: 医療ステーションの強化効果"
      }
    ],
    "ffguide5": [
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "To read this codex, use your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset; and click the Book icon.",
        "normalizedSource": "To read this codex, use your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset; and click the Book icon.",
        "translation": "このコーデックスを読むには、^orange;個人用トライコーダー^reset;を使って、本のアイコンをクリックしてください。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "description",
        "source": "Effects and You",
        "normalizedSource": "Effects and You",
        "translation": "環境と状態効果について"
      },
      {
        "field": "longContentPages",
        "source": "FrackinUniverse adds a great number of additional status effects, environmental hazards and environmental interactions. These can be both detrimental or beneficial depending on circumstances. This short guide should help to sort them out for you. Click next page to continue.\n\n\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Resistances^reset;:\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\n   Your resistance to effects is a pretty big deal. Bear in mind that the ^cyan;higher your value^reset; in a resistance type, the ^cyan;less you are affected by various debuffs as well as damage of that type^reset;. ^red;Weakness^reset; plays a factor too.\n\n   ^orange;Example^reset; :\n\n   A Floran has ^red;-50% Fire Resistance^reset;. He will take ^red;50% more damage from fire^reset; and will need an ^orange;additional 50% resistance^reset; in order to negate the penalty. That means that if a biome has a 40% resistance requirement for immunity to its effects he will ^orange;actually need 90%^reset;.\n\n   On the other hand, should your race have a ^cyan;bonus against elements^reset; you will need ^orange;less resistance^reset; than the normal amount. A race with ^green;+30% to Fire Resistance^reset; would need ^green;30% less resistance to fire effects in order to gain immunity^reset;. This allows you to have native immunity to minor effects such as desert heat or minor cold.\n\n^cyan;All resistances stack^reset;.\n\n\n   ^blue;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   As a general rule, assume resistance for biome types works as such:\n\n   ^green;20%^reset; (Mild) / ^yellow;40%^reset; (Moderate) / ^orange;60%^reset; (Extreme) / ^red;80%^reset; (Lethal)\n\n   Note that severe storms and other factors can influence the potency of a biomes effect, so on occasion you will have increased requirements while the event transpires.\n\n   Enemies can ^yellow;also have resistance strengths and weaknesses^reset;. Some are utterly immune to particular elements but easily felled by another, so be prepared to experiment.\n\n\n\n   ^blue;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Weather^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Various types of weather exist that can cause you harm. All can be resisted with a relevant protection type. Electrical storms are blocked by electric resistance, poison gas by poison, and so on. Some are less obvious however, such as Aether sickness, which requires specialized immunity from armor or augments.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Tile Breaking^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   If you're falling a bit too fast, some tiles will be unable to bear the strain of your weight. Ice, glass, slime, mud and other materials can break on impact. So, watch your step and take care.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Tile Effects^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Some tiles give buffs or debuffs when stepped on. Many of these will not give indicators, but will affect your movement. Snow, mud, jungle dirt and clay are some examples of this in action. Asphalt increases your ground speed, which is useful in bases. Experiment, and you might find some really useful stuff.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Temperature^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Cold, Heat and Radiation are things from ordinary Starbound, true. But in FU they play a different role. You won't find many Immunity effects on EPP packs. Instead, you'll primarily be using ^cyan;resistances^reset; obtained from them or augments. The higher your resistance in an element, the less it will bother you (or be blocked completely). Resistances stack.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Desert Heat^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Deserts are typically dry and non-humid, and their heat will slowly sap your health and food. From noon till sundown, it will be at its worst. Nights are relatively harmless and cool. Underground is colder. You can resist Deserts with Fire Resistance.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Jungle Heat^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Much like deserts, the heat of a Jungle will gradually drain your health and food, and is less severe at night. Unlike Desert Heat, it will take Physical resistance to counter this effect.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Radiation^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Radiation can be rather hazardous to the unprepared. This nasty effect will drain your health and energy rapidly (your max health/energy, not your current amount). If you reach 0 max health, you will die without warning...so do keep an eye on yourself. You will also starve faster. Wind will make things worse for you. Resistance requires Radioactive Resistance.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Sulphuric^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Sulphuric effects can be nasty, rapidly eating your armor and then doing health damage. Worse, on sulphuric worlds you have storms to contend with that make this effect even more dangerous, acid rain and pools of caustic acid! To resist this effect you'll need ^orange;Physical resistance^reset; or an ^orange;acid immunity^reset; effect.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Proto-Poison^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   This nasty effect is a threat on Proto Worlds. It will slowly sap your maximum health and *will* eventually kill you. Furthermore, it will reduce your critChance and apply damage over time. Seek out ^orange;proto-poison protection^reset; from various gears in your lab stations, ^orange;poison resistance^reset;.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Insanity^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   A constant degradation of your mental state, insanity saps your ability to protect yourself over a sustained period by draining your Protection. Additionally, it gives a mild bit of damage per tick. Your brain will become muddled and you will hallucinate, and go hungry faster. Augments and armor exist to combat this nasty effect, or you could have decent resistance to ^orange;both Shadow and Cosmic^reset; and you'll be okay.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Pressure^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Perhaps the deadliest of all the status effects, extreme pressure will ^red;definitely kill you in seconds^reset; if you do not have protection. Thankfully, it is found in few places (primarily on Gas Ball biomes). ^orange;Do not risk this environment effect without a protective suit^reset;. You *will* die.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Poison^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Fairly self explanatory. You don't want to be poisoned, but some are worse than others. You've got basic poisoned, mercury poison (which is especially nasty), contaminated water, food poisoning and darkwater poison to name a few. ^orange;Poisoned immunity or resistance^reset; will do the trick in avoiding this particular set of hazards. Potent poisons require higher amounts of resistance.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Pus^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   This fluid is absolutely repulsive, and even having the stuff on you causes retching and nausea. To traverse it, you will need some sort of ^orange;physical protection^reset;. This acidic bile is not your friend. I recommend against ingesting it.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Black Tar^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Black tar slows you down ^red;a lot^reset; and makes jumping a decent height nearly impossible. It hampers, but does not directly cause damage. You can block it with various armors or produce.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Gas^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Gas can be both positive (Helium 3) or negative (Caliginous Gas, Hydrogen etc) to immerse yourself in. Blocking gas is generally straightforward...^orange;wear something that protects from gas^reset;. However, Some are more specialized. ^orange;Caliginous Gas requires Shadow Resistance^reset; and ^orange;Poison Gas is non-functional with high poison resistance^reset;.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Organic Soup^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   One of the few effects that is actually something you *want*. Organic soup will increase your health total as well as remove the effects of hunger (and even fill you up!). Take a bath in it when you can!\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Bio Ooze^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   This fluid will stick to you, make you ill and affect your movement and survival chances while active. Wearing protection is recommended. Most common on Proto Worlds and a few other select biomes. Can be ^orange;blocked or mitigated with Poison Resistance or Immunity^reset;.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Liquid Nitrogen^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   I hear its a bit cold, so stepping in this might just be a crappy idea for fun times. However, you can make it a joyously fun event by simply wearing adequate ^orange;Ice Resistance^reset;.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Darkness^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   There is darkness capable of permeating your vision centers and turning the world around you into a lightless expanse. Be wary of these effects. Thankfully, it is most common in places that are already dark.\n\n\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\n   Note that there are many other effects you can be affected by in your exploration of the universe. Not all of them can be resisted, and some might be resisted by surprising things. Just stay aware...and stay safe.\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;The Frackin Wiki\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nIf you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here:\n^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset;\n\n^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.",
        "normalizedSource": "FrackinUniverse adds a great number of additional status effects, environmental hazards and environmental interactions. These can be both detrimental or beneficial depending on circumstances. This short guide should help to sort them out for you. Click next page to continue. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Resistances^reset;: ^blue;------------------------^reset; Your resistance to effects is a pretty big deal. Bear in mind that the ^cyan;higher your value^reset; in a resistance type, the ^cyan;less you are affected by various debuffs as well as damage of that type^reset;. ^red;Weakness^reset; plays a factor too. ^orange;Example^reset; : A Floran has ^red;-50% Fire Resistance^reset;. He will take ^red;50% more damage from fire^reset; and will need an ^orange;additional 50% resistance^reset; in order to negate the penalty. That means that if a biome has a 40% resistance requirement for immunity to its effects he will ^orange;actually need 90%^reset;. On the other hand, should your race have a ^cyan;bonus against elements^reset; you will need ^orange;less resistance^reset; than the normal amount. A race with ^green;+30% to Fire Resistance^reset; would need ^green;30% less resistance to fire effects in order to gain immunity^reset;. This allows you to have native immunity to minor effects such as desert heat or minor cold. ^cyan;All resistances stack^reset;. ^blue;-----------------------------------^reset; As a general rule, assume resistance for biome types works as such: ^green;20%^reset; (Mild) / ^yellow;40%^reset; (Moderate) / ^orange;60%^reset; (Extreme) / ^red;80%^reset; (Lethal) Note that severe storms and other factors can influence the potency of a biomes effect, so on occasion you will have increased requirements while the event transpires. Enemies can ^yellow;also have resistance strengths and weaknesses^reset;. Some are utterly immune to particular elements but easily felled by another, so be prepared to experiment. ^blue;-----------------------------------^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Weather^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; Various types of weather exist that can cause you harm. All can be resisted with a relevant protection type. Electrical storms are blocked by electric resistance, poison gas by poison, and so on. Some are less obvious however, such as Aether sickness, which requires specialized immunity from armor or augments. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Tile Breaking^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; If you're falling a bit too fast, some tiles will be unable to bear the strain of your weight. Ice, glass, slime, mud and other materials can break on impact. So, watch your step and take care. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Tile Effects^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; Some tiles give buffs or debuffs when stepped on. Many of these will not give indicators, but will affect your movement. Snow, mud, jungle dirt and clay are some examples of this in action. Asphalt increases your ground speed, which is useful in bases. Experiment, and you might find some really useful stuff. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Temperature^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; Cold, Heat and Radiation are things from ordinary Starbound, true. But in FU they play a different role. You won't find many Immunity effects on EPP packs. Instead, you'll primarily be using ^cyan;resistances^reset; obtained from them or augments. The higher your resistance in an element, the less it will bother you (or be blocked completely). Resistances stack. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Desert Heat^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; Deserts are typically dry and non-humid, and their heat will slowly sap your health and food. From noon till sundown, it will be at its worst. Nights are relatively harmless and cool. Underground is colder. You can resist Deserts with Fire Resistance. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Jungle Heat^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; Much like deserts, the heat of a Jungle will gradually drain your health and food, and is less severe at night. Unlike Desert Heat, it will take Physical resistance to counter this effect. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Radiation^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; Radiation can be rather hazardous to the unprepared. This nasty effect will drain your health and energy rapidly (your max health/energy, not your current amount). If you reach 0 max health, you will die without warning...so do keep an eye on yourself. You will also starve faster. Wind will make things worse for you. Resistance requires Radioactive Resistance. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Sulphuric^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; Sulphuric effects can be nasty, rapidly eating your armor and then doing health damage. Worse, on sulphuric worlds you have storms to contend with that make this effect even more dangerous, acid rain and pools of caustic acid! To resist this effect you'll need ^orange;Physical resistance^reset; or an ^orange;acid immunity^reset; effect. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Proto-Poison^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; This nasty effect is a threat on Proto Worlds. It will slowly sap your maximum health and *will* eventually kill you. Furthermore, it will reduce your critChance and apply damage over time. Seek out ^orange;proto-poison protection^reset; from various gears in your lab stations, ^orange;poison resistance^reset;. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Insanity^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; A constant degradation of your mental state, insanity saps your ability to protect yourself over a sustained period by draining your Protection. Additionally, it gives a mild bit of damage per tick. Your brain will become muddled and you will hallucinate, and go hungry faster. Augments and armor exist to combat this nasty effect, or you could have decent resistance to ^orange;both Shadow and Cosmic^reset; and you'll be okay. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Pressure^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; Perhaps the deadliest of all the status effects, extreme pressure will ^red;definitely kill you in seconds^reset; if you do not have protection. Thankfully, it is found in few places (primarily on Gas Ball biomes). ^orange;Do not risk this environment effect without a protective suit^reset;. You *will* die. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Poison^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; Fairly self explanatory. You don't want to be poisoned, but some are worse than others. You've got basic poisoned, mercury poison (which is especially nasty), contaminated water, food poisoning and darkwater poison to name a few. ^orange;Poisoned immunity or resistance^reset; will do the trick in avoiding this particular set of hazards. Potent poisons require higher amounts of resistance. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Pus^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; This fluid is absolutely repulsive, and even having the stuff on you causes retching and nausea. To traverse it, you will need some sort of ^orange;physical protection^reset;. This acidic bile is not your friend. I recommend against ingesting it. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Black Tar^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; Black tar slows you down ^red;a lot^reset; and makes jumping a decent height nearly impossible. It hampers, but does not directly cause damage. You can block it with various armors or produce. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Gas^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; Gas can be both positive (Helium 3) or negative (Caliginous Gas, Hydrogen etc) to immerse yourself in. Blocking gas is generally straightforward...^orange;wear something that protects from gas^reset;. However, Some are more specialized. ^orange;Caliginous Gas requires Shadow Resistance^reset; and ^orange;Poison Gas is non-functional with high poison resistance^reset;. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Organic Soup^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; One of the few effects that is actually something you *want*. Organic soup will increase your health total as well as remove the effects of hunger (and even fill you up!). Take a bath in it when you can! ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Bio Ooze^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; This fluid will stick to you, make you ill and affect your movement and survival chances while active. Wearing protection is recommended. Most common on Proto Worlds and a few other select biomes. Can be ^orange;blocked or mitigated with Poison Resistance or Immunity^reset;. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Liquid Nitrogen^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; I hear its a bit cold, so stepping in this might just be a crappy idea for fun times. However, you can make it a joyously fun event by simply wearing adequate ^orange;Ice Resistance^reset;. ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Darkness^reset; ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset; There is darkness capable of permeating your vision centers and turning the world around you into a lightless expanse. Be wary of these effects. Thankfully, it is most common in places that are already dark. ^blue;------------------------^reset; Note that there are many other effects you can be affected by in your exploration of the universe. Not all of them can be resisted, and some might be resisted by surprising things. Just stay aware...and stay safe. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^yellow;The Frackin Wiki ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; If you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here: ^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset; ^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.",
        "translation": "FrackinUniverseは、多くの追加のステータス効果、環境上の危険性、環境上の相互作用を追加します。 これらは、状況に応じて有害または有益である可能性があります。 この短いガイドはあなたのためにそれらを並べ替えるのに役立ちます。 次のページをクリックして続行します。\n\n\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n   ^yellow;レジスタンス^reset;:\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n\n   効果に対する抵抗はとても大きいのです ^cyan;あなたの価値は^reset; 抵抗のタイプでは ^cyan;さまざまなデバッフやそのタイプの損傷に影響を受けにくくなります。^reset;. ^red;弱さ^reset; 要因にもなります\n\n   ^orange;例^reset;例:\n\n   花屋は ^red;-50% 耐火性^reset;彼は取る ^red;50% 火による被害は^reset; 必要なのは ^orange;追加 50% 抵抗^reset; ペナルティを否定するためです つまり バイオームに 40% 免疫力に対する抵抗力の要求は ^orange;必要なのは 90%^reset;.\n\n   一方 人種が同じなら ^cyan;要素に対するボーナス^reset; 必要なのは ^orange;抵抗力も減ります^reset; 通常の量よりも ^green;+30% 耐火性^reset; 必要となるでしょう ^green;30% 防火効果に対する抵抗が減り^reset;これにより、砂漠の暑さや小さな寒さなどのマイナーな効果に対するネイティブ免疫を持つことができます。\n\n^cyan; すべての抵抗スタック ^reset; 。\n\n\n   ^blue; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   原則として、バイオームタイプの抵抗を仮定すると、次のようになります。\n\n   ^green;20%^reset;(Mild) / ^yellow;40%^reset;(Moderate) / ^orange;60%^reset;(Extreme) / ^red;80%^reset;(Lethal)\n\n   激しい嵐やその他の要因がバイオーム効果の効力に影響を与える可能性があるため、イベントが送信される間、要件が増加することがあります。\n\n   敵は ^yellow;抵抗力と弱さがあり^reset;特定の要素に完全に免疫があるものもありますが、簡単に別の要素に倒れてしまうため、実験する準備をしてください。\n\n\n\n   ^blue; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;天気^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   さまざまな種類の天候があり害を及ぼす可能性があります全ては関連する保護タイプで抵抗できます電気的嵐は電気抵抗によって遮断され毒ガスは毒によってなどですしかしアーサー病のような装甲や拡張から特別な免疫を必要とするものもあります\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;TileBreaking^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   少し速すぎると体重の緊張に耐えられないタイルがいくつかあります氷、ガラス、スライム、泥などの材料が衝突で壊れる恐れがありますだから足元を見て気をつけてください\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;タイル効果^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   階段を上ると瓦が立ち上がることがあります多くは指標を与えませんが動きに影響します雪や泥やジャングルの汚れや粘土が作用している例ですアスファルトは地面の速度を上げます基地で有効です実験をすると本当に有用なものを見つけるかもしれません\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;温度^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   寒さや熱や放射線は通常のスターバウンドのものですが FUでは違う役割を演じます EPPパックに免疫作用は多くありません代わりに主にそれらから得られる ^cyan;レジスタンス ^reset; を使っています要素の抵抗が高いほど抵抗は少なくなります (あるいは完全にブロックされます) 抵抗は積み上げられます\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;砂漠熱^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   砂漠は通常乾燥していて湿度は高くありませんそしてその熱はあなたの健康と食べ物をゆっくりと吸い上げます正午から日没まで最悪の状態になります夜は比較的無害で涼しいです地下は寒いです耐火性で砂漠に抵抗できます\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;ジャングルヒート^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   砂漠のように、ジャングルの熱は徐々にあなたの健康と食べ物を排水し、夜にはそれほど深刻ではありません砂漠の熱とは異なり、この効果に対抗するために物理的抵抗を取るでしょう。\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;放射線^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   放射線は準備されていない人にはかなり危険ですこの厄介な効果によって健康とエネルギーは急速に排出されます (あなたの最大健康/エネルギーは現在の量ではありません) もしあなたが 0最大健康に達すると警告なしに死ぬでしょうだから自分自身に目を光らせてくださいより速く飢えさせましょう風はあなたのために事態を悪化させます抵抗は放射性抵抗を必要とします\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow; 硫黄 ^reset; 。\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   硫黄の効果は悪質で、すぐに装甲を食べて、健康被害を及ぼす可能性があります。さらに悪いことに、硫黄の世界では、この効果に抵抗する嵐があります。この効果に抵抗するには、さらに危険な酸性雨と苛性酸のプール! ^orange;物理抵抗^reset; あるいは ^orange;酸性免疫^reset; 効果\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;プロト毒^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   この悪影響はProto 世界にとって脅威です。それはあなたの最大限の健康をゆっくりと吸い上げ、** 最終的にあなたを殺します。さらに、それはあなたの批評を軽減し、時間の経過とともに損害を与えるでしょう。あなたの研究室のステーションのさまざまなギアから^orange;プロト毒素保護^reset; 、^orange; 毒抵抗^reset; 。\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;狂気^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   精神状態が一定に悪化すると 狂気は持続的な期間をかけて 保護をしのぐ力を奪うのです さらに ダニあたりのダメージも軽度です 脳が混乱して幻覚を起こし より速く飢えます 増強と装甲が存在すれば この厄介な効果と戦うことができます あるいは まともな抵抗力があるかもしれません ^orange;影と宇宙の両方^reset; 大丈夫だよ\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;プレッシャー^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   おそらくすべてのステータス効果の最も致命的なものは、極端な圧力^red;は間違いなく数秒であなたを殺します^reset;あなたは保護を持っていない場合. ありがたいことに、それはいくつかの場所で(主にガスボールバイオームに)発見されます. ^orange;保護スーツなしでこの環境効果を危険にさらさないでください ^reset; ... あなたは*死ぬでしょう*。\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;毒^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   かなり自己説明的です 毒を被りたくないかもしれませんが 他の人よりも悪いものもあります 基本的な毒や水銀毒(特に嫌な毒) 汚染された水 食中毒や 暗い水毒もあります ^orange;毒免疫または抵抗^reset; 特定の危険を避けるための手口となります 潜在的な毒はより大量の抵抗を必要とします\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;膿^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   この液体は絶対に反発力があり体に何かが入ったとしてもレッチや吐き気を生じるのです逆行するには何らかの種類の ^orange;身体的保護^reset; が必要ですこの酸性胆汁は友達ではありません摂取を控えることをお勧めします\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;Black Tar^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   ブラックタールはあなたを遅くします。 ^red;たくさん^reset; ジャンプを適度な高さにするのは ほぼ不可能です 妨害しますが 直接損傷は起こしません 様々な装甲でブロックしたり 生産したりできます\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;ガス^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   ガスは両方ともポジティブです。 3またはマイナス(カリガス、水素など)に浸かる. 気体の遮断は一般的に簡単です。^orange;気体から保護するものを身に着ける^reset;ただし、より専門的なものもある。 ^orange;カルシウムガスは影抵抗を必要とする^reset; そして ^orange;毒ガスは高耐毒性非機能性です。^reset;.\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;オーガニックスープ^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   オーガニックスープは、あなたの健康増進と飢餓の影響をなくし(そしてあなたをいっぱいにさえします!)、できるときにお風呂に入ります!\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;BioDoze^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   この液体はあなたに固執し病気になり運動や生存の機会に影響を与えます保護を身に着けておくことをお勧めしますプロトワールドや他のいくつかのバイオームで最も一般的です ^orange; ブロックされるか毒抵抗や免疫力によって緩和される可能性があります ^reset; 。\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;液体窒素^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   ちょっと寒いから、楽しい時間に足を踏み入れるのって、ちょっとくだらない話かもしれないけど、でも、十分な^orange;氷レジスタンス^reset;を身に着けているだけで楽しいイベントにできる。\n\n\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n   ^yellow;Darkness^reset;\n   ^#555555; ----------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n   ビジョンセンターに浸透し周りの世界を光のない空間に変えることができる暗闇がありますこれらの影響に注意してくださいありがたいことにすでに暗い場所では最も一般的なことです\n\n\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n\n   宇宙の探索には他にも多くの影響が及ぶことに注意してくださいそれら全てに抵抗できるわけではなく驚くことに抵抗されることもあります気を付けて安全に保てばいいのです\n\n^blue; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^yellow; ウィキの亀裂\n^blue; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\nWikiのヘルプが必要な場合は、 ^cyan; 公式wiki ^reset; _ をここで使用します。\n^green;frackinUniverse.miraheze.org ^reset;\n\n^red; ^reset; は Fandom wiki を使用しないでください。 恐ろしく時代遅れです。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "title",
        "source": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Environments",
        "normalizedSource": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Environments",
        "translation": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : 環境"
      }
    ],
    "ffguide6": [
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Use the Enhanced Codex Viewer to read this. Access it in your Tricorder.",
        "normalizedSource": "Use the Enhanced Codex Viewer to read this. Access it in your Tricorder.",
        "translation": "この本は、トライコーダーから開ける拡張コーデックスで読めます。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "description",
        "source": "Armor Up and Nom",
        "normalizedSource": "Armor Up and Nom",
        "translation": "食事と防具で冒険に備えよう"
      },
      {
        "field": "longContentPages",
        "source": "FrackinUniverse adds a large amount of armors (and foods) and enhances some older ones, allowing for a greater variety of playstyles. These can be very useful through gameplay and provide exceptionally useful benefits!\n\n^yellow;Set Bonus Inheritance^reset;: As an important note, armors that are used to craft other armors can still be used to complete armor set bonuses for sets that were used in the crafting chain, so partially upgrading your set is still viable.\n\n^orange;Stats^reset; : Vanilla players may notice there are more than they are used to, and even the ones they are used to have different ranges. FU presents a wider variety of armor classes to spice up your play, and does the same with food.\n\nIf you are more interested in damage, pick up Power Armor or Hyper Power Armor to trade defensive stats for offensive ones. Alternatively, pick up Tank or Hyper Tank sets to outlast your enemy. They come in melee OR ranged! Fighting not quite your thing? Pick up an Exploration oriented set, and be at home in your environment! You're guaranteed to locate a set that suits your playstyle somewhere out there!\n\n^orange;Resistances^reset; : Many armors in FU come with inherent resistances. Many biome weather effects will simply stop affecting you once you hit an appropriate amount, and various enemy attacks will do less damage. Nifty, right? It gets better; upgrade your armor, and those resistances will increase!\n\n^orange;Bonuses^reset; : Most are increases to your stats, plenty are conditional.\nAny that say ^green;+value^reset; are typically additive increases. It can be a little confusing, however. As example: if it gives +^green;3^reset;% Crit Chance it increases your crit chance by a flat 3%, but if it says +^green;3^reset;% Energy Regen, that's 3% of your base. The easiest way to remember is to ask yourself...does it have a base of 0? If so, it likely is like Crit Chance! If a bonus says x^green;1.3^reset;, or ^green;More^reset;, that's a multiplier on the value you currently have. Have 1000% Damage somehow? 100% More (or 2x) would make it 2000%! Small note: Regen is usually per second.\n\nOf course, some bonuses have hidden components we couldn't easily include, for tooltip space.\n Additionally, there are some other phrase uses to note. If a set bonus states that it grants immunity to ^green;ALL^reset; of a related effect, that typically means all biome weather ^orange;as well as^reset; specific status effects related to that element. For heat, that includes burning and even lava! For radiation, that includes rad-burn.\nAs a small side-note, some terms or symbols are used loosely. If you see a bonus with x/y, that means the bonuses are different based on how their conditions are met. For weapons, this means how many of that type. If you see something like (Machine) Pistols, that means the bonus applies to Machine Pistols OR Pistols. This is typically done for tooltip space.\n\n^cyan;Mining Sets^reset; :\n Mining laser sets grant a lot more mining laser damage...but that bonus is reduced significantly if you are pairing them with something else. Using a mining laser with a pistol, as example: 2x Mining Laser Damage becomes 1.25x.\n^orange;Colors^reset;: Colors are important in identifying and understanding bonuses. To start with, set bonuses are identified by a ^yellow;^reset;, while a ^green;^reset; is only visible in crafting interfaces to display resistances. If a bonus stat is ^green;GREEN^reset;, that means it is a good thing. ^red;RED^reset; means it is a bad thing. ^cyan;Cyan^reset; is for bonuses that are binary. They typically do not stack with similar effects. This will be especially apparent with various foods...so choose carefully. It is worth noticing that there is ONE exception to the rules regarding colors: Glow. If you see Glow in a color, that is usually the color of the glow effect.\n\n^orange;Special Bonuses^reset; : Some sets have special bonuses that don't really display much information due to lack of space, an unfortunate limitation of the game. Here, some bonuses will be explained.\n\n^cyan;Adaptive Armor^reset;: Multiplies the wearer's total defense based on current health percentage, scaling between the left value at 20% health and the right value at 100% health.\n\n^cyan;Auto-Medic^reset;: More complicated than ordinary regeneration, this effect will restore more health per second at the cost of an equal percentage of energy. It will also decrease energy regen and increase energy regen lock-out multiplicatively at 2x the heal percent.\n\n^cyan;Thorns^reset;: a nova of thorns when hit, ^cyan;Fire Burst^reset; makes a nova of fire instead.\n\n^cyan;Summons Minions^reset;: summons short-lived allies to fight alongside you or distract enemies. These minions scale based on the lowest armor's tier, so upgrading it is essential! Upgrade ALL of the pieces.\n\n^cyan;Life/Energy Shell^reset;: Gain damage absorption (shell) which scales based on a resource (health, energy) to protect your health, comes with a matching overhead bar to indicate its state. Regenerates quickly if you haven't taken damage recently. ^cyan;Shell Immunities^reset; are granted only while the shell holds. The numbers on the effect's label indicate the conversion rate relative to the resource's stats. In order: capacity, regeneration rate, and the delay upon taking damage before it begins regenerating.\n\n^cyan;Life Shell^reset; specific: Regeneration rate is a direct percentage of health per second, lockout is in specified seconds.\n\n^cyan;Energy Shell^reset; specific: Regeneration rate is a percentage of the energy regeneration stat, base vanilla regeneration is 58.5% per second. Special note due to balance: Minimum lockout time of 0.5 seconds, and a maximum regen rate of 50% per second.\n\n^cyan;Gravity Normalization^reset;: Personal gravity too low? Up it goes. Too high? Down instead. Exception: Zero-gravity.\n\n^cyan;Vital Power^reset; and ^cyan;Juggernaut^reset;: these effects are set bonus exclusive, and quite powerful; they grant one stat based on a percent of another. Vital power grants power as life, Juggernaut grants life as power.\n\n^cyan;Undying Resolve^reset;: increases Protection as your life gets lower, up to the stated amount, while ^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset; grants HP Regen instead. If a set grants either, it will grant ^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset; to your pet.\n\n^cyan;Dark Commander^reset;/^cyan;Beast Master^reset;: Increases Damage, Protection, HP and Speed of your pets (both) and crew (Dark Commander) by the listed percent, increases their jump ability by half of that, and regenerates HP at a sixth of that amount per second.\n\n^cyan;Capturenaut^reset;: Increases pet count by 1, plus an additional 1 per 2 tiers (up to +2) of the lowest equipped set piece. Grants an additional +1 if using alongside the back item. This means a fully upgraded set will allow up to 5 additional pets!\n\n^red;Wretchel Toxicity^reset;: Ingesting Wretchel reduces core stats and healing received, and drains health over time. These effects increase in severity the more you consume in a short time frame, as well as while your health is critically low. It will ^red;KILL^reset; you, if you are careless.\n\n^cyan;Charisma^reset;: Your ability to bargain with Traders at space stations. The higher your charisma, the better the deal (and fatter your bank balance!)\n\n\n\n^cyan;Pet/Crew Stat Inheritance^reset;:\nOverall scaling is as follows: HP, directly from your character, rather than just equipped armor. Protection: applied as a multiplier to HP via a specific formula. Damage: directly from character sheet. Health Regen: Inherits as a flat amount, except in special cases (^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset;, effects not covered by FU, etc.). If you have 100 health and 10% HP Regen, it will grant your pet 10 HP per second. If a stat isn't here, a pet most likely does not inherit it.\n^yellow;Special notes^reset;: Be mindful when taking powerful buffs like ^cyan;Glass Cannon^reset;, as it will reduce their health noticeably.\n",
        "normalizedSource": "FrackinUniverse adds a large amount of armors (and foods) and enhances some older ones, allowing for a greater variety of playstyles. These can be very useful through gameplay and provide exceptionally useful benefits! ^yellow;Set Bonus Inheritance^reset;: As an important note, armors that are used to craft other armors can still be used to complete armor set bonuses for sets that were used in the crafting chain, so partially upgrading your set is still viable. ^orange;Stats^reset; : Vanilla players may notice there are more than they are used to, and even the ones they are used to have different ranges. FU presents a wider variety of armor classes to spice up your play, and does the same with food. If you are more interested in damage, pick up Power Armor or Hyper Power Armor to trade defensive stats for offensive ones. Alternatively, pick up Tank or Hyper Tank sets to outlast your enemy. They come in melee OR ranged! Fighting not quite your thing? Pick up an Exploration oriented set, and be at home in your environment! You're guaranteed to locate a set that suits your playstyle somewhere out there! ^orange;Resistances^reset; : Many armors in FU come with inherent resistances. Many biome weather effects will simply stop affecting you once you hit an appropriate amount, and various enemy attacks will do less damage. Nifty, right? It gets better; upgrade your armor, and those resistances will increase! ^orange;Bonuses^reset; : Most are increases to your stats, plenty are conditional. Any that say ^green;+value^reset; are typically additive increases. It can be a little confusing, however. As example: if it gives +^green;3^reset;% Crit Chance it increases your crit chance by a flat 3%, but if it says +^green;3^reset;% Energy Regen, that's 3% of your base. The easiest way to remember is to ask yourself...does it have a base of 0? If so, it likely is like Crit Chance! If a bonus says x^green;1.3^reset;, or ^green;More^reset;, that's a multiplier on the value you currently have. Have 1000% Damage somehow? 100% More (or 2x) would make it 2000%! Small note: Regen is usually per second. Of course, some bonuses have hidden components we couldn't easily include, for tooltip space. Additionally, there are some other phrase uses to note. If a set bonus states that it grants immunity to ^green;ALL^reset; of a related effect, that typically means all biome weather ^orange;as well as^reset; specific status effects related to that element. For heat, that includes burning and even lava! For radiation, that includes rad-burn. As a small side-note, some terms or symbols are used loosely. If you see a bonus with x/y, that means the bonuses are different based on how their conditions are met. For weapons, this means how many of that type. If you see something like (Machine) Pistols, that means the bonus applies to Machine Pistols OR Pistols. This is typically done for tooltip space. ^cyan;Mining Sets^reset; : Mining laser sets grant a lot more mining laser damage...but that bonus is reduced significantly if you are pairing them with something else. Using a mining laser with a pistol, as example: 2x Mining Laser Damage becomes 1.25x. ^orange;Colors^reset;: Colors are important in identifying and understanding bonuses. To start with, set bonuses are identified by a ^yellow;^reset;, while a ^green;^reset; is only visible in crafting interfaces to display resistances. If a bonus stat is ^green;GREEN^reset;, that means it is a good thing. ^red;RED^reset; means it is a bad thing. ^cyan;Cyan^reset; is for bonuses that are binary. They typically do not stack with similar effects. This will be especially apparent with various foods...so choose carefully. It is worth noticing that there is ONE exception to the rules regarding colors: Glow. If you see Glow in a color, that is usually the color of the glow effect. ^orange;Special Bonuses^reset; : Some sets have special bonuses that don't really display much information due to lack of space, an unfortunate limitation of the game. Here, some bonuses will be explained. ^cyan;Adaptive Armor^reset;: Multiplies the wearer's total defense based on current health percentage, scaling between the left value at 20% health and the right value at 100% health. ^cyan;Auto-Medic^reset;: More complicated than ordinary regeneration, this effect will restore more health per second at the cost of an equal percentage of energy. It will also decrease energy regen and increase energy regen lock-out multiplicatively at 2x the heal percent. ^cyan;Thorns^reset;: a nova of thorns when hit, ^cyan;Fire Burst^reset; makes a nova of fire instead. ^cyan;Summons Minions^reset;: summons short-lived allies to fight alongside you or distract enemies. These minions scale based on the lowest armor's tier, so upgrading it is essential! Upgrade ALL of the pieces. ^cyan;Life/Energy Shell^reset;: Gain damage absorption (shell) which scales based on a resource (health, energy) to protect your health, comes with a matching overhead bar to indicate its state. Regenerates quickly if you haven't taken damage recently. ^cyan;Shell Immunities^reset; are granted only while the shell holds. The numbers on the effect's label indicate the conversion rate relative to the resource's stats. In order: capacity, regeneration rate, and the delay upon taking damage before it begins regenerating. ^cyan;Life Shell^reset; specific: Regeneration rate is a direct percentage of health per second, lockout is in specified seconds. ^cyan;Energy Shell^reset; specific: Regeneration rate is a percentage of the energy regeneration stat, base vanilla regeneration is 58.5% per second. Special note due to balance: Minimum lockout time of 0.5 seconds, and a maximum regen rate of 50% per second. ^cyan;Gravity Normalization^reset;: Personal gravity too low? Up it goes. Too high? Down instead. Exception: Zero-gravity. ^cyan;Vital Power^reset; and ^cyan;Juggernaut^reset;: these effects are set bonus exclusive, and quite powerful; they grant one stat based on a percent of another. Vital power grants power as life, Juggernaut grants life as power. ^cyan;Undying Resolve^reset;: increases Protection as your life gets lower, up to the stated amount, while ^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset; grants HP Regen instead. If a set grants either, it will grant ^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset; to your pet. ^cyan;Dark Commander^reset;/^cyan;Beast Master^reset;: Increases Damage, Protection, HP and Speed of your pets (both) and crew (Dark Commander) by the listed percent, increases their jump ability by half of that, and regenerates HP at a sixth of that amount per second. ^cyan;Capturenaut^reset;: Increases pet count by 1, plus an additional 1 per 2 tiers (up to +2) of the lowest equipped set piece. Grants an additional +1 if using alongside the back item. This means a fully upgraded set will allow up to 5 additional pets! ^red;Wretchel Toxicity^reset;: Ingesting Wretchel reduces core stats and healing received, and drains health over time. These effects increase in severity the more you consume in a short time frame, as well as while your health is critically low. It will ^red;KILL^reset; you, if you are careless. ^cyan;Charisma^reset;: Your ability to bargain with Traders at space stations. The higher your charisma, the better the deal (and fatter your bank balance!) ^cyan;Pet/Crew Stat Inheritance^reset;: Overall scaling is as follows: HP, directly from your character, rather than just equipped armor. Protection: applied as a multiplier to HP via a specific formula. Damage: directly from character sheet. Health Regen: Inherits as a flat amount, except in special cases (^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset;, effects not covered by FU, etc.). If you have 100 health and 10% HP Regen, it will grant your pet 10 HP per second. If a stat isn't here, a pet most likely does not inherit it. ^yellow;Special notes^reset;: Be mindful when taking powerful buffs like ^cyan;Glass Cannon^reset;, as it will reduce their health noticeably.",
        "translation": "FrackinUniverseは、大量の装甲(および食品)を追加し、いくつかの古いものを強化し、より多様なプレイスタイルを可能にします。 これらは、ゲームプレイを通じて非常に有用であり、非常に有用な利益をもたらすことができます!\n\n^yellow;セットボーナスの継承 ^reset;:重要な注意として、他の装甲を作製するために使用される装甲は、製造チェーンで使用されたセットの装甲セットボーナスを完了するためにまだ使用できます。\n\n^orange;能力値 ^reset;:バニラプレイヤーは、彼らが慣れ親しんだものよりも多くがあることに気づくかもしれません。 FUは、あなたの遊びをスパイスアップするための装甲クラスの広い範囲を提供し、食品で同じことを行います。\n\nより被害に興味がある場合は、Power 防具またはHyper Power 防具を拾って、攻撃的なものに防御統計を交換してください。 または、タンクまたはハイパータンクをピックアップして敵を長持ちさせます。 彼らはメリーOR範囲で来ます! 戦いはあなたのものではない? 探索指向のセットを拾って、あなたの環境の中で家にいる! どこかでプレイスタイルに合ったセットを見つけることができます!\n\n^orange;レジスタンス^reset;:FUの多くの装甲には固有の抵抗があります。 多くのバイオームの気象効果は、適切な量に達したら、あなたに影響しなくなり、さまざまな敵の攻撃はより少ない被害を与えます。 良いでしょう? 装甲をアップグレードすると、それらの抵抗が増加します!\n\n^orange;ボーナス^reset;:ほとんどが統計に増加し、多くは条件付きです。\n^green;+value ^reset; と表記するものは、一般に付加的な増加である。 でも、やや混乱することもある。 例えば:もしそれが +^green;3^reset;% クリティカル チャンスを平らにすることで、クリトリスチャンスを増加させます。 3%でも もしそうなら +^green;3^reset;% エネルギー・レーゲンは 3% 基地の 覚えておくべき最も簡単な方法は、自分自身に問いかけることです... 0 のベースがありますか? もしそうなら、それはおそらくクリティカル率のようなものです! ボーナスが x^green;1.3^reset;, または ^green;More ^reset; と表示されている場合、それは現在持っている値の乗数です。 1000% 何らかの損傷がありますか? 100% 以上 (または 2x) すると 2000% になります! 小さなメモ:レーゲンは通常一秒あたりです。\n\nもちろん、いくつかのボーナスには、簡単には入れられない隠れたコンポーネントがあります。\n 他にも、いくつかのフレーズで注意しなければならないことがある。もしセットボーナスが、関連する効果の^green;ALL^reset;に対して免疫を与えると述べれば、それは典型的には、すべての生物の天気^orange;と、その要素に関連する^reset;の特定のステータス効果を意味する。熱の場合、燃焼と溶岩でさえ含まれる!放射線の場合、ラッドバーンを含む。\n小さなサイドノートとして、いくつかの用語やシンボルはゆるく使用されます。 x/yでボーナスを見た場合、それはボーナスが条件がどのように満たされているかに基づいて異なることを意味します。 武器の場合は、その種類の数を意味します。 マシンピストル(Machine ピストル)のようなものが表示される場合、それはマシンピストルまたはピストルにボーナスが適用されることを意味します。 これは、通常、ツールチップスペースに対して行われる。\n\n^cyan;マイニング設定 ^reset;:\n 採掘レーザー セットはもっと多くの 採掘レーザー ダメージ...しかし、何か他のものとペアリングしている場合、そのボーナスは大幅に減少します。 採掘レーザー 例えば ピストルを使って 2十 採掘レーザー 被害は 1.25Xだ\n^orange; Colors ^reset; : ボーナスの識別と理解には色が重要です。 最初に、設定されたボーナスは ^yellow;^reset; によって識別され、 ^green;^reset; は抵抗を表示するためのインタフェースを作成する場合にのみ表示されます。 ボーナスステータスが ^green;GREEN ^reset; であれば、それは良いことです。 ^red;RED^reset;は悪いことを意味します。 ^cyan;Cyan^reset;はバイナリーのボーナスです。 通常は同様の効果を伴わない。 これは、さまざまな食べ物で特に明らかになります...ので、慎重に選択してください。 色に関するルールには、一つの例外があることに注意してください。 あなたが色でグローを見るならば、それは通常グロー効果の色です。\n\n^orange;特別ボーナス^reset;:スペース不足、ゲームの残念な制限のために、いくつかのセットには、実際には多くの情報を表示しない特別なボーナスがあります。 ここでは、いくつかのボーナスを説明します。\n\n^cyan;アダプティブアーマー^reset;:現在の健康率に基づいて着用者の総防御を倍増し、左の値の間にスケーリングします。 20% 健康と適切な価値を 100% 健康\n\n^cyan;Auto-Medic ^reset;:通常の再生よりも複雑で、この効果はエネルギーの同等の割合のコストで一秒あたりの健康を回復します。 また、2xのヒーリングパーセントでエネルギー再生を減少させ、エネルギー再生ロックアウトを倍増させます。\n\n^cyan;竜^reset;突っ込んだときのノバを ^cyan;火のバースト^reset; 代わりに火のノバを作るのです\n\n^cyan; ミニオンズ^reset; : 短命の同盟者を呼び出して、あなたと一緒に戦ったり、敵を邪魔したりします。 これらのミニオンは最低の装甲ティアに基づいてスケールするので、アップグレードが不可欠です! すべてのピースをアップグレードします。\n\n^cyan;Life / エネルギー Shell ^reset;:健康を守るための資源(健康、エネルギー)に基づいてスケールする損傷吸収(シェル)を獲得します。 最近損傷を受けていない場合はすぐに再生します。 ^cyan;シェル免疫^reset;はシェルを保持する間のみ付与されます。 エフェクトのラベルの数字は、リソースの統計に対する変換率を示しています。 順序:容量、再生率、およびそれが再生を開始する前に損傷を受ける際の遅延。\n\n^cyan;Life Shell ^reset;specific:再生率は一秒あたりの健康率の直接的な割合であり、ロックアウトは指定された秒数です。\n\n^cyan; エネルギー Shell ^reset;specific:再生率はエネルギー再生統計のパーセンテージであり、ベースバニラ再生は58.5%per secondである。 バランスによる特別な注意: 0.5秒の最小ロックアウト時間、および 50%秒あたりの最大再生率。\n\n^cyan;重力正規化^reset;:個人の重力が低すぎる? 上に行く。 高すぎる? 代わりにダウン。 例外: ゼロ重力。\n\n^cyan; Vital Power ^reset;と^cyan;ジャガーノート ^reset;:これらの効果は、ボーナスの排他的で非常に強力に設定されています。 生命力は生命力、ジャガーノートは生命力となる。\n\n^cyan;未解決の解決^reset;: 保護を増加します。あなたの人生が下がるにつれて、指定された量まで保護します。 ^cyan;不死の解決^reset; 代わりに体力再生を付与する。 セットが許可された場合、それはあなたのペットに^cyan;ImmortalResolve^reset;を付与します。\n\n^cyan;ダークコマンド ^reset;/^cyan;ビーストマスター ^reset;: ペット(両方とも)と乗組員(両方ともダークコマンド)の損傷、保護、速度をリストアップし、その半分ずつジャンプ能力を高め、その量の六分の一秒でHPを再生します。\n\n^cyan;捕獲探検家^reset;: ペットの数を増やす。 1プラス追加 1 パー 2 階層(最大) +2最低装備セット片の)。 バックアイテムと一緒に使用する場合は、追加 +1 を付与します。 つまり、完全にアップグレードされたセットでは、5追加ペットを許可します!\n\n^red; レッチェル Toxicity ^reset;: レッチェルを摂取すると、コアステータスとヒーリングが減少し、時間の経過とともに健康が低下します。 これらの効果は、短時間で消費するほど重大度が増加し、健康状態は極めて低い。 不注意であれば ^red;KILL^reset; になります。\n\n^cyan;カリスマ ^reset; : 宇宙ステーションでトレーダーと交渉するあなたの能力。 カリスマ性が高いほど、取引は良くなります(そして、銀行残高を肥大化させます!\n\n\n\n^cyan;Pet/CrewStat 継承 ^reset;:\n全体的なスケーリングは次のとおりだ: HPは、装備された装甲機ではなく、あなたのキャラクターから直接。 保護:特定の式を介してHPに乗算器として適用されます。 損傷: キャラクターシートから直接。 ヘルスレーゲン: 特殊な場合(^cyan;Immortal Resolve ^reset;、FUでカバーされていない効果など)を除いて、平坦な量として継承します。 100健康と10%体力再生があれば、あなたのペット10HPを毎秒与えます。 ステータスがここにない場合、ペットはおそらくそれを継承しません。\n^yellow;特別なメモ ^reset; : ^cyan; Glass Cannon ^reset; のような強力なバフを服用するときは、健康を著しく低下させるので、注意してください。\n",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "title",
        "source": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Food and Armor",
        "normalizedSource": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Food and Armor",
        "translation": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : 食料と防具"
      }
    ],
    "ffguidebattle": [
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "View in your Tricorder Codex tab in the 'FU' section.",
        "normalizedSource": "View in your Tricorder Codex tab in the 'FU' section.",
        "translation": "トライコーダーのコーデックスを開き、「FU」のカテゴリから読んでください。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "description",
        "source": "Changes to Weapons and Combat in FU.",
        "normalizedSource": "Changes to Weapons and Combat in FU.",
        "translation": "FUでの武器と戦闘の変更点。"
      },
      {
        "field": "longContentPages",
        "source": "\n^orange;Monster Resistances^reset;\n------------------------\nSome monsters resist, or are completely immune to, certain types of damage.\n\nTo combat these threats you are going to need weapons of ^green;different elemental types^reset; at any given moment. Try to use ^green;at least 2 to 3^reset; of the more than 8 available types so you are ready for any challenge.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\n\n^orange;Weapons and Combat^reset;\n----------------------\nRanged and Melee weapons behave a little differently in FrackinUniverse. The most important changes are listed in this codex.\n\n\n^orange;Crit Chance and Crit Damage^reset;\n---------------------------\nWeapon item tooltips have new icons. The two on the left represent Critical Chance bonus and Critical Damage bonus.\n\n\n^orange;Ammo and Reload Speed^reset;\n---------------------------\nAmmo and Reload speed are represented by the right-side icons.\n\nItems with a '--' representing a value in any of the above stats means it does not apply to them. This is the case with modded weapons, or energy-only (non-ammo) guns, primarily.\n\n\n^orange;Mastery^reset;\n---------------\n\nOccasionally, you'll see Mastery traits applied to equippable gear, or in Racial Bonuses. These imply that you have greater capability in a particular weapon type. Generally speaking, ^yellow;Masteries^reset; simply ^cyan;improve already existing weapon benefits^reset; including Tech bonuses. In an upcoming topic below, you'll see various weapons listed along with the various capabilities each carries with it. These listed benefits will all be improved through ^yellow;Mastery^reset;.\n\nAn example: When wielded individually a Rapier will provide an increase to Crit Chance when timing strikes carefully (to a max of 5). The amount of the bonus applied is higher by the amount listed in your ^yellow;Mastery^reset; stat. At 100% this would mean a maximum Crit Chance bonus of +10.\n\nThe amount of benefit gained can vary from weapon to weapon. In some cases you will get a modifier based directly on your ^yellow;Mastery^reset; trait, while others will reduce that value by half, quarter, eigth or other such fractions.\n\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\n\n^green;Ranged^reset;\n----------------------------------\n\n^orange;Ammo-Based Weapons^reset;\n------------------\nSome weapons now use ammunition. Don't worry, you won't need to carry resources around with you to refill them. These weapons simply use much, much less energy in exchange for the mobility boost provided by having extra energy! Note that their alt fires will always require energy, regardless of their primary fire.\n\nYou can reload these weapons manually by holding the SHIFT key and clicking the mouse button. Emptying the magazine through shooting will also automatically engage the reload.\n\n^orange;Ammo Mastery^reset;\n------------------\nThis Mastery is quite straightforward: your rating in Ammo Mastery directly correlates to the % reduced from your Reload Time as well as the $ of ammo gained per magazine.\n\n^orange;Pistol^reset;\n------------------\nWith mastery applied, Pistols gain increased Damage, reduced reload time and a higher critical strike chance.\n\n^orange;Machine Pistol^reset;\n------------------\nWith mastery applied, Machine Pistols gain increased Damage, reduced reload time and a higher critical strike chance.\n\n^orange;Arm Cannon^reset;\n------------------\nWith mastery applied, Arm Cannons provide varied benefits based on how they are wielded. Power, Crit Chance, Crit Damage and Protection are all impacted. When using just arm cannons (dual or single) you get less protection benefits but a much higher critical chance. With an armcannon and shield you gain a much better protection bonus in exchange for reduced power.\n\n^orange;Assault Rifle^reset;\n------------------\nAssault rifles benefit from mastery by increasing overall damage output while increasing magazine size and critical damage.\n\n^orange;Sniper Rifle^reset;\n------------------\nWith a mastery in Sniper rifles you gain magazine size and critical chance. This stacks with the usual crit benefits of sniper rifles and allows for a very high crit chance with charge-ups!\n\n^orange;Grenade Launcher^reset;\n----------------------\nWhen wielding grenade launchers with mastery expect to gain increased damage and magazine size while also benefiting from reduced reload time.\n\n^orange;Rocket Launcher^reset;\n----------------------\nObliterating the enemy is easy with mastery in rockets! You'll do a lot more damage, reload faster and have increased magazine size.\n\n^orange;Shotgun^reset;\n----------------------\nThese dangerous weapons, when mastered, profice exceptional crit chance and power along with increased magazine size and reduced reload time.\n\n^orange;Magnorb^reset;\n----------------------\nThese unusual weapons provide increased damage, crit chance, crit damage and energy to masters that wield them.\n\n^orange;Bow^reset;\n----------------------\nBows have a large number of benefits masters can take advantage of. Crit damage and crit chance increase, along with damage. In addition, they can fire bows faster and shoot arrows farther while consuming less energy!\n\n^orange;Whip^reset;\n----------------------\nWhip users get a sizeable increase in crit chance and crit damage while also increasing damage output with this mastered weapon.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^green;Melee^reset;\n\n^orange;Combos^reset;\n---------------\nEach strike of a combo, whether or not it hits a target, consumes 1% of your energy. If your energy is expended, you will no longer be able to combo and will instead perform frenzied normal attacks.\nBe warned, tactics involving stun-locking enemies are no longer as viable.\n\nMany weapons with combos provide additional bonuses when striking with these combos.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Shield Bash^reset;\n---------------\nBlocking with shields on enemies has a chance to Shield Bash. Certain gear can increase the Shield Bash chances.\n\nShield Bash can damage foes, and send them reeling backwards. When Perfect Blocking, there is a 50% chance to Stun foes that are successfully bashed. When not perfect blocking, be wary: There is a chance -you- will get stunned on a badly timed block.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Hammer^reset;\n---------------\nThe longer you hold the charge of this melee weapon type, the higher your Critical and Stun chance get (to a maximum of ^green;100^reset;%).\n\nA hammer charged above ^green;75^reset;% will inflict a massive bonus eruption capable of stunning and tossing foes around.\n\nOver-Charging the hammer past ^green;100^reset;% will automatically cancel the bonus.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Great Axe^reset;\n---------------\nThe longer you hold the charge of this melee weapon type, the higher your Critical Chance and Critical Damage get (to a maximum of ^green;100^reset;%).\n\nA greataxe charged above ^green;75^reset;% will inflict a massive bonus eruption capable of bleeding and tossing foes around.\n\nOver-Charging the greataxe past ^green;100^reset;% will automatically cancel the bonus.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Axe^reset;\n---------------\nEach consecutive kill made with an axe increases your maximum damage by +^green;1^reset;%, to a maximum of ^green;50^reset;%.\n\nIf your health is reduced below ^red;20^reset;%, this bonus is cancelled.\n\nEach consecutive hit in a row with an axe increases Crit Chance by +^green;3^reset;% (to a maximum of ^green;15^reset;%)\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Dagger^reset;\n---------------\nConsecutive rapid kills temporarily increase damage\n\n+^green;25^reset;% Dodge Tech Efficiency\n\nCombo Strikes increase Protection and Crit Chance with each strike. The protection bonus is greatest on First Strike, and reduces each hit thereafter.\n\n^cyan;Dual-Wield (Melee):^reset; +^green;5^reset;% Movement Speed\n\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Shortsword^reset;\n---------------\n+1 Combo strike (was 2, now 3)\n\nEach combo hit increases your Crit Damage amount\n\n+^green;1^reset;% Crit Chance per Combo Strike\n\nFirst Combo strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage. Second hit does +^green;25^reset;% Crit Damage.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Broadsword^reset;\n---------------\nKills made in rapid succession increase defense for a short time\n\n+^green;1^reset;% Crit Chance per Combo Strike\n\nFirst Combo strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage. Second hit does +^green;25^reset;% Crit Damage.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Scythe^reset;\n---------------\n+^green;1^reset;% Crit Chance per Combo Strike\n\nFirst Combo strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage. Second hit does +^green;25^reset;% Crit Damage.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Longsword^reset;\n---------------\n3rd Combo Strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage\n\n^cyan;Single Longsword^reset;: -^green;30^reset;% Combo Cooldown\n\n^cyan;Longsword + Shield (Dual Wield)^reset;: +^green;4^reset;% Shield Bash, +^green;1^reset; Shield Bash Push Distance, +^green;15^reset;% Healing Tech Efficiency, +^green;25^reset;% Defense Tech Efficiency\n\n^cyan;Longsword + Any Weapon (Dual Wield)^reset;: Defense x^red;0.8^reset;, +^green;5^reset;% Movement Speed\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Rapier^reset;\n---------------\nWhen wielding a rapier, the longer you wait between swings the higher your critical strike chance becomes (to a maximum of 5). Attacking resets this bonus.\n\n^cyan;Single Rapier:^reset; +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage, +^green;35^reset;% Dodge and Dash Tech Efficiency\n\n^cyan;Rapier + Dagger (Dual Wield):^reset; x^green;1.12^reset; Protection, +^green;15^reset;% Dodge and Dash Tech Efficiency\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Shortspear^reset;\n---------------\n^cyan;Single Shortspear^reset;: +^green;30^reset;% Crit Damage\n\n^cyan;Shortspear + Shield^reset;: +^green;10^reset;% Shield Bash, +^green;2^reset; Shield Push Distance, Shield Regen x^green;1.2^reset;, +^green;50^reset;% Defense Tech Efficiency\n\n^cyan;Shortspear + Shortspear (Dual Wield)^reset;: Defense x^red;0.8^reset;, Bonus Crit Chance x^red;0.5^reset;\n\nShort Spears also count as Hunting weapons.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Spear^reset;\n---------------\nSpears are relatively straightforward. They gain crit chance, higher damage output and an increase in Dash Tech efficiency.\n\nSpears can be held out by holding the fire button to help keep enemies at bay. If using a Lance typed spear you also gain increased damage based on your movement speed while holding it out. It cannot be aimed during this.\n\nSpears also count as Hunting weapons.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Quarterstaff^reset;\n---------------\nEach hit with a combo increases your Defense.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Mace^reset;\n---------------\nCombo strikes increase Stun Chance by 2% per hit.\n\n^cyan;Single Mace^reset;: +^green;2^reset;% Stun Chance\n\n^cyan;Mace + Shield^reset;: +^green;3^reset;% Shield Bash, +^green;1^reset; Shield Push Distance, Defense x^green;1.1^reset;\n\n^cyan;Mace + Any Weapon (Dual Wield)^reset;: Bonus Crit Chance x^red;0.85^reset;, Bonus Stun Chance x^red;0.5^reset;, +^green;5^reset;% Movement Speed\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Katana^reset;\n---------------\nEach swing grants a Movement Speed bonus of ^green;1 + (combo step / 10)^reset;%\n\nCombo hits increase knockback resistance\n\n^cyan;Single Katana^reset;: +^green;15^reset;% Defense Tech Efficiency\n\n^cyan;Katana + Heavy Melee (Dual Wield)^reset;: Damage x^red;0.8^reset;, Defense x^red;0.9^reset;\n\n^cyan;Katana + Light Melee (Dual Wield)^reset;: Energy x^green;1.15^reset;, +^green;20^reset;% Crit Damage, +^green;25^reset;% Dodge and Dash Tech Efficiency\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Fists^reset;\n---------------\n\nNormal attacks consume ^red;3% energy^reset; per attack. Holding the button will activate this mode.\n\nCombos require timing: Holding or tapping the button too rapidly will use a normal attack.\n\nCombo strikes increase Crit Chance by ^green;1%^reset;, Stun chance by ^green;4%^reset; and Protection +1 per strike. When attacking, they use ^red;1%^reset; energy.\n\nAlt/Finisher is activated with ^cyan;[Shift + Click]^reset;. Outside of a combo this will use ^red;15%^reset; energy. When completing a combo as the last strike, it will consume none.\n\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Addendum^reset;\n---------------\nBonus Crit/Stun Chance refer to stats that are not inherent on the weapons themselves, such as from armor or consumables.\n",
        "normalizedSource": "^orange;Monster Resistances^reset; ------------------------ Some monsters resist, or are completely immune to, certain types of damage. To combat these threats you are going to need weapons of ^green;different elemental types^reset; at any given moment. Try to use ^green;at least 2 to 3^reset; of the more than 8 available types so you are ready for any challenge. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Weapons and Combat^reset; ---------------------- Ranged and Melee weapons behave a little differently in FrackinUniverse. The most important changes are listed in this codex. ^orange;Crit Chance and Crit Damage^reset; --------------------------- Weapon item tooltips have new icons. The two on the left represent Critical Chance bonus and Critical Damage bonus. ^orange;Ammo and Reload Speed^reset; --------------------------- Ammo and Reload speed are represented by the right-side icons. Items with a '--' representing a value in any of the above stats means it does not apply to them. This is the case with modded weapons, or energy-only (non-ammo) guns, primarily. ^orange;Mastery^reset; --------------- Occasionally, you'll see Mastery traits applied to equippable gear, or in Racial Bonuses. These imply that you have greater capability in a particular weapon type. Generally speaking, ^yellow;Masteries^reset; simply ^cyan;improve already existing weapon benefits^reset; including Tech bonuses. In an upcoming topic below, you'll see various weapons listed along with the various capabilities each carries with it. These listed benefits will all be improved through ^yellow;Mastery^reset;. An example: When wielded individually a Rapier will provide an increase to Crit Chance when timing strikes carefully (to a max of 5). The amount of the bonus applied is higher by the amount listed in your ^yellow;Mastery^reset; stat. At 100% this would mean a maximum Crit Chance bonus of +10. The amount of benefit gained can vary from weapon to weapon. In some cases you will get a modifier based directly on your ^yellow;Mastery^reset; trait, while others will reduce that value by half, quarter, eigth or other such fractions. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^green;Ranged^reset; ---------------------------------- ^orange;Ammo-Based Weapons^reset; ------------------ Some weapons now use ammunition. Don't worry, you won't need to carry resources around with you to refill them. These weapons simply use much, much less energy in exchange for the mobility boost provided by having extra energy! Note that their alt fires will always require energy, regardless of their primary fire. You can reload these weapons manually by holding the SHIFT key and clicking the mouse button. Emptying the magazine through shooting will also automatically engage the reload. ^orange;Ammo Mastery^reset; ------------------ This Mastery is quite straightforward: your rating in Ammo Mastery directly correlates to the % reduced from your Reload Time as well as the $ of ammo gained per magazine. ^orange;Pistol^reset; ------------------ With mastery applied, Pistols gain increased Damage, reduced reload time and a higher critical strike chance. ^orange;Machine Pistol^reset; ------------------ With mastery applied, Machine Pistols gain increased Damage, reduced reload time and a higher critical strike chance. ^orange;Arm Cannon^reset; ------------------ With mastery applied, Arm Cannons provide varied benefits based on how they are wielded. Power, Crit Chance, Crit Damage and Protection are all impacted. When using just arm cannons (dual or single) you get less protection benefits but a much higher critical chance. With an armcannon and shield you gain a much better protection bonus in exchange for reduced power. ^orange;Assault Rifle^reset; ------------------ Assault rifles benefit from mastery by increasing overall damage output while increasing magazine size and critical damage. ^orange;Sniper Rifle^reset; ------------------ With a mastery in Sniper rifles you gain magazine size and critical chance. This stacks with the usual crit benefits of sniper rifles and allows for a very high crit chance with charge-ups! ^orange;Grenade Launcher^reset; ---------------------- When wielding grenade launchers with mastery expect to gain increased damage and magazine size while also benefiting from reduced reload time. ^orange;Rocket Launcher^reset; ---------------------- Obliterating the enemy is easy with mastery in rockets! You'll do a lot more damage, reload faster and have increased magazine size. ^orange;Shotgun^reset; ---------------------- These dangerous weapons, when mastered, profice exceptional crit chance and power along with increased magazine size and reduced reload time. ^orange;Magnorb^reset; ---------------------- These unusual weapons provide increased damage, crit chance, crit damage and energy to masters that wield them. ^orange;Bow^reset; ---------------------- Bows have a large number of benefits masters can take advantage of. Crit damage and crit chance increase, along with damage. In addition, they can fire bows faster and shoot arrows farther while consuming less energy! ^orange;Whip^reset; ---------------------- Whip users get a sizeable increase in crit chance and crit damage while also increasing damage output with this mastered weapon. ^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^green;Melee^reset; ^orange;Combos^reset; --------------- Each strike of a combo, whether or not it hits a target, consumes 1% of your energy. If your energy is expended, you will no longer be able to combo and will instead perform frenzied normal attacks. Be warned, tactics involving stun-locking enemies are no longer as viable. Many weapons with combos provide additional bonuses when striking with these combos. ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Shield Bash^reset; --------------- Blocking with shields on enemies has a chance to Shield Bash. Certain gear can increase the Shield Bash chances. Shield Bash can damage foes, and send them reeling backwards. When Perfect Blocking, there is a 50% chance to Stun foes that are successfully bashed. When not perfect blocking, be wary: There is a chance -you- will get stunned on a badly timed block. ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Hammer^reset; --------------- The longer you hold the charge of this melee weapon type, the higher your Critical and Stun chance get (to a maximum of ^green;100^reset;%). A hammer charged above ^green;75^reset;% will inflict a massive bonus eruption capable of stunning and tossing foes around. Over-Charging the hammer past ^green;100^reset;% will automatically cancel the bonus. ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Great Axe^reset; --------------- The longer you hold the charge of this melee weapon type, the higher your Critical Chance and Critical Damage get (to a maximum of ^green;100^reset;%). A greataxe charged above ^green;75^reset;% will inflict a massive bonus eruption capable of bleeding and tossing foes around. Over-Charging the greataxe past ^green;100^reset;% will automatically cancel the bonus. ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Axe^reset; --------------- Each consecutive kill made with an axe increases your maximum damage by +^green;1^reset;%, to a maximum of ^green;50^reset;%. If your health is reduced below ^red;20^reset;%, this bonus is cancelled. Each consecutive hit in a row with an axe increases Crit Chance by +^green;3^reset;% (to a maximum of ^green;15^reset;%) ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Dagger^reset; --------------- Consecutive rapid kills temporarily increase damage +^green;25^reset;% Dodge Tech Efficiency Combo Strikes increase Protection and Crit Chance with each strike. The protection bonus is greatest on First Strike, and reduces each hit thereafter. ^cyan;Dual-Wield (Melee):^reset; +^green;5^reset;% Movement Speed ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Shortsword^reset; --------------- +1 Combo strike (was 2, now 3) Each combo hit increases your Crit Damage amount +^green;1^reset;% Crit Chance per Combo Strike First Combo strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage. Second hit does +^green;25^reset;% Crit Damage. ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Broadsword^reset; --------------- Kills made in rapid succession increase defense for a short time +^green;1^reset;% Crit Chance per Combo Strike First Combo strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage. Second hit does +^green;25^reset;% Crit Damage. ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Scythe^reset; --------------- +^green;1^reset;% Crit Chance per Combo Strike First Combo strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage. Second hit does +^green;25^reset;% Crit Damage. ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Longsword^reset; --------------- 3rd Combo Strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage ^cyan;Single Longsword^reset;: -^green;30^reset;% Combo Cooldown ^cyan;Longsword + Shield (Dual Wield)^reset;: +^green;4^reset;% Shield Bash, +^green;1^reset; Shield Bash Push Distance, +^green;15^reset;% Healing Tech Efficiency, +^green;25^reset;% Defense Tech Efficiency ^cyan;Longsword + Any Weapon (Dual Wield)^reset;: Defense x^red;0.8^reset;, +^green;5^reset;% Movement Speed ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Rapier^reset; --------------- When wielding a rapier, the longer you wait between swings the higher your critical strike chance becomes (to a maximum of 5). Attacking resets this bonus. ^cyan;Single Rapier:^reset; +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage, +^green;35^reset;% Dodge and Dash Tech Efficiency ^cyan;Rapier + Dagger (Dual Wield):^reset; x^green;1.12^reset; Protection, +^green;15^reset;% Dodge and Dash Tech Efficiency ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Shortspear^reset; --------------- ^cyan;Single Shortspear^reset;: +^green;30^reset;% Crit Damage ^cyan;Shortspear + Shield^reset;: +^green;10^reset;% Shield Bash, +^green;2^reset; Shield Push Distance, Shield Regen x^green;1.2^reset;, +^green;50^reset;% Defense Tech Efficiency ^cyan;Shortspear + Shortspear (Dual Wield)^reset;: Defense x^red;0.8^reset;, Bonus Crit Chance x^red;0.5^reset; Short Spears also count as Hunting weapons. ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Spear^reset; --------------- Spears are relatively straightforward. They gain crit chance, higher damage output and an increase in Dash Tech efficiency. Spears can be held out by holding the fire button to help keep enemies at bay. If using a Lance typed spear you also gain increased damage based on your movement speed while holding it out. It cannot be aimed during this. Spears also count as Hunting weapons. ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Quarterstaff^reset; --------------- Each hit with a combo increases your Defense. ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Mace^reset; --------------- Combo strikes increase Stun Chance by 2% per hit. ^cyan;Single Mace^reset;: +^green;2^reset;% Stun Chance ^cyan;Mace + Shield^reset;: +^green;3^reset;% Shield Bash, +^green;1^reset; Shield Push Distance, Defense x^green;1.1^reset; ^cyan;Mace + Any Weapon (Dual Wield)^reset;: Bonus Crit Chance x^red;0.85^reset;, Bonus Stun Chance x^red;0.5^reset;, +^green;5^reset;% Movement Speed ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Katana^reset; --------------- Each swing grants a Movement Speed bonus of ^green;1 + (combo step / 10)^reset;% Combo hits increase knockback resistance ^cyan;Single Katana^reset;: +^green;15^reset;% Defense Tech Efficiency ^cyan;Katana + Heavy Melee (Dual Wield)^reset;: Damage x^red;0.8^reset;, Defense x^red;0.9^reset; ^cyan;Katana + Light Melee (Dual Wield)^reset;: Energy x^green;1.15^reset;, +^green;20^reset;% Crit Damage, +^green;25^reset;% Dodge and Dash Tech Efficiency ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Fists^reset; --------------- Normal attacks consume ^red;3% energy^reset; per attack. Holding the button will activate this mode. Combos require timing: Holding or tapping the button too rapidly will use a normal attack. Combo strikes increase Crit Chance by ^green;1%^reset;, Stun chance by ^green;4%^reset; and Protection +1 per strike. When attacking, they use ^red;1%^reset; energy. Alt/Finisher is activated with ^cyan;[Shift + Click]^reset;. Outside of a combo this will use ^red;15%^reset; energy. When completing a combo as the last strike, it will consume none. ^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset; ^orange;Addendum^reset; --------------- Bonus Crit/Stun Chance refer to stats that are not inherent on the weapons themselves, such as from armor or consumables.",
        "translation": "\n^orange;モンスターレジスタンス^reset;\n------------------------\n一部のモンスターは、特定の種類の損傷に抵抗する、または完全に免疫する。\n\nこれらの脅威と戦うためには ^green;異なる要素型^reset; いつでも ご利用ください。 ^green;少なくとも 2 です 3^reset; より多く 8 利用可能なタイプなので、どんなチャレンジにも準備が整います。\n\n\n^blue; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n\n^orange;武器と戦闘^reset;\n----------------------\nレンジドとメリーの武器は、フラッキンユニバースで少し異なる動作をします。 最も重要な変更は、このコードにリストされています。\n\n\n^orange;Crit チャンスとCrit ダメージ ^reset;\n---------------------------\nWeaponアイテムツールチップに新しいアイコンがあります。 左の二つは、クリティカルチャンスボーナスとクリティカルダメージボーナスです。\n\n\n^orange;弾薬と速さのリロード^reset;\n---------------------------\n弾薬とリロード速度は右側のアイコンで表されます。\n\n上記の統計値のいずれかに値を表す '--' を持つ項目は、それらに適用されないことを意味します。 主に弾薬弾(非弾薬銃)を装填した武器である。\n\n\n^orange;Mastery^reset;\n---------------\n\n時折、装備可能なギア、または人種別ボーナスにマスター特性が適用されます。 これは、特定の武器タイプでより大きな能力を持つことを意味します。 一般的に言うと、^yellow;マスターズ^reset;単純に^cyan;既存の武器の利点^reset;技術ボーナスを含め改善します。 以下のトピックでは、それぞれが持っているさまざまな能力とともに、さまざまな武器がリストされています。 これらのリストされた利点はすべて^yellow;Mastery^reset;によって改善されます。\n\n例: 個別に処理した場合、タイミングが注意深く(最大5)ヒットすると、RapierはCrit Chanceに増加します。 ボーナスの額は ^yellow;Mastery^reset;stat に記載されている金額で高くなります。 100%では、+10の最大Crit Chanceボーナスを意味します。\n\n利益の獲得量は、武器ごとに異なる場合があります。 場合によっては、^yellow;Mastery^reset; trait に基づいた修飾子を直接取得しますが、その値の半分、四分の一、八分の一、その他の分数を削減します。\n\n\n\n^blue; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n\n\n^green;範囲^reset;\n----------------------------------\n\n^orange;弾薬ベースの武器^reset;\n------------------\n武器は弾薬が用いられる。 心配しないで、それらを補充するためにリソースを運ぶ必要はありません。 これらの武器は、余分なエネルギーを持つことによって提供される移動性向上と引き換えに、はるかに少ないエネルギーを単に使用します! なお、アルト火は主火に関係なく常にエネルギーを必要とします。\n\nSHIFTキーを長押ししてマウスボタンをクリックすると、これらの武器を手動でリロードできます。 シューティングを通して雑誌を空にすることも自動的にリロードに関与します。\n\n^orange;Ammo Mastery^reset;\n------------------\nAmmo Masteryのレーティングは、リロード時間から削減された % と雑誌ごとに得られる弾薬の$と直接相関します。\n\n^orange;Pistol^reset;\n------------------\nピストルは、マスタリーを適用すると、損傷の増加、リロード時間の短縮、およびクリティカルストライクチャンスの増加を得られる。\n\n^orange;マシンピストル^reset;\n------------------\nマスタリーが適用されると、マシンピストルは損傷の増加、リロード時間の短縮、およびクリティカルストライクチャンスの増加を得る。\n\n^orange;アームキャノン^reset;\n------------------\nアームキャノンは熟練度によって、腕を振り回す方法によって様々な利点を提供します。 パワー、クリティカルチャンス、クリティカルダメージ、および保護はすべて影響を受けます。 アームキャノン(デュアルまたはシングル)だけを使用する場合、保護上のメリットは少なくなりますが、より重要なチャンスがはるかに高くなります。 アームキャノンとシールドを使用すると、電力を削減した代わりに、はるかに優れた保護ボーナスを得ることができます。\n\n^orange;アサルトライフル^reset;\n------------------\nアサルトライフルは、雑誌のサイズと重大な損傷を増加させながら、全体的な損傷出力を増加させることで習得の恩恵を受けます。\n\n^orange;狙撃ライフル^reset;\n------------------\nスナイパーライフルで熟達すると、雑誌のサイズと重要なチャンスを得ることができます。 これは狙撃ライフルの通常のクリトリスの利点と積み重なり、チャージアップと非常に高いクリトリスチャンスを可能にします!\n\n^orange;グレネードランチャー^reset;\n----------------------\n手すり発射機を熟達させると、リロード時間の短縮の恩恵を受けながら、損傷と雑誌のサイズの増加が期待されます。\n\n^orange;ロケット発射器^reset;\n----------------------\nロケットで熟達すれば、敵を消すのは簡単! より多くの損傷をし、リロードを速くし、雑誌のサイズを増加させます。\n\n^orange;Shotgun^reset;\n----------------------\nこれらの危険な武器は、マスターされると、雑誌のサイズの増加とリロード時間の短縮とともに、例外的なクリトリスチャンスとパワーを提供します。\n\n^orange;Magnorb^reset;\n----------------------\nこれらの珍しい武器は、それらを振るったマスターに、被害の増加、危機機会、危機的被害とエネルギーを提供します。\n\n^orange;Bow^reset;\n----------------------\n弓はマスターが活用できる多くの利点があります。 損傷とともに、クリトリス被害とクリトリス確率の増加。 さらに、彼らはより少ないエネルギーを消費しながら弓を速く発射し、矢印を遠くに発射することができます!\n\n^orange; ホイップ^reset;\n----------------------\nホイップユーザーは、このマスター武器で損傷出力を増やしながら、クリトリスチャンスとクリトリスダメージを大幅に増加させます。\n\n\n^blue; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^green;Melee^reset;\n\n^orange; 複合 ^reset;\n---------------\nターゲットにヒットするかどうかに関係なく、コンボの各ストライクは、あなたのエネルギーの1%を消費します。 あなたのエネルギーが消費されると、あなたはもはや組み合わせることができなくなり、代わりに熱狂的な通常の攻撃を実行します。\n注意してください、解錠された敵を含む戦術はもはや実行不可能です。\n\nコンボを持つ多くの武器は、これらのコンボで攻撃すると追加のボーナスを提供します。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;シールドバッシュ^reset;\n---------------\nシールドで敵をブロックすると、バッシュをシールドする機会があります。 特定のギアは、シールドバッシュのチャンスを増やすことができます。\n\nShield Bash は敵を攻撃し、それらを後方へ送ります。 Perfect Blocking では、50% がうまくバッシングされた敵をスタンするチャンスがあります。 完璧なブロックがない場合、注意してください: 最悪のブロックで - あなた - が驚かれる可能性があります。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;Hamer^reset;\n---------------\nこの武器タイプの充電を長く保つほど、クリティカルとスタンの確率が高くなります(最大^green;100^reset;%)。\n\n上述のハンマーが^green;75^reset;%を充電すると、素晴らしい敵を回すことができる大量のボーナス噴火が引き起こされます。\n\nハンマーの過去^green;100^reset;%過充電すると自動的にボーナスがキャンセルされます。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;Great Axe^reset;\n---------------\nこの武器タイプの充電を長持ちすればするほど、クリティカルチャンスとクリティカルダメージが高くなります(最大^green;100^reset;%)。\n\n上記料金の大きい軸。 ^green;75^reset;% 血を流し敵を倒すことができる 大きな賞与の噴火を引き起こすでしょう\n\n超過チャージの過去の^green;100^reset;%は自動的にボーナスをキャンセルします。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;Axe^reset;\n---------------\n軸で連続殺すと、最大損傷が増加します。 +^green;1^reset;%最大で ^green;50^reset;%.\n\n^red;20^reset;%以下で健康状態が低下した場合、このボーナスはキャンセルされます。\n\n連続した各ヒットを軸にすると、Crit Chance が増加します。 +^green;3^reset;% 最大で ^green;15^reset;%)\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;Dagger^reset;\n---------------\n急激な殺害で一時的に被害増加\n\n+^green;25^reset;%ダッジ技術効率\n\nコンボストライクは、各ストライクで保護とクリトリスチャンスを増やします。 保護ボーナスはFirst Strikeで最高であり、その後の各ヒットを減らします。\n\n^cyan;デュアル=ヴィルト (Melee)^reset; +^green;5^reset;% 移動速度\n\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;ショートソード^reset;\n---------------\n+1 コンボストライク(2, 今すぐ3)\n\nそれぞれのコンボヒットで、Critダメージ額が増加します。\n\n+^green;1^reset;% コンボストライクあたりのクリトリスチャンス\n\n最初のコンボストライキは +^green;15^reset;% クリットダメージ。 第二ヒットは+^green;25^reset;%Critダメージです。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;ブロードワード^reset;\n---------------\n急激な継承による殺害は短期間の防御を増加させます。\n\n+^green;1^reset;% コンボストライクあたりのクリトリスチャンス\n\n最初のコンボストライキは +^green;15^reset;% クリットダメージ。 第二ヒットは+^green;25^reset;%Critダメージです。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;Scythe^reset;\n---------------\n+^green;1^reset;% コンボストライクあたりのクリトリスチャンス\n\n最初のコンボストライキは +^green;15^reset;% クリットダメージ。 第二ヒットは+^green;25^reset;%Critダメージです。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;ロングソード^reset;\n---------------\n3rd コンボストライクは +^green;15^reset;% クリティカルダメージ。\n\n^cyan;シングルロングソード ^reset;:-^green;30^reset;%コンボクールダウン。\n\n^cyan;ロングソード+シールド(デュアルワイヤ)^reset;: +^green;4^reset;% シールドバッシュ +^green;1^reset; シールドバッシュプッシュ距離。 +^green;15^reset;% 治療技術効率 +^green;25^reset;% 防衛技術効率\n\n^cyan;ロングソード+武器(デュアルワイルド)^reset;:防御x^red;0.8^reset;,+^green;5^reset;%移動速度。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;Rapier^reset;\n---------------\nラピアを振ると、スイング間の待ち時間が長ければ長いほど、クリティカルストライクの確率が高くなります(最大5)。 攻撃はこのボーナスをリセットします。\n\n^cyan;シングルラピア^reset; +^green;15^reset;% 犯罪被害 +^green;35^reset;% ダッジとダッシュ技術効率\n\n^cyan; Rapier + Dagger (デュアルワイルド): ^reset;x ^green;1.12^reset;Protection, +^green;15^reset;%Ddge, DashTech 効率\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;ショートスピア^reset;\n---------------\n^cyan;単一ショートスピア^reset;:+^green;30^reset;%クリティカルダメージ\n\n^cyan;短槍 + 盾^reset;: シールドバッシュ +^green;10^reset;%、盾で押し出す距離 +^green;2^reset;、盾の回復速度 x^green;1.2^reset;、防御テック効率 +^green;50^reset;%\n\n^cyan;ショートスピア+ショートスピア(デュアルワイルド)^reset;:防御x ^red;0.8^reset;、ボーナスクリトリスx ^red;0.5^reset;\n\nショートスピアーズは狩猟用の武器としても数えられる。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;Spear^reset;\n---------------\nスピーカは比較的単純である。 危機的状況、高い損傷出力、ダッシュテックの効率向上を実現します。\n\n火のボタンを長押しすることで、敵を湾に留めておくことができます。 ランスタイプのスピアを使用すると、持ち歩き速度に基づいて損傷も増加します。 この間は狙えない。\n\nクモは狩猟用の武器としても用いられる。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;クォータースタッフ^reset;\n---------------\nコンボで各ヒットはあなたの防衛を増加させます。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;Mace^reset;\n---------------\nコンボストライキでStun Chanceが上昇 2% ヒットごとに\n\n^cyan;シングルメイス^reset;:+^green;2^reset;% チャンスです。\n\n^cyan; Mace + Shield ^reset;: +^green;3^reset;% Shield Bash, +^green;1^reset; _ Shield Push Distance, Defense x ^green;1.1^reset;\n\n^cyan;Mace + 武器(デュアルワイルド) ^reset;:ボーナスクリティカルチャンスx ^red;0.85^reset;、ボーナススタンチャンスx ^red;0.5^reset;、+^green;5^reset;%移動速度。\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;カタナ^reset;\n---------------\n各スイングは、^green;1+(コンボステップ/10)^reset;%の移動速度ボーナスを付与します。\n\nコンボが耐ノックバック性を高める\n\n^cyan; 単一カタナ ^reset; : +^green;15^reset;% 防衛技術効率\n\n^cyan; Katana + Heavy Melee (Dual Wield) ^reset;: ダメージ x ^red;0.8^reset;, 防御 x ^red;0.9^reset;\n\n^cyan; Katana + Light Melee (デュアルワイルド) ^reset;: エネルギー x ^green;1.15^reset;, +^green;20^reset;%Crit ダメージ, +^green;25^reset;% ダッシュ技術効率\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;拳^reset;\n---------------\n\n通常の攻撃は、攻撃ごとに ^red;3% エネルギー ^reset; を消費します。 ボタンを押すと、このモードが有効になります。\n\nコンボではタイミングが必要: ボタンを長押ししたりタップしたりすると、通常の攻撃を使用します。\n\nコンボストライクは、クリトリスチャンスを^green;1%^reset;、スタンチャンスを^green;4%^reset;、プロテクション+1で増加します。 攻撃時には ^red;1%^reset; エネルギーを使用します。\n\nAlt/Finisher は ^cyan;[Shift+Click]^reset; で有効になります。 コンボの外では ^red;15%^reset;energy を使用します。 最後のストライキとしてコンボを完了すると、何も消費しません。\n\n\n^#555555; -------------------------------------------------- ^reset;\n^orange;追加 ^reset;\n---------------\nボーナスクリット/スタン・チャンス(英: Bonus Crit/Stun Chance)は、武器自体に固有の統計値であり、例えば装甲や消耗品などである。\n",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "title",
        "source": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Battle",
        "normalizedSource": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Battle",
        "translation": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : 戦闘"
      }
    ],
    "ffguidepower": [
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Use the Enhanced Codex Viewer to read this. Access it in your Tricorder.",
        "normalizedSource": "Use the Enhanced Codex Viewer to read this. Access it in your Tricorder.",
        "translation": "この本は、トライコーダーから開ける拡張コーデックスで読めます。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "description",
        "source": "Power Your Lab",
        "normalizedSource": "Power Your Lab",
        "translation": "研究施設に電力を供給しよう"
      },
      {
        "field": "longContentPages",
        "source": "In Frackin' Universe, there are many generators and power sources to fuel your labs and factories. In this codex, each type of generator, its functionality and its mechanics are described.\n\n\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^pink;A Note on Batteries^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nEight kinds of batteries can be crafted in Frackin' Universe. These store energy and dispense it as needed at any level of power, allowing even a weak generator to fuel a very power-hungry machine, if only slowly.\n\nIt is always beneficial to use a battery in any power setup, no matter how small or how large, and it will help eliminate problems where a generator produces power at a different rate than the machine expects it.\n\n\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^white;Table of Contents^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\n^green;Renewable Power^reset;\n  ^#F9F193;Solar Panels^reset;\n  ^#AA6DFF;Nocturn Panels^reset;\n  ^#BBE5E8;Wind Turbines^reset;\n\n^#FF612F;Fuel-Based Generators^reset;\n  ^#BA893F;Alternator Generators^reset;\n  ^gray;Combustion Generators^reset;\n  ^pink;Neuro-Psionic Generators^reset;\n  ^#8CBEF2;Quantum Reactors^reset;\n  ^#FFC600;Precursor Reactors^reset;\n\n^yellow;Decay-Based Generators^reset;\n  ^red;Hydraulic Dynamos^reset;\n  ^#CEF400;Fission Reactors^reset;\n  ^#B7E3E5;Small Fusion Reactors^reset;\n  ^cyan;Large Fusion Reactors^reset;\n\n",
        "normalizedSource": "In Frackin' Universe, there are many generators and power sources to fuel your labs and factories. In this codex, each type of generator, its functionality and its mechanics are described. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^pink;A Note on Batteries^reset; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Eight kinds of batteries can be crafted in Frackin' Universe. These store energy and dispense it as needed at any level of power, allowing even a weak generator to fuel a very power-hungry machine, if only slowly. It is always beneficial to use a battery in any power setup, no matter how small or how large, and it will help eliminate problems where a generator produces power at a different rate than the machine expects it. ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^white;Table of Contents^reset; ^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Renewable Power^reset; ^#F9F193;Solar Panels^reset; ^#AA6DFF;Nocturn Panels^reset; ^#BBE5E8;Wind Turbines^reset; ^#FF612F;Fuel-Based Generators^reset; ^#BA893F;Alternator Generators^reset; ^gray;Combustion Generators^reset; ^pink;Neuro-Psionic Generators^reset; ^#8CBEF2;Quantum Reactors^reset; ^#FFC600;Precursor Reactors^reset; ^yellow;Decay-Based Generators^reset; ^red;Hydraulic Dynamos^reset; ^#CEF400;Fission Reactors^reset; ^#B7E3E5;Small Fusion Reactors^reset; ^cyan;Large Fusion Reactors^reset;",
        "translation": "Frackin' Universeには、あなたの研究室や工場に燃料を供給するための発電機や電源がたくさんあります。 このコーデックスでは、各タイプのジェネレータ、その機能、およびそのメカニズムが記述されている。\n\n\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n   ^pink;バッテリーに関するメモ ^reset;\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n\nフラッキン宇宙では八種類の電池を製造できる。 エネルギーを蓄え、必要に応じて必要な電力を消費することで、弱い発電機でもゆっくりでも非常に電力を消費する機械に燃料を供給することができます。\n\nどんなパワーセットアップでも、どんなに小さくても、どんな大きさでも、バッテリーを使うのは常に有益です。そして、発電機が機械が期待するとは異なる速度で発電する問題を解消するのに役立ちます。\n\n\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n   ^white;コンテンツ表 ^reset;\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n\n^green;再生可能電源^reset;\n  ^#F9F193;ソーラーパネル^reset;\n  ^#AA6DFF;夜のパネル^reset;\n  ^#BBE5E8;風車^reset;\n\n^#FF612F;燃料ベースの発電機^reset;\n  ^#BA893F;オルタネータジェネレータ^reset;\n  ^gray;燃焼発電機^reset;\n  ^pink;神経-超能力ジェネレータ^reset;\n  ^#8CBEF2;量子反応器^reset;\n  ^#FFC600;プレカーリアクター^reset;\n\n^yellow;Decayベースの発電機^reset;\n  ^red;油圧ダイナモ^reset;\n  ^#CEF400;フィッション反応器^reset;\n  ^#B7E3E5;小型核融合炉^reset;\n  ^cyan;大型核融合炉^reset;\n\n",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "longContentPages",
        "source": "\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^green;Renewable Power^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nGreen energy. Low-powered, situational, inconsistent but completely free to operate, renewable energy is suitable for low-power setups or where power is needed infrequently enough that it can be left to build up in a battery for later use.\n\nIf intending to explore renewable energy sources it's recommended to craft the Weather Beacon, researched in the initial node of the ^orange;Electronics tree^reset;. It can be used to determine the power output of renewable energy sources placed at that location, to determine the suitability of the planet.\n\n\n^#F9F193;Solar Panels^reset;\n\nSolar panels come in three varieties. The ^#F9F193;Solar Panel^reset;, ^orange;Solar Array^reset; and ^red;Solar Tower^reset;. When placed on a planet, they generate power during the day and when the natural light is bright enough - up to ^#F9F193;4W^reset;, ^orange;10W^reset; and ^red;24W^reset; respectively on a typical planet, such as a Lush world. On some rare planet types, the light can exceed normal levels and produce significantly more power. Artificial light sources cannot power a solar panel, and panels will not function when submerged in liquid.\n\nOn a ship, space station, or in a star-orbiting asteroid belt, there is no day-night cycle and so solar panels will always produce a fixed amount of power - ^#F9F193;3.5W^reset;, ^orange;8.75W^reset; and ^red;21W^reset; respectively. They're a much more reliable source of energy when the sun never sets.\n\n\n^#AA6DFF;Nocturn Panels^reset;\n\nSimilar to solar panels, Nocturn Panels care about the level of light falling upon them. Unlike solar panels, however, Nocturn Panels fear the light and thus produce more energy in a darkened space - up to ^#AA6DFF;10W^reset; in the pitch black. Nocturn Panels are perfectly content underground and do not care whether it is day or night. They're happy to be contained within a lightless box, producing the same level of power eternally, but they do not function when submerged.\n\nNocturn Panels are the product of ^orange;maddened research^reset;, and function anywhere.\n\n\n^#BBE5E8;Wind Turbines^reset;\n\nWind Turbines come in one variety, which can produce up to ^#BBE5E8;12W^reset; in ideal conditions. The amount of power produced depends on how windy the current weather is, and the types of weather available depend on the planet. Some planet types have eternally windy weather and will produce a constant ^#BBE5E8;12W^reset; of power, while some will never produce any power at all, and others will vary. Experimentation and the Weather Beacon will help identify the best planets for wind power.\n\nWind Turbines do not function on ships, space stations, and in asteroid belts.\n\n",
        "normalizedSource": "^blue;------------------------^reset; ^green;Renewable Power^reset; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Green energy. Low-powered, situational, inconsistent but completely free to operate, renewable energy is suitable for low-power setups or where power is needed infrequently enough that it can be left to build up in a battery for later use. If intending to explore renewable energy sources it's recommended to craft the Weather Beacon, researched in the initial node of the ^orange;Electronics tree^reset;. It can be used to determine the power output of renewable energy sources placed at that location, to determine the suitability of the planet. ^#F9F193;Solar Panels^reset; Solar panels come in three varieties. The ^#F9F193;Solar Panel^reset;, ^orange;Solar Array^reset; and ^red;Solar Tower^reset;. When placed on a planet, they generate power during the day and when the natural light is bright enough - up to ^#F9F193;4W^reset;, ^orange;10W^reset; and ^red;24W^reset; respectively on a typical planet, such as a Lush world. On some rare planet types, the light can exceed normal levels and produce significantly more power. Artificial light sources cannot power a solar panel, and panels will not function when submerged in liquid. On a ship, space station, or in a star-orbiting asteroid belt, there is no day-night cycle and so solar panels will always produce a fixed amount of power - ^#F9F193;3.5W^reset;, ^orange;8.75W^reset; and ^red;21W^reset; respectively. They're a much more reliable source of energy when the sun never sets. ^#AA6DFF;Nocturn Panels^reset; Similar to solar panels, Nocturn Panels care about the level of light falling upon them. Unlike solar panels, however, Nocturn Panels fear the light and thus produce more energy in a darkened space - up to ^#AA6DFF;10W^reset; in the pitch black. Nocturn Panels are perfectly content underground and do not care whether it is day or night. They're happy to be contained within a lightless box, producing the same level of power eternally, but they do not function when submerged. Nocturn Panels are the product of ^orange;maddened research^reset;, and function anywhere. ^#BBE5E8;Wind Turbines^reset; Wind Turbines come in one variety, which can produce up to ^#BBE5E8;12W^reset; in ideal conditions. The amount of power produced depends on how windy the current weather is, and the types of weather available depend on the planet. Some planet types have eternally windy weather and will produce a constant ^#BBE5E8;12W^reset; of power, while some will never produce any power at all, and others will vary. Experimentation and the Weather Beacon will help identify the best planets for wind power. Wind Turbines do not function on ships, space stations, and in asteroid belts.",
        "translation": "\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n   ^green;再生可能電源^reset;\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n\nグリーンエネルギー。 低電力、状況、一貫性がないが完全に自由に動作できる再生可能エネルギーは、低電力のセットアップや、後で使用するバッテリーに蓄積できるほど電源が必要な場合に適しています。\n\n再生可能エネルギー源を探索する場合は、^orange;Electronicstree^reset;の最初のノードで研究されたWeather ビーコンを作成することをお勧めします。 それは、惑星の適合性を決定するために、その場所に置かれた再生可能エネルギー源の出力を決定するために使用することができます。\n\n\n^#F9F193;ソーラーパネル^reset;\n\nソーラーパネルは三種類あります。 ^#F9F193; ソーラーパネル ^reset; 、 ^orange; ソーラーアレイ ^reset; 、 ^red; ソーラータワー ^reset; 。 惑星上に置くと、日中に、そして自然光が十分に明るいときに、それぞれ、ラッシュワールドなどの典型的な惑星で、^#F9F193;4W^reset;、^orange;10W^reset;、^red;24W^reset;まで発電します。 いくつかの希少な惑星では、光は通常のレベルを超え、かなり多くの電力を発生させることができる。 人工光源は太陽光パネルに電力を供給できず、液体に浸すとパネルは機能しません。\n\n宇宙船や宇宙ステーション、あるいは小惑星帯の軌道を周回する小惑星には、昼夜周期はなく、ソーラーパネルは常に一定量の電力を発生させます。 - ^#F9F193;3.5W:^reset;, ^orange;8.75W:^reset; そして ^red;21W:^reset; それぞれです 太陽が決して沈まないとき、彼らははるかに信頼性の高いエネルギー源です。\n\n\n^#AA6DFF;夜のパネル^reset;\n\nソーラーパネルと同様に、夜のパネルはそれらに落ちる光のレベルを気にします。 しかし、ソーラーパネルとは異なり、ナイトターンパネルは光を恐れ、暗い空間でより多くのエネルギーを発生させます。 ^#AA6DFF;10W:^reset; 真っ黒に 夜のパネルは地下に完全に含まれており、昼夜問わずに構いません。 光のない箱の中に閉じ込めて、同じレベルの力を永遠に生み出すことは幸せですが、水中では機能しません。\n\n夜のパネルは^orange;狂った研究^reset;の製品であり、どこでも機能します。\n\n\n^#BBE5E8;風車^reset;\n\n風車には一種類の種類があり、理想的な条件で最大^#BBE5E8;12W^reset;を生成することができます。 発電量は、現在の気象の風向きと、利用可能な天候の種類によって異なります惑星によって異なります。 一部の惑星タイプは、恒久的な風の天気があり、一定の^#BBE5E8;12W ^reset;を生成するが、一部の惑星タイプは決して電力を生産せず、他の惑星タイプも変化する。 実験と気象ビーコンは、風力にとって最適な惑星を特定するのに役立ちます。\n\n風力タービンは、船、宇宙ステーション、小惑星帯では機能しません。\n\n",
        "index": 2
      },
      {
        "field": "longContentPages",
        "source": "\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^#FF612F;Fuel-Based Generators^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nBad for the environment and good for your factory, fuel-based generators are the backbone of any serious early- to mid-game lab or factory, producing significant power.\n\nAll fuel-based generators work using a Heat system. When fuel is first placed in the generator, or it is turned on, it will consume one fuel item and begin heating up. Its heat level, which reaches maximum productivity after 18-20 seconds, either partially or fully determines the power output of the generator. In some generators the chosen fuel determines only how quickly the generator consumes fuel, and in some the chosen fuel also provides power on top of that generated by its heat.\n\nWhen a fuel-based generator is turned off, by supplying an 'off' signal to its first blue input node, it will finish consuming its current fuel item before ceasing operation to avoid wasting fuel.\n\n\n^#BA893F;Alternator Generators^reset;\n\nThe first generator a player will gain access to. The Alternator Generator can only consume wood and coal, though these materials are abundant on most worlds. The Alternator Generator will only produce ^#BA893F;4W^reset; at full heat (reached after 18s), and so it should be quickly replaced by the ^gray;Combustion Generator^reset; or another power source.\n\nAccepted fuels (burn time):\n----------\nWooden Log (10s), Coal (16s), Golden Wood (20s), Redwood Bark (20s), Penumbral Bark (30s), Alien Weird Wood (40s), Energy Wood (50s), Aen Wood Log (60s)\n\n\n^gray;Combustion Generator^reset;\n\nA serious power source for a growing industrialist, the Combustion Generator accepts the greatest variety of fuels of any generator and can produce a respectable amount of power from both solid and liquid fuels, including wood, erchius and fuel canisters. The Combustion Generator produces ^gray;12W^reset; of power at full heat (reached after 18s).\n\nAccepted fuels (burn time):\n----------\nPaper (1s), Unrefined Wood (2s), Wooden Log (5s), Coal (8s), Hydrogen (9s), Methanol (9s), Liquid Erchius Fuel (10s), Oil (10s), Redwood Bark (10s), Biofuel Canister (10s), Crystal Erchius Fuel (12s), Unrefined Fuel (13s), Refined Fuel (15s), Penumbral Bark (15s), Golden Wood (15s), Erithian Biofuel Canister (15s), Protocite Fuel Canister (20s), Alien Weird Wood (20s), Energy Wood (25s), Erchius Crystal (25s), Aen Wood Log (30s), Crunchy Chick (30s)\n\n\n^pink;Neuro-Psionic Generators^reset;\n\nThe product of ^orange;maddened research^reset;, Neuro-Psionic Generators use neurological power, drawn from stolen brains, to fuel your mad experimentation. Brains are a plentiful resource with the right equipment, and so a budding mad scientist can easily provide for all their power needs if they're not afraid to get their hands dirty. Neuro-Psionic Generators can produce ^pink;60W^reset; of power at full heat (reached after 18s).\n\nAccepted fuels (burn time):\n----------\nInferior Brain (10s), Superior Brain (20s), Artificial Brain (60s), Perfect Brain (60s), Psi-1 Energy (60s), Psi-2 Energy (80s), Psi-3 Energy (100s), Psi-4 Energy (120s), Brain in a Jar (200s), Superior Brain Housing (360s), Artificial Brain Housing (360s), Advanced Brain Housing (520s)\n\n\n^#8CBEF2;Quantum Reactors^reset;\n\nAn incredibly efficient and powerful generator, a single Quantum Reactor is sufficient to power a substantial lab all by itself, and can be trivially powered by infinitely-obtainable fuel sources in the late game. The Quantum Reactor's output depends on its fuel source, and can reach ^#8CBEF2;620W^reset;, of which ^#8CBEF2;20W^reset; is heat built up over 20s of use.\n\nAccepted fuels (power, burn time):\n----------\nBiofuel Canister (60W, 40s), Erithian Biofuel Canister (70W, 50s), Uranium Rod (70W, 50s), Energiflower (80W, 60s), Plutonium Rod (80W, 60s), Helium-3 (90W, 70s), Liquid Protocite (100W, 80s), Neptunium Rod (110W, 90s), Thorium Rod (110W, 90s), Energy Wood (125W, 105s), Enriched Uranium Rod (150W, 130s), Essentia Obscura (170W, 150s), Protocite Fuel Canister (220W, 200s), Enriched Plutonium Rod (240W, 220s), Metallic Hydrogen (275W, 255s), Deuterium Rod (300W, 280s), Tritium Rod (320W, 300s), Solarium Star (470W, 450s), Ultronium Rod (520W, 500s), Liquid Metallic Hydrogen (570W, 550s), Liquid Deuterium (620W, 600s)\n\n\n^#FFC600;Precursor Reactors^reset;\n\nThe most powerful generator in the game bar none, Precursor Reactors create phenomenal amounts of power but cannot be crafted, and are instead found in the abandoned colonies and factories of the extinct Precursors. Unlike other generators, they have an additional requirement - to channel the power sources of the ancients, you must place one Neutronium Rod and one Anti-Neutronium Rod, both products of ^orange;maddened research^reset;, in the designated slots. For your trouble, Precursor Generators can produce up to ^#FFC600;1055W^reset; depending on their fuel source, of which ^#FFC600;95W^reset; is heat, reaching their full output (50%+ heat) after 20s.\n\nAccepted fuels (power, burn time):\n----------\nPoop (135W, 40s), Crunchy Chick (195W, 100s), Essentia Obscura (315W, 220s), Quantum Fluid (515W, 420s), Ultronium Rod (745W, 650s), Dimensional Cell (1055W, 960s)\n\n",
        "normalizedSource": "^blue;------------------------^reset; ^#FF612F;Fuel-Based Generators^reset; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Bad for the environment and good for your factory, fuel-based generators are the backbone of any serious early- to mid-game lab or factory, producing significant power. All fuel-based generators work using a Heat system. When fuel is first placed in the generator, or it is turned on, it will consume one fuel item and begin heating up. Its heat level, which reaches maximum productivity after 18-20 seconds, either partially or fully determines the power output of the generator. In some generators the chosen fuel determines only how quickly the generator consumes fuel, and in some the chosen fuel also provides power on top of that generated by its heat. When a fuel-based generator is turned off, by supplying an 'off' signal to its first blue input node, it will finish consuming its current fuel item before ceasing operation to avoid wasting fuel. ^#BA893F;Alternator Generators^reset; The first generator a player will gain access to. The Alternator Generator can only consume wood and coal, though these materials are abundant on most worlds. The Alternator Generator will only produce ^#BA893F;4W^reset; at full heat (reached after 18s), and so it should be quickly replaced by the ^gray;Combustion Generator^reset; or another power source. Accepted fuels (burn time): ---------- Wooden Log (10s), Coal (16s), Golden Wood (20s), Redwood Bark (20s), Penumbral Bark (30s), Alien Weird Wood (40s), Energy Wood (50s), Aen Wood Log (60s) ^gray;Combustion Generator^reset; A serious power source for a growing industrialist, the Combustion Generator accepts the greatest variety of fuels of any generator and can produce a respectable amount of power from both solid and liquid fuels, including wood, erchius and fuel canisters. The Combustion Generator produces ^gray;12W^reset; of power at full heat (reached after 18s). Accepted fuels (burn time): ---------- Paper (1s), Unrefined Wood (2s), Wooden Log (5s), Coal (8s), Hydrogen (9s), Methanol (9s), Liquid Erchius Fuel (10s), Oil (10s), Redwood Bark (10s), Biofuel Canister (10s), Crystal Erchius Fuel (12s), Unrefined Fuel (13s), Refined Fuel (15s), Penumbral Bark (15s), Golden Wood (15s), Erithian Biofuel Canister (15s), Protocite Fuel Canister (20s), Alien Weird Wood (20s), Energy Wood (25s), Erchius Crystal (25s), Aen Wood Log (30s), Crunchy Chick (30s) ^pink;Neuro-Psionic Generators^reset; The product of ^orange;maddened research^reset;, Neuro-Psionic Generators use neurological power, drawn from stolen brains, to fuel your mad experimentation. Brains are a plentiful resource with the right equipment, and so a budding mad scientist can easily provide for all their power needs if they're not afraid to get their hands dirty. Neuro-Psionic Generators can produce ^pink;60W^reset; of power at full heat (reached after 18s). Accepted fuels (burn time): ---------- Inferior Brain (10s), Superior Brain (20s), Artificial Brain (60s), Perfect Brain (60s), Psi-1 Energy (60s), Psi-2 Energy (80s), Psi-3 Energy (100s), Psi-4 Energy (120s), Brain in a Jar (200s), Superior Brain Housing (360s), Artificial Brain Housing (360s), Advanced Brain Housing (520s) ^#8CBEF2;Quantum Reactors^reset; An incredibly efficient and powerful generator, a single Quantum Reactor is sufficient to power a substantial lab all by itself, and can be trivially powered by infinitely-obtainable fuel sources in the late game. The Quantum Reactor's output depends on its fuel source, and can reach ^#8CBEF2;620W^reset;, of which ^#8CBEF2;20W^reset; is heat built up over 20s of use. Accepted fuels (power, burn time): ---------- Biofuel Canister (60W, 40s), Erithian Biofuel Canister (70W, 50s), Uranium Rod (70W, 50s), Energiflower (80W, 60s), Plutonium Rod (80W, 60s), Helium-3 (90W, 70s), Liquid Protocite (100W, 80s), Neptunium Rod (110W, 90s), Thorium Rod (110W, 90s), Energy Wood (125W, 105s), Enriched Uranium Rod (150W, 130s), Essentia Obscura (170W, 150s), Protocite Fuel Canister (220W, 200s), Enriched Plutonium Rod (240W, 220s), Metallic Hydrogen (275W, 255s), Deuterium Rod (300W, 280s), Tritium Rod (320W, 300s), Solarium Star (470W, 450s), Ultronium Rod (520W, 500s), Liquid Metallic Hydrogen (570W, 550s), Liquid Deuterium (620W, 600s) ^#FFC600;Precursor Reactors^reset; The most powerful generator in the game bar none, Precursor Reactors create phenomenal amounts of power but cannot be crafted, and are instead found in the abandoned colonies and factories of the extinct Precursors. Unlike other generators, they have an additional requirement - to channel the power sources of the ancients, you must place one Neutronium Rod and one Anti-Neutronium Rod, both products of ^orange;maddened research^reset;, in the designated slots. For your trouble, Precursor Generators can produce up to ^#FFC600;1055W^reset; depending on their fuel source, of which ^#FFC600;95W^reset; is heat, reaching their full output (50%+ heat) after 20s. Accepted fuels (power, burn time): ---------- Poop (135W, 40s), Crunchy Chick (195W, 100s), Essentia Obscura (315W, 220s), Quantum Fluid (515W, 420s), Ultronium Rod (745W, 650s), Dimensional Cell (1055W, 960s)",
        "translation": "\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n   ^#FF612F;燃料ベースの発電機^reset;\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n\n環境に悪影響を及ぼし、あなたの工場にとって良い、燃料ベースの発電機は、深刻な早期から中期の研究室や工場のバックボーンであり、大きな力を生み出します。\n\nすべての燃料ベースの発電機はヒートシステムを使用して動作します。 発電機に燃料を入れたり、電源を入れたりすると、燃料アイテムを一つ消費して加熱を開始します。 18-20秒後に最大生産性に達するその熱レベルは、発電機の出力を部分的または完全に決定する。 いくつかの発電機では、選択した燃料は発電機が燃料をどれだけ早く消費するかだけを決定し、一部の発電機では、選択した燃料は、その熱によって生成された上に電力も供給します。\n\n燃料ベースの発電機をオフにすると、最初の青色入力ノードに「オフ」信号を供給することで、燃料を無駄にしないように操作を終了する前に現在の燃料アイテムを消費終了します。\n\n\n^#BA893F;オルタネータジェネレータ^reset;\n\nプレーヤーがアクセス可能な最初のジェネレータ。 オルタネータ発電機は木材と石炭しか消費できないが、これらの材料はほとんどの世界で豊富である。 オルタネータ発電機は ^#BA893F;4W:^reset; 全熱で到達する 18s)) なので、すぐに置き換えるべきです。 ^gray;燃焼発電機^reset; あるいは別の電源です\n\n許容される燃料(燃焼時間)。\n----------\nウッドログ (Wooden Log)10s)、Coal ()16ゴールデンウッド (Golden Wood)20レッドウッド・バーク (Redwood Bark)20ペヌブラール樹皮(Penumbral Bark)30エイリアン・ウィアード・ウッド (Alien Weird Wood)40エナジーウッド(英: Energy Wood)50)、Aen Wood Log ()。60)\n\n\n^gray;燃焼発電機^reset;\n\n成長している産業家にとって深刻な電源である燃焼発電機は、あらゆる発電機の燃料の多種多様を受け入れ、木、エルキウス、燃料キャニスターなどの固体燃料と液体燃料の両方からかなりの量の電力を生成することができます。 燃焼発生器は、全熱で電力の^gray;12W^reset;を生成する(18sの後に到達する)。\n\n許容される燃料(燃焼時間)。\n----------\n紙(紙)1木(木)2)、木製ログ (s)。5s)、Coal ()8s)、水素()9s)、メタノール(s)9液状エルキウス燃料(s)10s)、オイル()10レッドウッド・バーク (Redwood Bark)10バイオ燃料キャニスター(バイオ燃料キャニスター)10結晶性アーキウス燃料 (Crystal Erchius Fuel)。12)、未精製燃料()。13s)、精製燃料()。15ペヌブラール樹皮(Penumbral Bark)15ゴールデンウッド (Golden Wood)15エリート式バイオ燃料キャニスター(エリート式)15燃料キャニスター(燃料キャニスター)をプロトサイトします。20エイリアン・ウィアード・ウッド (Alien Weird Wood)20エナジーウッド(英: Energy Wood)25)、Erchius Crystal ()。25)、Aen Wood Log ()。30Crunchy Chick () です。30)\n\n\n^pink;神経-Psionicジェネレータ^reset;\n\n^orange; 狂った研究 ^reset; の製品は、神経-Psionicジェネレータは、あなたの狂った実験を燃料に、盗まれた脳から引き出された神経学的パワーを使用します。 脳は、適切な機器を備えた豊富なリソースです。したがって、手が汚れるのを恐れていない場合、最新の狂気の科学者は簡単にすべてのパワーニーズを提供できます。 神経Psionicジェネレータは、フルヒートで^pink;60W^reset;を生成することができます(18sの後に到達)。\n\n許容される燃料(燃焼時間)。\n----------\n下脳(英語)10頭脳(S)20人工脳 (Artificial Brain) (英語)60パーフェクト・ブレイン(Perfect Brain)60s)、Psi-1 エネルギー60s)、Psi-2 エネルギー80s)、Psi-3 エネルギー100s)、Psi-4 エネルギー120)、ジャー内の脳(。200スペリオル・ブレイン・ハウジング(英: Superior Brain House)360人工脳ハウジング (Artificial Brain Housing)。360)、高度な脳ハウジング。520)\n\n\n^#8CBEF2;量子反応器^reset;\n\n信じられないほど効率的で強力な発電機である単一の量子反応器は、それ自体で実質的な実験室を駆動するのに十分であり、後期ゲームで無限に入手可能な燃料源によって自明に動力を得ることができます。 量子リアクタの出力は燃料源に依存し、^#8CBEF2;620W^reset;に達することができ、その^#8CBEF2;20W^reset;は20sで熱蓄積される。\n\n許容される燃料(電力、燃焼時間)。\n----------\nバイオ燃料キャニスター(Biofuel Canister)60W: 40エリート式バイオ燃料キャニスター(エリート式)70W: 50ウラン棒(U)70W: 50)、Energiflower ()80W: 60プルトニウムロッド(Plutonium Rod)80W: 60ヘリウム-3 (90W: 70s)、液体プロトサイト(。100W: 80s)、Neptunium Rod()110W: 90)、トリウム・ロッド(Torium Rod)。110W: 90エナジーウッド(英: Energy Wood)125W: 105ウラン棒(ウラン棒)を濃縮します。150W: 130エッセンシア・オブスキュラ(Essentia Obscura)170W: 150燃料キャニスター(燃料キャニスター)をプロトサイトします。220W: 200)、富化プルトニウムロッド(。240W: 220s)、金属水素(s)275W: 255s)、重水素棒()。300W: 280三重棒(トリチウム棒)320W: 300s)、Solarium Star ()。470W: 450ウルトロニウムロッド(Ultronium Rod)520W: 500s), 液体金属水素 (570W, 550s), 液体重水素 (620W, 600s)\n\n\n^#FFC600;プレカーリアクター^reset;\n\nゲーム内で並ぶもののない最強の発電機、先駆者リアクターは、驚異的な電力を生み出します。ただし製作はできず、絶滅した先駆者たちが残した、放棄されたコロニーや工場で見つける必要があります。 他の発電機とは異なり、彼らは追加の要件を持っています - 古代の電源をチャネルするには、指定されたスロットに^orange;狂った研究^reset;の両方の製品である一つのノイトロニウムロッドと一つの反ノイトロニウムロッドを置く必要があります。 問題が発生した場合、プリカーサジェネレータは最大で生成できます。 ^#FFC600;1055W:^reset; 燃料源によっては ^#FFC600;95W:^reset; 熱で全出力に達しています50%熱)後 20ス\n\n許容される燃料(電力、燃焼時間)。\n----------\nうんち(うんち)135W: 40Crunchy Chick () です。195W: 100エッセンシア・オブスキュラ(Essentia Obscura)315W: 220量子流体(Quantum Fluid)515W: 420ウルトロニウムロッド(Ultronium Rod)745W: 650)、寸法セル()。1055W: 960)\n\n",
        "index": 3
      },
      {
        "field": "longContentPages",
        "source": "\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Decay-Based Generators^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nMake sure to dispose of the waste cleanly (or profitably). Decay-based generators output power by gradually and randomly consuming isotopes over time. Uniquely, these generators come with multiple fuel slots, giving them the ability to vary their power output by filling the desired number of slots to adapt to any required workload without changing the fuel type, though each fuel slot may use different fuel if desired.\n\nDecay-based generators will turn off immediately when an 'off' signal is supplied to their first blue input node, and will not waste fuel in doing so.\n\n\n^red;Hydraulic Dynamo^reset;\n\nAn honourable inclusion, the Hydraulic Dynamo is an early-game generator that evaporates water using hot solids and liquids (or liquid nitrogen) in order to generate power. Although very large, it outperforms many other early generators despite being craftable on the first world and fuelled by trivially-obtainable substances such as lava and core fragments. The Hydraulic Dynamo can generate up to ^red;21W^reset; at maximum output, but will not function without water, consuming one for each fuel item used. The Hydraulic Dynamo has three fuel slots.\n\nAccepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time):\n----------\nLava (4W, 10s), Core Fragment (5W, 40s), Liquid Iron (6W, 32s), Volatile Powder (7W, 40s), Scorched Core (7W, 180s), Liquid Nitrogen (6W, 20s)\n\n\n^#CEF400;Fission Reactors^reset;\n\nGood old-fashioned nuclear power, the greenest thing about it is the uranium it consumes. Fission Reactors are an affordable way to create significant amounts of power, reaching up to ^#CEF400;360W^reset; across their four fuel slots. Uniquely, this generator creates Tritium Rods as a by-product of its fission, with a 50% chance for one to be made each time a fuel item is consumed. It will also create Toxic Waste, two if Tritium is created and one otherwise. While active, depending on how long it's been operating and how much power it's generating, the Fission Generator will begin to flood its nearby area with Moderate Radiation, up to 16 tiles away. Walls and other containment will not block this, only distance and Moderate Radiation immunity will help.\n\nAccepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time):\n----------\nTritium Rod (10W, 40s), Deuterium Rod (15W, 50s), Uranium Rod (20W, 90s), Plutonium Rod (30W, 90s), Neptunium Rod (40W, 90s), Thorium Rod (50W, 90s), Enriched Uranium Rod (60W, 120s), Enriched Plutonium Rod (80W, 180s), Solarium Star (80W, 240s), Ultronium Rod (90W, 300s)\n\n\n^#B7E3E5;Small Fusion Reactors^reset;\n\nHarness the power of the stars for your lab, albeit on a very small scale. Fusion Reactors of both kinds fuse light isotopes together, releasing nuclear energy from them to create power. Like the Fission Reactor, Fusion Reactors generate Moderate Radiation the longer and more productively they operate, which cannot be blocked. Small Fusion Reactors have four fuel slots, and can generate ^#B7E3E5;360W^reset; when filling all of them. They must be given coolant to continue operating or will quickly overheat and shut down, releasing a burst of radiation, though water is typically sufficient. Each consumed fuel will create one Toxic Waste, which can be used as coolant in a pinch.\n\nAccepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time):\n----------\nHydrogen (15W, 50s), Tritium Rod (25W, 60s), Helium-3 (45W, 80s), Solarium Star (55W, 150s), Deuterium Rod (60W, 120s), Ultronium Rod (90W, 700s)\n\nAccepted coolants (heat reduction per item)\nToxic Waste (10), Salt Water (30), Water (30), Liquid Nitrogen (80), Cryonic Extract (125)\n\n\n^cyan;Large Fusion Reactors^reset;\n\nOriginally pioneered by the Skath, Large Fusion Reactors are simply better-built, scaled-up versions of Small Fusion Reactors with a greater power output. Filling their four slots, they can generate up to ^cyan;600W^reset;. They generate radiation and produce Toxic Waste as Small Fusion Reactors do.\n\nAccepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time):\n----------\nHydrogen (35W, 50s), Tritium Rod (55W, 60s), Helium-3 (60W, 80s), Solarium Star (105W, 150s), Deuterium Rod (90W, 120s), Liquid Deuterium (90W, 120s), Ultronium Rod (150W, 700s)\n\nAccepted coolants (heat reduction per item)\nSalt Water (20), Water (30), Toxic Waste (40), Liquid Nitrogen (80), Cryonic Extract (125)\n\n",
        "normalizedSource": "^blue;------------------------^reset; ^yellow;Decay-Based Generators^reset; ^blue;------------------------^reset; Make sure to dispose of the waste cleanly (or profitably). Decay-based generators output power by gradually and randomly consuming isotopes over time. Uniquely, these generators come with multiple fuel slots, giving them the ability to vary their power output by filling the desired number of slots to adapt to any required workload without changing the fuel type, though each fuel slot may use different fuel if desired. Decay-based generators will turn off immediately when an 'off' signal is supplied to their first blue input node, and will not waste fuel in doing so. ^red;Hydraulic Dynamo^reset; An honourable inclusion, the Hydraulic Dynamo is an early-game generator that evaporates water using hot solids and liquids (or liquid nitrogen) in order to generate power. Although very large, it outperforms many other early generators despite being craftable on the first world and fuelled by trivially-obtainable substances such as lava and core fragments. The Hydraulic Dynamo can generate up to ^red;21W^reset; at maximum output, but will not function without water, consuming one for each fuel item used. The Hydraulic Dynamo has three fuel slots. Accepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time): ---------- Lava (4W, 10s), Core Fragment (5W, 40s), Liquid Iron (6W, 32s), Volatile Powder (7W, 40s), Scorched Core (7W, 180s), Liquid Nitrogen (6W, 20s) ^#CEF400;Fission Reactors^reset; Good old-fashioned nuclear power, the greenest thing about it is the uranium it consumes. Fission Reactors are an affordable way to create significant amounts of power, reaching up to ^#CEF400;360W^reset; across their four fuel slots. Uniquely, this generator creates Tritium Rods as a by-product of its fission, with a 50% chance for one to be made each time a fuel item is consumed. It will also create Toxic Waste, two if Tritium is created and one otherwise. While active, depending on how long it's been operating and how much power it's generating, the Fission Generator will begin to flood its nearby area with Moderate Radiation, up to 16 tiles away. Walls and other containment will not block this, only distance and Moderate Radiation immunity will help. Accepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time): ---------- Tritium Rod (10W, 40s), Deuterium Rod (15W, 50s), Uranium Rod (20W, 90s), Plutonium Rod (30W, 90s), Neptunium Rod (40W, 90s), Thorium Rod (50W, 90s), Enriched Uranium Rod (60W, 120s), Enriched Plutonium Rod (80W, 180s), Solarium Star (80W, 240s), Ultronium Rod (90W, 300s) ^#B7E3E5;Small Fusion Reactors^reset; Harness the power of the stars for your lab, albeit on a very small scale. Fusion Reactors of both kinds fuse light isotopes together, releasing nuclear energy from them to create power. Like the Fission Reactor, Fusion Reactors generate Moderate Radiation the longer and more productively they operate, which cannot be blocked. Small Fusion Reactors have four fuel slots, and can generate ^#B7E3E5;360W^reset; when filling all of them. They must be given coolant to continue operating or will quickly overheat and shut down, releasing a burst of radiation, though water is typically sufficient. Each consumed fuel will create one Toxic Waste, which can be used as coolant in a pinch. Accepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time): ---------- Hydrogen (15W, 50s), Tritium Rod (25W, 60s), Helium-3 (45W, 80s), Solarium Star (55W, 150s), Deuterium Rod (60W, 120s), Ultronium Rod (90W, 700s) Accepted coolants (heat reduction per item) Toxic Waste (10), Salt Water (30), Water (30), Liquid Nitrogen (80), Cryonic Extract (125) ^cyan;Large Fusion Reactors^reset; Originally pioneered by the Skath, Large Fusion Reactors are simply better-built, scaled-up versions of Small Fusion Reactors with a greater power output. Filling their four slots, they can generate up to ^cyan;600W^reset;. They generate radiation and produce Toxic Waste as Small Fusion Reactors do. Accepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time): ---------- Hydrogen (35W, 50s), Tritium Rod (55W, 60s), Helium-3 (60W, 80s), Solarium Star (105W, 150s), Deuterium Rod (90W, 120s), Liquid Deuterium (90W, 120s), Ultronium Rod (150W, 700s) Accepted coolants (heat reduction per item) Salt Water (20), Water (30), Toxic Waste (40), Liquid Nitrogen (80), Cryonic Extract (125)",
        "translation": "\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n   ^yellow;Decayベースの発電機^reset;\n   ^blue; ------------------------ ^reset;\n\n廃棄物をきれいに(または利益を)処理してください。 劣化ベースの発電機は、時間とともに徐々にランダムに同位体消費によって電力を出力する。 ユニークなことに、これらの発電機には複数の燃料スロットが付属しており、燃料タイプを変更することなく必要な負荷に適応するために所望の数のスロットを充填することで、出力を変化させることができますが、各燃料スロットは必要に応じて異なる燃料を使用する場合があります。\n\n停電ベースの発電機は、最初の青色入力ノードに「オフ」信号が供給されるとすぐに停止し、燃料を無駄にしません。\n\n\n^red;油圧ダイナモ^reset;\n\n特筆しておきたいのが、序盤に使える発電機の水力ダイナモだ。高温の固体や液体（または液体窒素）を使って水を蒸発させ、電力を生み出す。 非常に大きいにもかかわらず、それは最初の世界で製造可能であり、溶岩やコアフラグメントなどの自明に得られる物質によって燃料を供給されているにもかかわらず、他の多くの初期の発電機よりも優れています。 油圧ダイナモは最大出力で最大^red;21W^reset;を生成することができますが、水なしでは機能せず、使用する燃料アイテムごとに一つを消費します。 油圧ダイナモには三つの燃料スロットがあります。\n\n許容される燃料(燃料スロットあたりの電力、平均減衰時間)。\n----------\nLava (4W, 10s), Core Fragment (5W, 40s), Liquid Iron (6W, 32s), Volatile Powder (7W, 40s), Scorched Core (7W, 180s), Liquid Nitrogen (6W, 20s)\n\n\n^#CEF400;フィッション反応器^reset;\n\n昔ながらの原子力発電としては、最も緑色のものはウランです。 核分裂反応器は、四つの燃料スロットで^#CEF400;360W^reset;に達する大量の電力を生成する手頃な価格の方法です。 この生成装置は、核分裂の副産物としてトリチウムロッドを生成し、燃料アイテムが消費されるたびに一つが作られる50%チャンスを持つ。 また、トリチウムが作成され、そうでなければ二つの毒性廃棄物を作成します。 アクティブで、動作期間や発電量によっては、核分裂生成装置は近隣エリアに、最大で16タイルまで、中程度の放射線を吹き込み始めます。 壁やその他の封じ込めはこれをブロックしませんが、距離と適度な放射線免疫だけが役立ちます。\n\n許容される燃料(燃料スロットあたりの電力、平均減衰時間)。\n----------\nトリチウム棒10W: 40s)、重水素棒()。15W: 50ウラン棒(U)20W: 90プルトニウムロッド(Plutonium Rod)30W: 90s)、Neptunium Rod()40W: 90)、トリウム・ロッド(Torium Rod)。50W: 90ウラン棒(ウラン棒)を濃縮します。60W: 120)、富化プルトニウムロッド(。80W: 180s)、Solarium Star ()。80W: 240ウルトロニウムロッド(Ultronium Rod)90W: 300)\n\n\n^#B7E3E5;小型核融合炉^reset;\n\n非常に小さなスケールで、あなたの研究室のための星の力をハーネスします。 両方の種類の核融合反応器は、それらから原子力エネルギーを解放して、電源を生成する。 核融合反応器は核分裂反応器と同様に、より長く生産的に動作し、ブロックできないほど中程度の放射線を発生させる。 小型核融合炉は燃料スロットが四つあり、全てを充填すると ^#B7E3E5;360W^reset; を生成することができます。 冷却剤を投与して作動し続けるか、またはすばやく過熱して閉鎖し、放射線を放出しなければならないが、水は通常十分である。 各消費燃料は、ピンチで冷却剤として使用できる一つの毒性廃棄物を作成します。\n\n許容される燃料(燃料スロットあたりの電力、平均減衰時間)。\n----------\n水素15W: 50三重棒(トリチウム棒)25W: 60ヘリウム-3 (45W: 80s)、Solarium Star ()。55W: 150s)、重水素棒()。60W: 120ウルトロニウムロッド(Ultronium Rod)90W: 700)\n\nAccepted coolants (heat reduction per item)\n有害廃棄物(10)、塩水(30)、水(30)、液体窒素(80)、結晶性抽出物(125)\n\n\n^cyan;大型核融合炉^reset;\n\nSkathによって最初に先駆されたLarge Fusion Reactorsは、より大きな出力を持つSmall Fusion Reactorsのより優れた、スケールアップされたバージョンです。 四つのスロットを埋めると、最大^cyan;600W^reset;を生成することができます。 小型核融合炉のように放射線を発生させ、有害廃棄物を発生させます。\n\n許容される燃料(燃料スロットあたりの電力、平均減衰時間)。\n----------\n水素35W: 50三重棒(トリチウム棒)55W: 60ヘリウム-3 (60W: 80s)、Solarium Star ()。105W: 150s)、重水素棒()。90W: 120液体重水素 (Liquid Deuterium)90W: 120ウルトロニウムロッド(Ultronium Rod)150W: 700)\n\nAccepted coolants (heat reduction per item)\n塩水(20)、水(30)、有害廃棄物(40)、液体窒素(80)、結晶性抽出物(125)\n\n",
        "index": 4
      },
      {
        "field": "title",
        "source": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Generators and You",
        "normalizedSource": "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Generators and You",
        "translation": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : 発電機の使い方"
      }
    ],
    "networkguide": [
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Inventory Transference Network (ITN) devices allow you to create an automated, object-based network that can move and sort any item between your inventory, containers, and the open world. ITN objects use Starbound's wiring system to function, a familiarity with wiring is recommended but not required to use the ITN. All ITN objects are found at the Electronics Center (or its upgraded version, the Power Center).",
        "normalizedSource": "Inventory Transference Network (ITN) devices allow you to create an automated, object-based network that can move and sort any item between your inventory, containers, and the open world. ITN objects use Starbound's wiring system to function, a familiarity with wiring is recommended but not required to use the ITN. All ITN objects are found at the Electronics Center (or its upgraded version, the Power Center).",
        "translation": "在庫転送ネットワーク(ITN)デバイスを使用すると、在庫、コンテナ、オープンワールド間で任意のアイテムを移動およびソートできる自動化されたオブジェクトベースのネットワークを作成できます。 ITNオブジェクトはStarboundの配線システムを使用して機能しますが、配線に精通していることをお勧めしますが、ITNを使用する必要はありません。 すべてのITNオブジェクトは、電子工作台(またはアップグレードされたバージョン、Power Center)にあります。",
        "index": 1
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Pay close attention to the item tooltips for the various ITN objects, these will tell you exactly what each of that object's nodes are used for. Also be aware that some item descriptions will change after being placed - examine them both in your inventory and while placed! Also note that while many of these objects have power nodes that can be used to toggle them between active and inactive, none of the ITN objects require power (as created by generators) to function.",
        "normalizedSource": "Pay close attention to the item tooltips for the various ITN objects, these will tell you exactly what each of that object's nodes are used for. Also be aware that some item descriptions will change after being placed - examine them both in your inventory and while placed! Also note that while many of these objects have power nodes that can be used to toggle them between active and inactive, none of the ITN objects require power (as created by generators) to function.",
        "translation": "さまざまなITNオブジェクトのアイテムツールチップに注意を払い、これらのオブジェクトの各ノードが何に使われているかを正確に教えてくれます。 また、いくつかのアイテムの説明は配置後に変更されることに注意してください - あなたのインベントリと配置中にそれらを調べてください! また、これらのオブジェクトの多くは、アクティブと非アクティブの間でそれらを切り替えるために使用できるパワーノードを持っているが、機能するために(ジェネレータによって作成されたように)パワーを必要とするITNオブジェクトはない。",
        "index": 2
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "You can place items in the empty item boxes in the top-right corner of an ITD's configuration screen to tell it to pull specific kinds of items and ignore others. You can further specify whether you want the ITD to pull that exact item, or else the same types or categories of that item. Furthermore, you can specify how many to move at a time by placing stacks of the desired quantity. Using the Inverted Logic setting tells the ITD to ignore that specific, type, or category of item.",
        "normalizedSource": "You can place items in the empty item boxes in the top-right corner of an ITD's configuration screen to tell it to pull specific kinds of items and ignore others. You can further specify whether you want the ITD to pull that exact item, or else the same types or categories of that item. Furthermore, you can specify how many to move at a time by placing stacks of the desired quantity. Using the Inverted Logic setting tells the ITD to ignore that specific, type, or category of item.",
        "translation": "ITDのコンフィギュレーション画面の右上隅にある空のアイテムボックスにアイテムを配置して、特定の種類のアイテムをプルして、他のアイテムを無視するように指示することができます。 さらに、ITDがその正確なアイテムをプルするかどうか、あるいはそのアイテムの同じタイプまたはカテゴリを指定することもできます。 さらに、希望する量のスタックを配置することで、一度に移動する数を指定することができます。 Inverted Logic設定を使用すると、アイテムの特定のタイプやカテゴリを無視するようにITDに指示します。",
        "index": 11
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Item Types:\n  Hand Tools (Flashlight, rope, picks)\n  Instruments (Violin, xylaphone, assflute)\n  Thrown weapons (Throwing knives, bombs)\n  Augments\n  Collars\n  Dyes",
        "normalizedSource": "Item Types: Hand Tools (Flashlight, rope, picks) Instruments (Violin, xylaphone, assflute) Thrown weapons (Throwing knives, bombs) Augments Collars Dyes",
        "translation": "アイテムの種類：\n  道具（懐中電灯、ロープ、つるはし）\n  楽器（バイオリン、木琴、お尻フルート）\n  投てき武器（投げナイフ、爆弾）\n  拡張パーツ\n  首輪\n  染料",
        "index": 12
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Item Categories:\n  Treasure (Valuable & rare items)\n  Materials (Blocks, liquids, platforms)\n  Rails (Including platforms and trams)\n  Books (Including Blueprints)\n  Ingredients (Crafting materials, ores)\n  Objects (Containers, crafting stations, lights & doors)\n  Farm (Most agricultural products)\n  Weapons\n  Armor (Including back items & augments)\n  Unhandled (Anything not in the other categories)",
        "normalizedSource": "Item Categories: Treasure (Valuable & rare items) Materials (Blocks, liquids, platforms) Rails (Including platforms and trams) Books (Including Blueprints) Ingredients (Crafting materials, ores) Objects (Containers, crafting stations, lights & doors) Farm (Most agricultural products) Weapons Armor (Including back items & augments) Unhandled (Anything not in the other categories)",
        "translation": "項目カテゴリ:\n  宝物(貴重品・希少品)\n  材料(ブロック、液体、プラットフォーム)\n  Rails (プラットフォームとトラムを含む)\n  書物(青写真含む)\n  材料(材料、鉱石)\n  物(容器・造船所・照明・ドア)\n  農園(ほとんどの農産物)\n  武器\n  アーマー(バックアイテム&エンハンスメントを含む)\n  未処理 (他のカテゴリにはないもの)",
        "index": 13
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Once you have a basic ITN setup (described on page 9), you can make a terminal at the electronics/power center. By connecting the output of a container's storage bridge to a terminal's input node, you can see and search through every item stored in that container, and pull them into your inventory - but you cannot send items back through the terminal. A single terminal can be connected to multiple containers this way, letting you view and pull items from multiple containers at once.",
        "normalizedSource": "Once you have a basic ITN setup (described on page 9), you can make a terminal at the electronics/power center. By connecting the output of a container's storage bridge to a terminal's input node, you can see and search through every item stored in that container, and pull them into your inventory - but you cannot send items back through the terminal. A single terminal can be connected to multiple containers this way, letting you view and pull items from multiple containers at once.",
        "translation": "基本的なITN設定(ページ 9 に記載)が終わったら、電子/電源センターで端末を作成できます。 コンテナのストレージブリッジの出力を端末の入力ノードに接続することで、コンテナに格納されているすべてのアイテムを検索および検索し、それらをインベントリに引っ張ることができます - しかし、端末を通してアイテムを送信することはできません。 ひとつのターミナルを複数のコンテナに接続することで、複数のコンテナからアイテムを一度に表示およびプルすることができます。",
        "index": 14
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "A common, useful storage setup is to have rows of containers and storage bridges all linked to a single terminal (or series of terminals) so you can pull from all of them, with a chest nearby and its storage bridge linked to multiple ITDs that will automatically sort any items you dump into it into specific containers in the network without you having to do anything else.",
        "normalizedSource": "A common, useful storage setup is to have rows of containers and storage bridges all linked to a single terminal (or series of terminals) so you can pull from all of them, with a chest nearby and its storage bridge linked to multiple ITDs that will automatically sort any items you dump into it into specific containers in the network without you having to do anything else.",
        "translation": "便利な基本構成は、収納容器とストレージブリッジを列状に並べ、それらを一台の端末（または複数の端末）につないで、どの容器からも取り出せるようにするものだ。さらに近くにチェストを置き、そのストレージブリッジを複数のITDにつなぐ。こうすれば、そのチェストに放り込んだアイテムは、何もしなくてもネットワーク内の指定された容器へ自動で仕分けされる。",
        "index": 15
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "As you start making more sophisticated ITN setups, you may have trouble getting your wiring across large areas of space without vanishing, or else want to optimize the efficiency of your wiring. Repeaters can serve as wiring waypoints to extend your wiring range, while a single Repeater can be wired to all your containers so that you do not need to wire all of them individually between a dozen different terminals. It is important to note that if repeaters are looped, they will cease function.",
        "normalizedSource": "As you start making more sophisticated ITN setups, you may have trouble getting your wiring across large areas of space without vanishing, or else want to optimize the efficiency of your wiring. Repeaters can serve as wiring waypoints to extend your wiring range, while a single Repeater can be wired to all your containers so that you do not need to wire all of them individually between a dozen different terminals. It is important to note that if repeaters are looped, they will cease function.",
        "translation": "より洗練されたITNのセットアップを始めると、多くのスペースをまたいで配線が切れたり、配線の効率を最適化したりすることが難しくなることがあります。 リピータは、配線範囲を拡張するための配線ウェイポイントとして機能し、一方、一つのリピータはすべてのコンテナに配線できるため、一ダース単位の異なる端末間で個別に配線する必要はありません。 リピータがループされている場合は、機能を停止させることに注意することが重要です。",
        "index": 16
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Dos & Don'ts:\n\n  Do daisy-chain multiple containers. Use ITDs to draw items out of a container dumped to by another ITD to help automatically compress item stacks where possible and to give you more item-specific storage space.\n\n  Do not try to move large amounts of items into a container which already has many items in it. Do not daisy-chain ITDs. These are sources of lag, and ITD configurations do not stack without a separating container.",
        "normalizedSource": "Dos & Don'ts: Do daisy-chain multiple containers. Use ITDs to draw items out of a container dumped to by another ITD to help automatically compress item stacks where possible and to give you more item-specific storage space. Do not try to move large amounts of items into a container which already has many items in it. Do not daisy-chain ITDs. These are sources of lag, and ITD configurations do not stack without a separating container.",
        "translation": "Dos & Don't:\n\n  複数のコンテナをデイジーチェーン化して、ITDを使って別のITDによってダンプされたコンテナからアイテムを引き出し、可能な限りアイテムスタックを自動的に圧縮し、アイテム固有のストレージスペースを提供します。\n\n  大量のアイテムを、すでに多くのアイテムがあるコンテナに移動しようとしないでください。デイジーチェーンのITDはしないでください。これらは遅延の源であり、ITD構成はコンテナを分離せずにスタックしません。",
        "index": 17
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Dos & Don'ts:\n\n  Do create branching ITD trees along a string of containers where you feel you need to.\n\n  Do Not create any sort of infinite back-and-forth loop that shifts the same items between the same containers unless you have a very good reason to do so. This can be a substantial source of lag.",
        "normalizedSource": "Dos & Don'ts: Do create branching ITD trees along a string of containers where you feel you need to. Do Not create any sort of infinite back-and-forth loop that shifts the same items between the same containers unless you have a very good reason to do so. This can be a substantial source of lag.",
        "translation": "運用のコツと注意点：\n\n  必要に応じて、並べた収納容器に沿ってITDの経路を分岐させてください。\n\n  明確な理由がない限り、同じアイテムを同じ容器の間で延々と往復させる無限ループは作らないでください。大きな処理遅延の原因になります。",
        "index": 18
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "The pros of the ITN system are that it allows for extremely powerful, precise, decentralized and fully automated item storage. No more having to prance between dozens of different containers whenever you get back from a loot haul, you can just drop it all in a single chest and have it all sorted exactly where you need it, or else retrieve exactly the materials you need for crafting without having to leave a crafting station.",
        "normalizedSource": "The pros of the ITN system are that it allows for extremely powerful, precise, decentralized and fully automated item storage. No more having to prance between dozens of different containers whenever you get back from a loot haul, you can just drop it all in a single chest and have it all sorted exactly where you need it, or else retrieve exactly the materials you need for crafting without having to leave a crafting station.",
        "translation": "ITNシステムの長所は、非常に強力で、正確で、分散化され、完全に自動化されたアイテムストレージを可能にすることです。 戦利品を持ち帰るたびに何十個もの容器の間を走り回る必要はもうない。すべてを一つのチェストへ放り込めば、必要な場所へきちんと仕分けされる。製作台を離れずに、製作に必要な材料だけを取り出すこともできる。",
        "index": 19
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "The cons of the ITN system are that that it requires extensive setup and occasionally sophisticated wiring to get working, and requires examples of the items you want it to filter. It can also be a significant source of lag, the process of shifting and reorganizing upwards of a hundred stacks of items between multiple containers at once can be one of the most process-intensive aspects present in Starbound.",
        "normalizedSource": "The cons of the ITN system are that that it requires extensive setup and occasionally sophisticated wiring to get working, and requires examples of the items you want it to filter. It can also be a significant source of lag, the process of shifting and reorganizing upwards of a hundred stacks of items between multiple containers at once can be one of the most process-intensive aspects present in Starbound.",
        "translation": "ITNシステムの欠点は、動作するためには、大規模なセットアップと時には高度な配線が必要であり、フィルタリングしたいアイテムの例が必要であることです。 複数のコンテナ間で一〇〇スタックのアイテムを一度にシフトおよび再編成するプロセスは、Starboundに存在する最もプロセス集約的な側面の一つである。",
        "index": 20
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "The first core component of the ITN is the storage bridge, which is used to provide containers with input & output wiring nodes by way of proxy. Storage bridges look around themselves for the nearest container to connect to (by placement point), but can get confused if you put them right between multiple containers. Make sure your storage bridges are placed as close as possible to the one container you want them linked to, and to leave space between them and other containers.",
        "normalizedSource": "The first core component of the ITN is the storage bridge, which is used to provide containers with input & output wiring nodes by way of proxy. Storage bridges look around themselves for the nearest container to connect to (by placement point), but can get confused if you put them right between multiple containers. Make sure your storage bridges are placed as close as possible to the one container you want them linked to, and to leave space between them and other containers.",
        "translation": "ITNの最初のコアコンポーネントであるストレージブリッジは、プロキシを介してコンテナに入出力配線ノードを提供するために使用される。 ストレージブリッジは最寄りのコンテナを(配置ポイントによって)接続するために自分自身を見回しますが、複数のコンテナの間に配置すると混乱することがあります。 ストレージブリッジがリンクしたいコンテナに可能な限り近くに配置され、それらと他のコンテナの間にスペースが残されていることを確認してください。",
        "index": 3
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Credits:\n\n  Kherae for making all this arcane schlock work.\n  HelloWorld123 for writing the original Network Guide.\n  TP for Steambound Reloaded.\n  Cratesmith for the Vesselbound Container Link Code.\n  Terminal for figuring out how to reverse entropy and for writing this guide.",
        "normalizedSource": "Credits: Kherae for making all this arcane schlock work. HelloWorld123 for writing the original Network Guide. TP for Steambound Reloaded. Cratesmith for the Vesselbound Container Link Code. Terminal for figuring out how to reverse entropy and for writing this guide.",
        "translation": "クレジット：\n\n  Kherae：この複雑な仕組みを動くものにしてくれたことに感謝します。\n  HelloWorld123：元のネットワークガイドの執筆。\n  TP：Steambound Reloadedの制作。\n  Cratesmith：Vesselboundのコンテナ接続コードの制作。\n  Terminal：エントロピーを逆転させる方法の解明と、このガイドの執筆。",
        "index": 21
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Storage bridges work with more than just ordinary containers. Almost any object which can be interacted with that has item slots can be linked to a storage bridge. This includes some FrackinUniverse crafting stations and a few misc. objects that might already have power nodes (but no input/output nodes). If you find yourself uncertain about which nodes to use, remember that storage bridge nodes always function as ITN input/output nodes.",
        "normalizedSource": "Storage bridges work with more than just ordinary containers. Almost any object which can be interacted with that has item slots can be linked to a storage bridge. This includes some FrackinUniverse crafting stations and a few misc. objects that might already have power nodes (but no input/output nodes). If you find yourself uncertain about which nodes to use, remember that storage bridge nodes always function as ITN input/output nodes.",
        "translation": "ストレージブリッジは、通常のコンテナ以上のもので動作する。 アイテムスロットを持つオブジェクトと対話できるオブジェクトは、ほとんどすべてストレージブリッジにリンクすることができます。 これには、いくつかのFrackinUniverseクラフトステーションといくつかのミスが含まれます。 すでにパワーノードがあるかもしれないオブジェクト(入出力ノードがない)。 使用するノードが不確かであれば、ストレージブリッジノードは常にITNの入出力ノードとして機能することを忘れないでください。",
        "index": 4
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Object Data Sensor: Crafted in the tinkering table. Detects object placement points, to allow for more precise placement of Storage Bridges. Bridges select a single container based on the distance between themselves and object placement points.",
        "normalizedSource": "Object Data Sensor: Crafted in the tinkering table. Detects object placement points, to allow for more precise placement of Storage Bridges. Bridges select a single container based on the distance between themselves and object placement points.",
        "translation": "物体データセンサー: いじり台で作ったもの。 オブジェクト配置点を検出し、より正確なストレージブリッジの配置を可能にします。 ブリッジは、自分自身とオブジェクトの配置点との距離に基づいて単一のコンテナを選択します。",
        "index": 5
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Item Transference Devices (ITDs) are additional core components of the ITN system. While ITDs are capable of moving all items by default, you will need special token items to filter for currencies or items the ITD does not recognize. You can place them wherever you want as long as you can keep their wiring straight. Mastery of the ITD will bring mastery over the entire ITN system.",
        "normalizedSource": "Item Transference Devices (ITDs) are additional core components of the ITN system. While ITDs are capable of moving all items by default, you will need special token items to filter for currencies or items the ITD does not recognize. You can place them wherever you want as long as you can keep their wiring straight. Mastery of the ITD will bring mastery over the entire ITN system.",
        "translation": "アイテム転送デバイス(ITD)はITNシステムのコアコンポーネントである。 ITDはデフォルトですべてのアイテムを移動することができますが、ITDが認識していない通貨やアイテムをフィルタリングする特別なトークンアイテムが必要になります。 配線をまっすぐに保てる限り、どこにでも配置できます。 ITDの習得はITNシステム全体の習得をもたらす。",
        "index": 6
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Overflow: ITDs will sound off alarms if you are trying to move too much into a container that does not have space. They will also slow down their processing speed. If you have alarms sounding and periodic lag, you should work on improving flow control.",
        "normalizedSource": "Overflow: ITDs will sound off alarms if you are trying to move too much into a container that does not have space. They will also slow down their processing speed. If you have alarms sounding and periodic lag, you should work on improving flow control.",
        "translation": "オーバーフロー: スペースのないコンテナにあまり移動しようとすると、ITDはアラームを鳴らします。 また、処理速度も遅くなります。 アラームの鳴りと周期的な遅延がある場合は、流量制御の改善に取り組む必要があります。",
        "index": 7
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "Stack Move: To move stacks of specific sizes, place the desired stack size in your filter area. This works well with Even Split and Slot Split, as it will only move stacks there are enough to do so equally. It does not, however, account for amounts in the destination.",
        "normalizedSource": "Stack Move: To move stacks of specific sizes, place the desired stack size in your filter area. This works well with Even Split and Slot Split, as it will only move stacks there are enough to do so equally. It does not, however, account for amounts in the destination.",
        "translation": "スタック移動: 特定のサイズのスタックを移動させるには、希望するスタックサイズをフィルター領域に配置します。 スタックを均等に移動できるのが十分なので、Event SplitとSlot Splitではこれがうまく機能します。 ただし、目的地の金額は考慮されません。",
        "index": 8
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "In order to set up a basic ITN network, connect the red output node for a container's storage bridge to the second blue input node for an ITD, and then connect the ITD's red output node to the blue input node of a second container's storage bridge. Now all items put into the first container will be automatically moved to the second one.",
        "normalizedSource": "In order to set up a basic ITN network, connect the red output node for a container's storage bridge to the second blue input node for an ITD, and then connect the ITD's red output node to the blue input node of a second container's storage bridge. Now all items put into the first container will be automatically moved to the second one.",
        "translation": "基本的なITNネットワークを設定するには、コンテナのストレージブリッジ用の赤い出力ノードをITD用の二番目の青い入力ノードに接続し、ITDの赤い出力ノードを二番目のコンテナのストレージブリッジの青い入力ノードに接続します。 これで、最初のコンテナに入れられたすべてのアイテムが自動的に二番目のコンテナに移動されます。",
        "index": 9
      },
      {
        "field": "contentPages",
        "source": "ITDs can be interacted with to bring up their configuration menu. Input slots indicate what slots in a container the ITD will pull from; output slots designate what inventory slots in a container the ITD will drop items into. You can press the red I button to invert the selected slots, telling the ITD to ignore those specific slots rather than use them specifically. Even splitting and slot splitting dictate whether the ITD sorts items into single stacks or splits items between every indicated output slot. ITDs may not be used as repeaters.",
        "normalizedSource": "ITDs can be interacted with to bring up their configuration menu. Input slots indicate what slots in a container the ITD will pull from; output slots designate what inventory slots in a container the ITD will drop items into. You can press the red I button to invert the selected slots, telling the ITD to ignore those specific slots rather than use them specifically. Even splitting and slot splitting dictate whether the ITD sorts items into single stacks or splits items between every indicated output slot. ITDs may not be used as repeaters.",
        "translation": "ITDは、設定メニューを作成するために対話することができます。 入力スロットは、ITDがコンテナ内のどのスロットから取得するかを示し、出力スロットは、ITDがアイテムをドロップするコンテナ内のどのインベントリスロットを指定する。 赤のIボタンを押すと、選択したスロットを反転させ、ITDに特定のスロットを具体的に使うのではなく、無視するように指示することができます。 分割やスロット分割でさえ、ITDがアイテムを単一のスタックに分類するか、表示された出力スロットごとにアイテムを分割するかを決定する。 ITDはリピーターとして使用することはできません。",
        "index": 10
      },
      {
        "field": "description",
        "source": "A Beginner's Guide to ITN",
        "normalizedSource": "A Beginner's Guide to ITN",
        "translation": "アイテムネットワーク入門"
      },
      {
        "field": "title",
